ement de fournisseurs","Outils d''analyse de données","Intégration avec des technologies de pointe comme React et Node.js","Support pour la prise de décisions éclairées"],"de":["Unternehmensarchitektur-Governance","Lieferantenbeschaffung","Datenanalyse-Tools","Integration mit SpitzenTechnologien wie React und Node.js","Unterstützung für fundierte Entscheidungen"],"pt":["Governança de arquitetura empresarial","Compra de fornecedores","Gerenciamento de projetos","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Análise de desempenho"],"ru":["Управление предприятием","Закупки","Управление проектами","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Анализ производительности"],"ar":["إدارة البنية التحتية للمشاريع","شراء الموردين","إدارة المشاريع","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","تحليل الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用auto-memory","什么是企业架构治理","auto-memory替代品","auto-memory vs 其他工具","auto-memory安装","auto-memory设置指南","企业架构治理最佳实践","供应商采购策略"],"ja":["auto-memoryの使用方法","エンタープライズアーキテクチャガバナンスとは","auto-memoryの代替品","auto-memory vs 他のツール","auto-memoryのインストール","auto-memoryの設定ガイド","エンタープライズアーキテクチャガバナンスのベストプラクティス","ベンダー調達戦略"],"ko":["auto-memory 사용법","엔터프라이즈 아키텍처 거버넌스란","auto-memory 대체품","auto-memory vs 다른 툴","auto-memory 설치","auto-memory 설정 가이드","엔터프라이즈 아키텍처 거버넌스 베스트 프랙티스","벤더 조달 전략"],"es":["cómo usar auto-memory","qué es la gobernanza de arquitectura empresarial","herramientas de agente de IA","auto-memory alternativa","auto-memory vs otros agentes de IA","instalación de auto-memory","guía de configuración de auto-memory"],"fr":["comment utiliser auto-mémoire","qu''est-ce que la gouvernance d''architecture d''entreprise","outils d''agent IA","auto-mémoire alternative","auto-mémoire vs autres agents IA","installation d''auto-mémoire","guide de configuration d''auto-mémoire"],"de":["wie man auto-speicher verwendet","was ist die Unternehmensarchitektur-Governance","AI-Agent-Tools","auto-speicher alternative","auto-speicher vs andere AI-Agenten","installation von auto-speicher","konfigurationshandbuch für auto-speicher"],"pt":["como usar auto-memory","o que é governança de arquitetura empresarial","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","auto-memory vs outras ferramentas","instalação do auto-memory","guia de configuração do auto-memory"],"ru":["как использовать auto-memory","что такое управление предприятием","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","auto-memory vs другие инструменты","установка auto-memory","руководство по настройке auto-memory"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام auto-memory","ما هي إدارة البنية التحتية للمشاريع","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","auto-memory مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت auto-memory","دليل إعداد auto-memory"]}},"owner":"tractorjuice","repo":"arc-kit","repoPath":"tractorjuice/arc-kit","stars":96,"forks":16,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T23:15:21Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"auto-memory","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to set up memory, create memory files, create MEMORY.md, set up topic files, improve memory organization, what should I remember, how to structure memory files, MEMORY.md is too long, what goes in memory vs topic files, memory best practices, or wants to establish a persistent knowledge base across Claude Code sessions. Triggers on: memory setup, MEMORY.md, topic files, cross-session knowledge, persistent notes, memory maintenance, memory pruning.","bodyPreview":"# Auto Memory Management\n\nUse persistent auto memory to retain project knowledge across Claude Code sessions. The memory directory (`~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/`) stores a concise index file (`MEMORY.md`) and detailed topic files, creating a structured knowledge base that grows with the project.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\n```text\n~/.claude/projects/<project-path>/memory/\n├── MEMORY.md          # Always loaded into system prompt (~200 lines max)\n├── architecture.md    # Topic file: system archi","body":"# Auto Memory Management\n\nUse persistent auto memory to retain project knowledge across Claude Code sessions. The memory directory (`~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/`) stores a concise index file (`MEMORY.md`) and detailed topic files, creating a structured knowledge base that grows with the project.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\n```text\n~/.claude/projects/<project-path>/memory/\n├── MEMORY.md          # Always loaded into system prompt (~200 lines max)\n├── architecture.md    # Topic file: system architecture decisions\n├── patterns.md        # Topic file: code patterns and conventions\n├── debugging.md       # Topic file: debugging insights\n├── workflows.md       # Topic file: development workflows\n└── known-issues.md    # Topic file: bug tracking\n```\n\n### Two-Tier Design\n\n1. **MEMORY.md** (always in context): Concise index with key facts, quick reference tables, and links to topic files. Lines after 200 are truncated — keep it tight.\n2. **Topic files** (consulted as needed): Detailed reference organized by domain. No size limit, but keep each file focused on one topic.\n\n## What to Save\n\n### Save These\n\n- **Stable patterns** confirmed across multiple interactions (naming conventions, file organization, coding style)\n- **Architectural decisions** and their rationale\n- **Important file paths** and project structure\n- **User preferences** for workflow, tools, and communication style\n- **Solutions to recurring problems** and debugging insights\n- **Critical gotchas** that cause repeated mistakes\n- **Explicit user requests** (\"always use bun\", \"never auto-commit\") — save immediately, no need to wait for confirmation across sessions\n\n### Do NOT Save\n\n- **Session-specific context** (current task details, in-progress work, temporary state)\n- **Unverified information** — verify against project docs before writing\n- **Duplicates of CLAUDE.md** — memory supplements project instructions, never contradicts them\n- **Speculative conclusions** from reading a single file\n- **Rapidly changing values** (exact line numbers, temporary feature flags)\n\n## Setting Up Auto Memory\n\n### Step 1: Create the Memory Directory\n\nThe directory is created automatically by Claude Code, but to initialize manually:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.claude/projects/<project-path>/memory/\n```\n\nThe `<project-path>` typically mirrors the working directory with slashes replaced by dashes (e.g., `/workspaces/my-app` becomes `-workspaces-my-app`).\n\n### Step 2: Create MEMORY.md\n\nStart with a minimal index and expand as patterns emerge. Include:\n\n- **Project overview**: Key architectural facts (2-3 bullet points)\n- **Quick reference**: Counts, paths, conventions that come up repeatedly\n- **Critical gotchas**: Hard-won lessons that prevent repeated mistakes\n- **Topic file index**: Table linking to detailed files with \"when to consult\" guidance\n\nSee [examples/MEMORY.md](examples/MEMORY.md) for a starter template.\n\n### Step 3: Create Topic Files as Needed\n\nCreate topic files only when a domain accumulates enough detail to warrant its own file. Common topic files:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `architecture.md` | System design decisions, component relationships |\n| `patterns.md` | Code conventions, naming, file organization |\n| `debugging.md` | Solutions to recurring problems |\n| `workflows.md` | Build, test, deploy procedures |\n| `known-issues.md` | Bug tracking, open/fixed issues |\n| `release-process.md` | Version management, release checklists |\n| `dependencies.md` | Package versions, compatibility notes |\n\nSee [examples/topic-file.md](examples/topic-file.md) for the recommended structure.\n\n## Organization Principles\n\n### Semantic Over Chronological\n\nOrganize by topic, not by date. \"Architecture decisions\" is better than \"Session notes 2026-02-15\". When new information arrives, integrate it into the appropriate topic rather than appending chronologically.\n\n### Concise Index, Detailed Topics\n\nMEMORY.md answers \"what do I need to know right now?\" Topic files answer \"what are all the details about X?\" Keep the index scannable — use bullet points, tables, and bold for key terms.\n\n### Topic File Index Table\n\nAlways include a table in MEMORY.md linking to topic files with guidance on when to consult each:\n\n```markdown\n## Topic Files\n\n| File | When to consult |\n|------|----------------|\n| `architecture.md` | Working on system design, component changes |\n| `patterns.md` | Writing new code, reviewing conventions |\n| `debugging.md` | Investigating bugs, error messages |\n```\n\n### One Topic Per File\n\nEach file covers one domain. If a file grows beyond ~5,000 words or covers multiple unrelated topics, split it. A file named `misc.md` or `notes.md` is a sign of poor organization.\n\n## Maintenance\n\n### When to Update\n\n- After discovering a mistake that could recur\n- When a pattern is confirmed across 2+ interactions\n- When the user explicitly asks to remember something\n- After resolving a tricky bug worth documenting\n- When project structure changes significantly\n\n### When to Remove or Edit\n\n- When stored information becomes outdated (version bumps, removed features)\n- When a gotcha is fixed and no longer relevant\n- When the user asks to forget something\n- When MEMORY.md exceeds ~200 lines — prune or move detail to topic files\n\n### Avoiding Drift\n\nPeriodically review memory files against the actual project state. Stale entries (wrong counts, outdated paths, fixed bugs still listed as open) erode trust in the memory system. Mark fixed issues as fixed rather than deleting them — the history of what went wrong is itself valuable.\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n\nFor detailed patterns, anti-patterns, and advanced techniques:\n\n- **[references/patterns.md](references/patterns.md)** — Writing style guide, MEMORY.md structure patterns, topic file patterns, common anti-patterns\n\n### Example Files\n\nWorking examples ready to adapt:\n\n- **[examples/MEMORY.md](examples/MEMORY.md)** — Starter MEMORY.md template\n- **[examples/topic-file.md](examples/topic-file.md)** — Topic file template with recommended structure\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T12:49:13.486Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code requiring persistent knowledge retention across sessions","zh":"适合于需要跨会话持久保留知识的AI代理，如Claude Code","ja":"セッション間で知識を保持する必要があるAIエージェント（Claude Codeなど）に適しています","ko":"세션 간 지식 보존이 필요한 AI 에이전트(Claude Code 등)에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code que requieren una retención de conocimiento persistente entre sesiones","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA comme Claude Code nécessitant une rétention de connaissances persistante entre sessions","de":"Ideal für KI-Agenten wie Claude Code, die eine persistente Wissensspeicherung über Sitzungen hinweg erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code que requerem retenção de conhecimento persistente entre sessões","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, требующих постоянного сохранения знаний между сессиями","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code الذي يتطلب الحفاظ على المعرفة المستمرة عبر الجلسات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage persistent auto memory, utilizing a structured knowledge base stored in a memory directory with concise index files like MEMORY.md and detailed topic files, facilitating project knowledge retention and growth","zh":"赋予代理利用持久的自动内存能力，使用存储在内存目录中的结构化知识库，具有简洁的索引文件（如MEMORY.md）和详细的主题文件，促进项目知识的保留和增长","ja":"エージェントに持続的な自動メモリを利用する能力を与え、メモリディレクトリに保存された構造化されたナレッジベースを使用し、MEMORY.mdなどの簡潔な索引ファイルと詳細なトピックファイルを備え、プロジェクトナレッジの保持と成長を促進する","ko":"에이전트가 지속적인 자동 메모리를 활용할 수 있도록 하여 메모리 디렉토리에 저장된 구조화된 지식베이스를 사용하고 MEMORY.md와 같은 간결한 색인 파일 및 자세한 주제 파일을 제공하여 프로젝트 지식 보존 및 성장을促進합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar la memoria automática persistente, utilizando una base de conocimientos estructurada almacenada en un directorio de memoria con archivos de índice concisos como MEMORY.md y archivos de temas detallados, facilitando la retención y el crecimiento del conocimiento del proyecto","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser la mémoire auto persistante, en utilisant une base de connaissances structurée stockée dans un répertoire de mémoire avec des fichiers d''index concis comme MEMORY.md et des fichiers de sujets détaillés, facilitant la rétention et la croissance des connaissances du projet","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, die persistente Auto-Speicherung zu nutzen, indem sie eine strukturierte Wissensbasis verwenden, die in einem Speicherverzeichnis mit knappen Indexdateien wie MEMORY.md und detaillierten Themendateien gespeichert ist, um die Wissensspeicherung und -entwicklung des Projekts zu erleichtern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar a memória automática persistente, utilizando uma base de conhecimento estruturada armazenada em um diretório de memória com arquivos de índice concisos como MEMORY.md e arquivos de tópico detalhados, facilitando a retenção e o crescimento do conhecimento do projeto","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать постоянную автоматическую память, используя структурированную базу знаний, хранящуюся в каталоге памяти с краткими индексными файлами, такими как MEMORY.md, и подробными тематическими файлами, облегчая сохранение и рост знаний проекта","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الاستفادة من الذاكرة التلقائية المستمرة، باستخدام قاعدة معرفة منظمة مخزنة في دليل الذاكرة مع ملفات فهرس متواضعة مثل MEMORY.md وملفات مواضيع مفصلة، مما يسهل الحفاظ على المعرفة وتطور المشروع"},"useCases":{"en":["Retaining project knowledge across sessions","Creating a structured knowledge base with MEMORY.md and topic files","Automating project data storage in the memory directory"],"zh":["跨会话保留项目知识","使用MEMORY.md和主题文件创建结构化知识库","将项目数据自动存储在内存目录中"],"ja":["セッション間でプロジェクトナレッジを保持する","MEMORY.mdとトピックファイルを使用して構造化されたナレッジベースを作成する","プロジェクトデータをメモリディレクトリに自動的に保存する"],"ko":["세션 간 프로젝트 지식을 보존합니다","MEMORY.md 및 주제 파일을 사용하여 구조화된 지식베이스를 생성합니다","프로젝트 데이터를 메모리 디렉토리에 자동으로 저장합니다"],"es":["Retener el conocimiento del proyecto entre sesiones","Crear una base de conocimientos estructurada con MEMORY.md y archivos de temas","Automatizar el almacenamiento de datos del proyecto en el directorio de memoria"],"fr":["Conserver les connaissances du projet entre sessions","Créer une base de connaissances structurée avec MEMORY.md et des fichiers de sujets","Automatiser le stockage des données du projet dans le répertoire de mémoire"],"de":["Das Projektwissen über Sitzungen hinweg beibehalten","Eine strukturierte Wissensbasis mit MEMORY.md und Themendateien erstellen","Die Speicherung von Projektdaten im Speicherverzeichnis automatisieren"],"pt":["Manter o conhecimento do projeto entre sessões","Criar uma base de conhecimento estruturada com MEMORY.md e arquivos de tópico","Automatizar o armazenamento de dados do projeto no diretório de memória"],"ru":["Сохранение знаний проекта между сессиями","Создание структурированной базы знаний с помощью MEMORY.md и тематических файлов","Автоматизация хранения данных проекта в каталоге памяти"],"ar":["الحفاظ على معرفة المشروع عبر الجلسات","إنشاء قاعدة معرفة منظمة باستخدام MEMORY.md وملفات المواضيع","تأتمتة تخزين بيانات المشروع في دليل الذاكرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the memory directory (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Limited to 200 lines in the MEMORY.md file"],"zh":["需要访问内存目录 (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","MEMORY.md文件限制为200行"],"ja":["メモリディレクトリ (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/) へのアクセスが必要","MEMORY.mdファイルは200行までに制限されます"],"ko":["메모리 디렉토리 (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)에 접근해야 합니다","MEMORY.md 파일은 200행까지 제한됩니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio de memoria (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Limitado a 200 líneas en el archivo MEMORY.md"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au répertoire de mémoire (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Limité à 200 lignes dans le fichier MEMORY.md"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Speicherverzeichnis (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Begrenzt auf 200 Zeilen in der Datei MEMORY.md"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao diretório de memória (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Limitado a 200 linhas no arquivo MEMORY.md"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к каталогу памяти (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","Ограничен до 200 строк в файле MEMORY.md"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى دليل الذاكرة (~/.claude/projects/<path>/memory/)","محدود بـ 200 سطر في ملف MEMORY.md"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"f9542fd6b0a8389cb06b08a7a4b1b4d9df75c4dc17233596625afe613dc30200","qualityScore":42}');
