 de aplicaciones web con Blazor"],"fr":["outils de débogage frontend","comment utiliser Blazor","quoi est .NET Core","alternatives à Aspire","guide d''installation de .NET","configuration de PostgreSQL","architecture logicielle CQRS","développement d''applications web avec .NET","débogage d''applications web avec Blazor"],"de":["Frontend-Debugging-Tools","wie man Blazor verwendet","was ist .NET Core","Alternativen zu Aspire",".NET-Installationsanleitung","PostgreSQL-Konfiguration","CQRS-Softwarearchitektur","Entwicklung von Webanwendungen mit .NET","Debuggen von Webanwendungen mit Blazor"],"pt":["como usar Blazor","o que é event sourcing","Aspire alternative","Blazor vs React","instalar .NET Core","guia de configuração da Aspire"],"ru":["как использовать Blazor","что такое event sourcing","алтернативы Aspire","Blazor vs React","установить .NET Core","руководство по настройке Aspire"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Blazor","ما هو مصدر الحدث","بديل Aspire","Blazor مقابل React","تثبيت .NET Core","دليل إعداد Aspire"]}},"owner":"aalmada","repo":"BookStore","repoPath":"aalmada/BookStore","stars":15,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T19:40:57Z","topics":["aspire","aspire-dotnet","blazor","cqrs","dotnet","dotnet-core","dotnetcore","event-sourcing","example","marten","postgres","wolverine"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend__debug_sse","description":"Debug Server-Sent Events (SSE) notification issues when real-time updates arent working. Use this when mutations dont trigger frontend updates.","bodyPreview":"Use this guide to troubleshoot Server-Sent Events (SSE) issues.\n\n## Quick Path (80% of issues)\n\n// turbo\n1. **Test SSE endpoint**:\n   ```bash\n   curl -N -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" http://localhost:5000/api/notifications/stream\n   ```\n   Should see: `data: {\"type\":\"Connected\",...}`\n\n2. **Check ProjectionCommitListener** has case for your projection\n3. **Check QueryInvalidationService** maps notification to query keys\n4. **Check ReactiveQuery** uses matching `queryKeys`\n\nIf still broken, conti","body":"Use this guide to troubleshoot Server-Sent Events (SSE) issues.\n\n## Quick Path (80% of issues)\n\n// turbo\n1. **Test SSE endpoint**:\n   ```bash\n   curl -N -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" http://localhost:5000/api/notifications/stream\n   ```\n   Should see: `data: {\"type\":\"Connected\",...}`\n\n2. **Check ProjectionCommitListener** has case for your projection\n3. **Check QueryInvalidationService** maps notification to query keys\n4. **Check ReactiveQuery** uses matching `queryKeys`\n\nIf still broken, continue to full debugging below.\n\n---\n\n## Symptoms\n\n- ✗ Frontend doesn''t update after mutation\n- ✗ `ReactiveQuery` doesn''t invalidate\n- ✗ SSE connection fails or disconnects\n- ✗ Events not received in browser\n\n## Related Skills\n\n**Prerequisites**:\n- `/aspire__start_solution` - Solution must be running to debug SSE\n\n**First Steps**:\n- `/test__verify_feature` - Run basic checks (build, tests) before deep debugging\n\n**Related Debugging**:\n- `/cache__debug_cache` - If issue seems cache-related instead of SSE\n- `/ops__doctor_check` - Check if environment setup is correct\n\n**After Fixing**:\n- `/test__verify_feature` - Confirm fix works\n- `/test__integration_scaffold` - Add tests to prevent regression\n\n## Debugging Steps\n\n### 1. Verify SSE Endpoint is Working\n\nTest the SSE endpoint directly:\n\n```bash\n# Terminal 1: Connect to SSE stream\ncurl -N -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" http://localhost:5000/api/notifications/stream\n```\n\nYou should see:\n```\n: connected\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"Connected\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-01-15T20:00:00Z\"}\n```\n\n**If connection fails**:\n- ✗ Check API service is running\n- ✗ Verify `/api/notifications/stream` endpoint exists in `NotificationEndpoints.cs`\n- ✗ Check firewall/network issues\n\n### 2. Verify Notifications Are Defined\n\nCheck `src/Shared/BookStore.Shared/Notifications/DomainEventNotifications.cs`:\n\n```csharp\n// ✅ Correct - implements IDomainEventNotification\npublic record BookCreatedNotification(Guid Id, string Title) : IDomainEventNotification;\n\n// ✗ Wrong - missing interface\npublic record BookCreatedNotification(Guid Id, string Title);\n```\n\n**If notification is missing**:\n1. Create notification in `DomainEventNotifications.cs`\n2. Implement `IDomainEventNotification` interface\n3. Include all data needed for frontend invalidation\n\n### 3. Verify ProjectionCommitListener Configuration\n\nOpen `src/BookStore.ApiService/Infrastructure/MartenCommitListener.cs`:\n\n**Check if your projection has a handler**:\n\n```csharp\nprivate async Task ProcessDocumentChangeAsync(\n    IDocumentChange change,\n    CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n{\n    switch (change)\n    {\n        case BookProjection proj:\n            await HandleBookChangeAsync(proj, cancellationToken);\n            break;\n\n        // ❌ Missing: Your projection case\n        case AuthorProjection proj:\n            await HandleAuthorChangeAsync(proj, cancellationToken);\n            break;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Check if handler sends notification**:\n\n```csharp\nprivate async Task HandleBookChangeAsync(\n    BookProjection book,\n    CancellationToken cancellationToken)\n{\n    var notification = new BookUpdatedNotification(book.Id, book.Title);\n\n    // ✅ Correct - sends notification\n    await _notificationService.NotifyAsync(notification, cancellationToken);\n\n    // ✗ Wrong - forgot to send\n    // (no NotifyAsync call)\n}\n```\n\n**If handler is missing**:\n1. Add case for your projection\n2. Create handler method that calls `NotifyAsync`\n3. Use appropriate notification type\n\n### 4. Verify QueryInvalidationService Mapping\n\nOpen `src/Web/BookStore.Web/Services/QueryInvalidationService.cs`:\n\n**Check if notification maps to query keys**:\n\n```csharp\nIEnumerable<string> GetInvalidationKeys(IDomainEventNotification notification)\n{\n    switch (notification)\n    {\n        case BookCreatedNotification n:\n            yield return \"Books\";\n            yield return $\"Book:{n.EntityId}\";\n            break;\n        case BookUpdatedNotification n:\n            yield return \"Books\";\n            yield return $\"Book:{n.EntityId}\";\n            break;\n\n        // ❌ Missing: Your notification\n        case AuthorUpdatedNotification n:\n            yield return \"Authors\";\n            yield return $\"Author:{n.EntityId}\";\n            break;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**If mapping is missing**:\n1. Add case for your notification type\n2. Yield return query keys that should be invalidated\n3. Match keys used in `ReactiveQuery` setup\n\n### 5. Verify Frontend BookStoreEventsService\n\nCheck browser console for SSE connection:\n\n**In Chrome DevTools**:\n1. Open Network tab\n2. Look for \"events\" request (type: eventsource)\n3. Check status is \"pending\" (active connection)\n4. View \"EventStream\" tab to see events\n\n**If connection is closed**:\n- Check `BookStoreEventsService.StartListening()` is called in `OnInitializedAsync`\n- Verify base URL is correct\n- Check for JavaScript errors\n\n### 6. Verify ReactiveQuery Configuration\n\nCheck component using `ReactiveQuery`:\n\n```csharp\n// ✅ Correct - query keys match invalidation mapping\nbookQuery = new ReactiveQuery<PagedListDto<BookDto>>(\n    queryFn: FetchBooksAsync,\n    eventsService: BookStoreEventsService,\n    invalidationService: InvalidationService,\n    queryKeys: new[] { \"Books\" },  // Matches QueryInvalidationService\n    onStateChanged: StateHasChanged,\n    logger: Logger\n);\n\n// ✗ Wrong - query keys don''t match\nqueryKeys: new[] { \"AllBooks\" }  // Doesn''t match \"Books\"\n```\n\n**If query doesn''t invalidate**:\n1. Ensure `queryKeys` match `QueryInvalidationService` mapping\n2. Verify `BookStoreEventsService` is subscribed\n3. Check `onStateChanged` callback is provided\n\n### 7. Test End-to-End\n\nPerform a mutation and watch the flow:\n\n```bash\n# Terminal 1: Watch SSE stream\ncurl -N -H \"Accept: text/event-stream\" http://localhost:5000/api/notifications/stream\n\n# Terminal 2: Trigger mutation\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/admin/books \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ''{\"title\":\"Test Book\",...}''\n```\n\n**Expected flow**:\n1. Command executed\n2. Event stored in Marten\n3. `ProjectionCommitListener` triggered\n4. Notification sent via SSE\n5. Browser receives event\n6. `QueryInvalidationService` maps to keys\n7. `ReactiveQuery` invalidates\n8. Query refetches\n9. UI updates\n\n**If any step fails**, locate where:\n- Check logs in Aspire dashboard\n- Add debug logging to `ProjectionCommitListener`\n- Use browser console to see received events\n\n## Common Issues & Fixes\n\n### Issue: Events Not Sent\n\n**Symptom**: ProjectionCommitListener not triggered\n\n**Fix**:\n- Ensure `ProjectionCommitListener` is registered in DI\n- Check Marten event store configuration\n- Verify projection lifecycle (`Inline` vs `Async`)\n\n### Issue: Wrong Event Type\n\n**Symptom**: Notification sent but frontend doesn''t invalidate\n\n**Fix**:\n```csharp\n// Check notification type name matches exactly\ncase \"BookUpdatedNotification\":  // ✅ Correct\ncase \"BookUpdated\":              // ✗ Wrong\n```\n\n### Issue: Multiple Tabs Don''t Update\n\n**Symptom**: Updates only visible in tab that made change\n\n**Fix**:\n- SSE works per-connection, each tab needs own connection\n- Each tab should call `BookStoreEventsService.StartListening()`\n- Verify SignalR isn''t being used (project uses SSE)\n\n### Issue: SSE Connection Drops\n\n**Symptom**: Connection works then stops\n\n**Fix**:\n- Check server-side timeout configuration\n- Verify no proxy/load balancer kills long connections\n- Add reconnection logic in `BookStoreEventsService`\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n- [ ] SSE endpoint accessible at `/api/notifications/stream`\n- [ ] Notification class implements `IDomainEventNotification`\n- [ ] `ProjectionCommitListener` has handler for projection\n- [ ] Handler calls `NotifyAsync` with notification\n- [ ] `QueryInvalidationService` maps notification to keys\n- [ ] Frontend `ReactiveQuery` uses matching query keys\n- [ ] `BookStoreEventsService.StartListening()` called on mount\n- [ ] Browser DevTools shows active EventSource connection\n- [ ] End-to-end test confirms UI updates after mutation\n\n## Debugging Tools\n\n**Backend**:\n- Aspire Dashboard → Structured Logs → Filter by \"notification\"\n- Add logging in `ProjectionCommitListener`: `_logger.LogInformation(\"Sending {Type}\", notification.GetType().Name)`\n\n**Frontend**:\n- Browser Console → Look for EventSource logs\n- React DevTools → Check component re-renders\n- Network tab → Verify EventSource connection\n\n## Related Skills\n\n**First Steps**:\n- `/test__verify_feature` - Run basic checks (build, tests) before deep debugging\n\n**Related Debugging**:\n- `/cache__debug_cache` - If issue seems cache-related instead of SSE\n- `/ops__doctor_check` - Check if environment setup is correct\n\n**After Fixing**:\n- `/test__verify_feature` - Confirm fix works\n- `/test__integration_scaffold` - Add tests to prevent regression\n\n**See Also**:\n- [wolverine__create_operation](../wolverine__create_operation/SKILL.md) - SSE notification setup in ProjectionCommitListener\n- [frontend__feature_scaffold](../frontend__feature_scaffold/SKILL.md) - Frontend SSE integration\n- [real-time-notifications](../../../docs/guides/real-time-notifications.md) - SSE architecture and data flow\n- ApiService AGENTS.md - Backend notification patterns\n- Web AGENTS.md - Frontend SSE patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:33:50.738Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Full-stack Agents troubleshooting Server-Sent Events (SSE) issues in .NET applications with Blazor frontend and event-sourced backend API.","zh":"适用于全栈代理调试使用Blazor前端和事件源后端API的.NET应用程序中的Server-Sent Events (SSE)问题。","ja":"BlazorフロントエンドとイベントソースバックエンドAPIを使用する.NETアプリケーションのServer-Sent Events (SSE)問題のトラブルシューティングに適しています。","ko":"Blazor 프론트엔드와 이벤트 소스 백엔드 API를 사용하는 .NET 애플리케이션의 Server-Sent Events(SSE) 문제를 트러블슈팅하는 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de full-stack que solucionan problemas de Server-Sent Events (SSE) en aplicaciones .NET con interfaz de usuario Blazor y API de backend con eventos como fuente","fr":"Idéal pour les agents full-stack qui dépannent les problèmes de Server-Sent Events (SSE) dans les applications .NET avec une interface utilisateur Blazor et une API de backend à source d''événements","de":"Ideal für Full-Stack-Agents, die Server-Sent Events (SSE)-Probleme in .NET-Anwendungen mit Blazor-Frontend und ereignisquellengesteuerter Backend-API beheben","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Full-stack de resolução de problemas de Eventos Enviados pelo Servidor (SSE) em aplicações .NET com frontend Blazor e API de backend baseada em eventos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для полноценных агентов по устранению неполадок событий, отправляемых сервером (SSE), в приложениях .NET с фронтендом Blazor и бэкендом API на основе событий.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تام لتحليل أسباب أعطال الأحداث المرسلة من الخادم (SSE) في تطبيقات .NET مع واجهة المستخدم Blazor وواجهة برمجة تطبيقات الخلفية القائمة على الأحداث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to debug SSE issues by testing endpoints with curl, inspecting ProjectionCommitListener, and verifying QueryInvalidationService mappings, all while leveraging event-streaming and reactive query capabilities.","zh":"通过使用curl测试端点、检查ProjectionCommitListener和验证QueryInvalidationService映射来赋予代理调试SSE问题的能力，同时利用事件流和响应式查询功能。","ja":"curlでエンドポイントをテストし、ProjectionCommitListenerを検査し、QueryInvalidationServiceのマッピングを検証することで、SSEの問題をデバッグするエージェントをEmpower化し、イベントストリーミングとリアクティブクエリの機能を活用します。","ko":"curl로 엔드ポイント를 테스트하고 ProjectionCommitListener를 검사하고 QueryInvalidationService 매핑을 확인함으로써 SSE 문제를 디버깅할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하며 이벤트 스트리밍과 리액티브 쿼리 기능을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a depurar problemas de SSE probando puntos de conexión con curl, inspeccionando ProjectionCommitListener y verificando asignaciones de QueryInvalidationService, todo mientras aprovecha las capacidades de transmisión de eventos y consultas reactivas","fr":"Permet aux agents de déboguer les problèmes de SSE en testant les points de terminaison avec curl, en inspectant ProjectionCommitListener et en vérifiant les mappages de QueryInvalidationService, le tout en exploitant les capacités de diffusion d''événements et de requêtes réactives","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, SSE-Probleme zu debuggen, indem Endpunkte mit curl getestet, ProjectionCommitListener untersucht und QueryInvalidationService-Zuordnungen überprüft werden, während die Möglichkeiten von Ereignisstreaming und reaktiven Abfragen genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a depurar problemas de SSE testando endpoints com curl, inspecionando ProjectionCommitListener e verificando mapeamentos de QueryInvalidationService, tudo isso aproveitando as capacidades de transmissão de eventos e consulta reativa.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отладки проблем с SSE, тестируя конечные точки с помощью curl, инспектируя ProjectionCommitListener и проверяя сопоставления QueryInvalidationService, все это при использовании возможностей потоковой передачи событий и реактивного запроса.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصحيح أعطال SSE من خلال اختبار النقاط النهائية باستخدام curl، وفحص ProjectionCommitListener، وตรวจ التحقق من مappings QueryInvalidationService، كل ذلك مع الاستفادة من إمكانيات بث الأحداث والاستفسار التفاعلي."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging Server-Sent Events connectivity","Validating ProjectionCommitListener configurations","Troubleshooting ReactiveQuery issues with query keys"],"zh":["调试Server-Sent Events连接性","验证ProjectionCommitListener配置","使用查询键调试ReactiveQuery问题"],"ja":["Server-Sent Eventsの接続性のデバッグ","ProjectionCommitListenerの設定の検証","クエリキーを使用したReactiveQueryの問題のトラブルシューティング"],"ko":["Server-Sent Events 연결성 디버깅","ProjectionCommitListener 구성 검증","쿼리 키를 사용한 ReactiveQuery 문제 트러블슈팅"],"es":["Depuración de la conectividad de Server-Sent Events","Validación de configuraciones de ProjectionCommitListener","Solución de problemas de ReactiveQuery con claves de consulta"],"fr":["Débogage de la connectivité de Server-Sent Events","Validation des configurations de ProjectionCommitListener","Dépannage des problèmes de ReactiveQuery avec des clés de requête"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei der Konnektivität von Server-Sent Events","Validierung von ProjectionCommitListener-Konfigurationen","Behandlung von ReactiveQuery-Problemen mit Abfrage-Schlüsseln"],"pt":["Depuração da conectividade de Eventos Enviados pelo Servidor","Validação de configurações de ProjectionCommitListener","Solução de problemas de ReactiveQuery com chaves de consulta"],"ru":["Отладка подключения событий, отправляемых сервером","Валидация конфигураций ProjectionCommitListener","Устранение неполадок с ReactiveQuery с ключами запроса"],"ar":["تصحيح الأعطال في الاتصال بأحداث الخادم المرسلة","التحقق من صحة تكوينات ProjectionCommitListener","حل مشاكل ReactiveQuery مع مفاتيح الاستفسار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET and Blazor setup","Specific to Server-Sent Events (SSE) protocol","Needs access to event-sourced backend API"],"zh":[".NETとBlazor設定が必要","特定于Server-Sent Events (SSE)协议","需要访问事件源后端API"],"ja":[".NETとBlazorの設定が必要","Server-Sent Events (SSE)プロトコルに特有","イベントソースバックエンドAPIへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":[".NET과 Blazor 설정이 필요함","Server-Sent Events(SSE) 프로토콜에 특정됨","이벤트 소스 백엔드 API에 대한 액세스가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere configuración de .NET y Blazor","Específico del protocolo Server-Sent Events (SSE)","Necesita acceso a la API de backend con eventos como fuente"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration .NET et Blazor","Spécifique au protocole Server-Sent Events (SSE)","Nécessite un accès à l''API de backend à source d''événements"],"de":["Benötigt .NET- und Blazor-Setup","Spezifisch für das Server-Sent Events (SSE)-Protokoll","Benötigt Zugriff auf die ereignisquellengesteuerte Backend-API"],"pt":["Exige configuração .NET e Blazor","Específico para protocolo de Eventos Enviados pelo Servidor (SSE)","Necessita acesso à API de backend baseada em eventos"],"ru":["Требует настройки .NET и Blazor","Специфичен для протокола событий, отправляемых сервером (SSE)","Требует доступа к бэкенд API на основе событий"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد .NET و Blazor","محدد لبروتوكول أحداث الخادم المرسلة (SSE)","يحتاج إلى وصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات الخلفية القائمة على الأحداث"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7e212838ed784d1a41dcc1880c73db777d7e5411a7098d132f5184aa0c396557","qualityScore":42}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('SylvainChabaud/spec-to-code-factory/factory-spec', 'community', 'SylvainChabaud', 'spec-to-code-factory', 'SylvainChabaud/spec-to-code-factory', 'factory-spec', 9, 2, 42, '2026-02-19T23:20:34Z', '2026-02-26T08:35:22.979Z', '1c71581457409be43a00f324c8704ee235056a1d50a7befc6e7f066904041edd', '{"id":"SylvainChabaud/spec-to-code-factory/factory-spec","name":"factory-spec","description":{"zh":"工厂规范是AI智能代理的Spec-to-Code管道自动化工具，通过4个阶段和5个验证门将需求转化为可交付项目","ja":"ファクトリースペックはAIエージェントのSpec-to-Codeパイプライン自動化ツールで、4つのステージと5つのバリデーションゲートを経て要件を実行可能なプロジェクトに変換する","ko":"공장 규격은 AI 에이전트의 Spec-to-Code 파이프라인 자동화 도구로서 4개의 단계와 5개의 검증 게이트를 통해 요구 사항을 실행 가능한 프로젝트로 변환","es":"Factory-spec es un pipeline automático que transforma un requirements.md en un proyecto livrable a través de 4 fases con agentes especializados y herramientas de calidad","fr":"Factory-spec est un pipeline automatisé qui transforme un requirements.md en un projet livrable via 4 phases avec des agents spécialisés et des outils de qualité","de":"Factory-spec ist ein automatisierter Pipeline, der ein requirements.md in ein lieferbares Projekt durch 4 Phasen mit spezialisierten Agenten und Qualitätswerkzeugen umwandelt","pt":"O factory-spec é uma ferramenta de IA que transforma especificações em código via 4 fases, com 5 gates de validação e agentes especializados","ru":"Factory-spec - это инструмент ИИ, который преобразует спецификации в код через 4 фазы, с 5 воротами проверки и специализированными агентами","ar":"factory-spec هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي تحول المواصفات إلى كود عبر 4 مراحل، مع 5 بوابات التحقق وأدوات متخصصة","en":"Pipeline automatisé Spec-to-Code pour Claude Code. Transforme un requirements.md en projet livrable via 4 phases (BREAK →     MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) avec 5 gates de validation. Inclut agents spécialisés, templates, et outils de qualité."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理工厂规范","ja":"AIエージェントファクトリースペック","ko":"AI 에이전트 공장 규격","es":"Herramientas de Agente de IA: factory-spec para Desarroll...","fr":"Outils d''Agents d''IA: factory-spec pour Développeurs","de":"KI-Tools: factory-spec für Entwickler","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: factory-spec para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: factory-spec для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: factory-spec لل مطورين","en":"factory-spec"},"description":{"zh":"工厂规范是AI智能代理的Spec-to-Code管道自动化工具，通过4个阶段和5个验证门将需求转化为可交付项目","ja":"ファクトリースペックはAIエージェントのSpec-to-Codeパイプライン自動化ツールで、4つのステージと5つのバリデーションゲートを経て要件を実行可能なプロジェクトに変換する","ko":"공장 규격은 AI 에이전트의 Spec-to-Code 파이프라인 자동화 도구로서 4개의 단계와 5개의 검증 게이트를 통해 요구 사항을 실행 가능한 프로젝트로 변환","es":"Factory-spec es un pipeline automático que transforma un requirements.md en un proyecto livrable a través de 4 fases con agentes especializados y herramienta...","fr":"Factory-spec est un pipeline automatisé qui transforme un requirements.md en un projet livrable via 4 phases avec des agents spécialisés et des outils de qua...","de":"Factory-spec ist ein automatisierter Pipeline, der ein requirements.md in ein lieferbares Projekt durch 4 Phasen mit spezialisierten Agenten und Qualitätswer...","pt":"O factory-spec é uma ferramenta de IA que transforma especificações em código via 4 fases, com 5 gates de validação e agentes especializados","ru":"Factory-spec - это инструмент ИИ, который преобразует спецификации в код через 4 фазы, с 5 воротами проверки и специализированными агентами","ar":"factory-spec هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي تحول المواصفات إلى كود عبر 4 مراحل، مع 5 بوابات التحقق وأدوات متخصصة","en":"Pipeline automatisé Spec-to-Code pour Claude Code. Transforme un requirements.md en projet livrable via 4 phases (BREAK →     MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) avec 5 g..."},"definition":{"en":"Pipeline automatisé Spec-to-Code pour Claude Code. Transforme un requirements.md en projet livrable via 4 phases (BREAK →     MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) avec 5 gates de validation. Inclut agents spécialisés, templates, et outils de qualité."},"features":{"zh":["自动化Spec-to-Code管道","4个阶段和5个验证门","支持多种模板和工具","提高开发效率和质量"],"ja":["Spec-to-Codeパイプラインの自動化","4つのステージと5つのバリデーションゲート","様々なテンプレートとツールのサポート","開発効率と品質の向上"],"ko":["Spec-to-Code 파이프라인 자동화","4개의 단계와 5개의 검증 게이트","다양한 템플릿과 도구 지원","개발 효율성과 품질 향상"],"es":["Pipeline automático Spec-to-Code","4 fases de desarrollo (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 puertas de validación","Agentes especializados","Herramientas de calidad"],"fr":["Pipeline automatisé Spec-to-Code","4 phases de développement (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 portes de validation","Agents spécialisés","Outils de qualité"],"de":["Automatisierter Pipeline Spec-to-Code","4 Entwicklungsphasen (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 Validierungstoren","Spezialisierte Agenten","Qualitätswerkzeuge"],"pt":["Automatização do processo de criação de código","4 fases de desenvolvimento (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 gates de validação para garantir a qualidade","Agentes especializados para cada fase do desenvolvimento","Templates e ferramentas de qualidade para melhorar a eficiência"],"ru":["Автоматизация процесса создания кода","4 фазы разработки (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 ворот проверки для обеспечения качества","Специализированные агенты для каждой фазы разработки","Шаблоны и инструменты качества для повышения эффективности"],"ar":["أوتوماتيكية عملية إنشاء الكود","4 مراحل من التطوير (BREAK, MODEL, ACT, DEBRIEF)","5 بوابات التحقق لضمان الجودة","أدوات متخصصة لكل مرحلة من مراحل التطوير","قوالب وأدوات جودة لتحسين الكفاءة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Spec-to-Code","自动化开发","提高开发效率","如何使用AI智能代理","AI智能代理工具","AI智能代理与传统开发方法的比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Spec-to-Code","自動化開発","開発効率の向上","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントツール","AIエージェントと伝統的な開発方法の比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Spec-to-Code","자동화 개발","개발 효율성 향상","AI 에이전트 사용 방법","AI 에이전트 도구","AI 에이전트와 전통적인 개발 방법의 비교"],"es":["cómo usar factory-spec","qué es Spec-to-Code","alternativas a factory-spec","factory-spec vs Claude Code","instalar factory-spec","guía de configuración de factory-spec","herramientas de agente de IA","desarrollo de software con factory-spec"],"fr":["comment utiliser factory-spec","qu''est-ce que Spec-to-Code","alternatives à factory-spec","factory-spec vs Claude Code","installer factory-spec","guide de configuration de factory-spec","outils d''agents d''IA","développement de logiciels avec factory-spec"],"de":["wie man factory-spec verwendet","was ist Spec-to-Code","alternativen zu factory-spec","factory-spec vs Claude Code","installation von factory-spec","konfigurationsanleitung für factory-spec","KI-Tools","Softwareentwicklung mit factory-spec"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","como usar factory-spec","o que é factory-spec","factory-spec vs competitors","factory-spec install","factory-spec setup guide","desenvolvimento de software com ia","automatização de código"],"ru":["инструменты ии","как использовать factory-spec","что такое factory-spec","factory-spec vs конкуренты","установка factory-spec","руководство по настройке factory-spec","разработка программного обеспечения с ии","автоматизация кода"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","كيفية استخدام factory-spec","ما هي factory-spec","factory-spec مقابل المنافسين","تثبيت factory-spec","دليل إعداد factory-spec","تطوير البرمجيات بالذكاء الاصطناعي","أوتوماتيكية الكود"]}},"owner":"SylvainChabaud","repo":"spec-to-code-factory","repoPath":"SylvainChabaud/spec-to-code-factory","stars":9,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-02-19T23:20:34Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"factory-spec","description":"Phase MODEL - Génère specs + ADR + rules","bodyPreview":"# Factory Spec - Phase MODEL\n\nTu es l''orchestrateur de la phase MODEL.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Verifier Gate 1 (entree)** :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/gate-check.js 1 --json\n   ```\n   - Si `status === \"FAIL\"` → STOP immediat (prerequis manquants, ne peut pas corriger).\n   - Terminer avec : `GATE_FAIL|1|<resume erreurs>|0`\n\n2. **Lire le state** :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/factory-state.js get\n   # Retourne: { \"evolutionMode\": \"greenfield|brownfield\", \"evolutionVersion\": N, \"requirementsFile\": \"...\", ...","body":"# Factory Spec - Phase MODEL\n\nTu es l''orchestrateur de la phase MODEL.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Verifier Gate 1 (entree)** :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/gate-check.js 1 --json\n   ```\n   - Si `status === \"FAIL\"` → STOP immediat (prerequis manquants, ne peut pas corriger).\n   - Terminer avec : `GATE_FAIL|1|<resume erreurs>|0`\n\n2. **Lire le state** :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/factory-state.js get\n   # Retourne: { \"evolutionMode\": \"greenfield|brownfield\", \"evolutionVersion\": N, \"requirementsFile\": \"...\", ... }\n\n   # Lister les ADR actifs (brownfield : exclut SUPERSEDED)\n   node tools/list-active-adrs.js --summary\n\n   # Extraire le delta de la version courante (brownfield uniquement)\n   node tools/extract-version-delta.js -f brief -f scope\n   ```\n   Extraire : `evolutionMode`, `evolutionVersion`.\n\n3. **Deleguer aux agents** (sequentiel strict, UN A LA FOIS) :\n\n   **3a. Agent PM** (specs fonctionnelles) :\n   ```bash\n   # Instrumenter la delegation (les hooks ne fonctionnent pas dans les forks)\n   node tools/instrumentation/collector.js agent ''{\"agent\":\"pm\",\"source\":\"factory-spec\"}''\n   ```\n   ```\n   Task(\n     subagent_type: \"pm\",\n     prompt: \"Genere les specs fonctionnelles du projet.\n     Mode: <evolutionMode>. Version: <evolutionVersion>.\n     Si mode=greenfield: CREATE docs/specs/system.md et docs/specs/domain.md.\n     Si mode=brownfield: EDIT les specs existantes pour les mettre a jour.\n     DELTA VERSION COURANTE: <output de extract-version-delta.js>\n     Lis les fichiers BREAK: docs/brief.md, docs/scope.md, docs/acceptance.md.\n     Lis les templates: templates/specs/system.md, templates/specs/domain.md.\n     IMPORTANT: Respecte EXACTEMENT les headings des templates (##).\n     IMPORTANT: NE PAS inventer de numeros de version pour les librairies.\n     Ecrire uniquement le nom de la lib (ex: ''Tailwind CSS'', pas ''Tailwind CSS 3+'').\",\n     description: \"MODEL - PM specs\"\n   )\n   ```\n\n   **3b. Verification web des dependances et generation de stack-reference.md** (fait par le fork, AVANT l''architect) :\n\n   > **OBLIGATOIRE** : Verifier les dependances de la stack sur internet AVANT de deleguer a l''architect.\n   > Les LLMs ont souvent des connaissances obsoletes sur les versions recentes des libs.\n   > L''architect n''a pas acces a WebSearch/WebFetch — c''est le fork qui fournit les infos verifiees.\n\n   **Etape 1 : Identifier la stack dans le brief/scope**\n\n   Lire `docs/brief.md` et `docs/scope.md` pour extraire la liste des dependances prevues (framework, CSS lib, bundler, test runner, linter, chart lib, etc.).\n   Constituer une liste : `[ \"react\", \"tailwindcss\", \"vite\", \"vitest\", ... ]`.\n\n   **Etape 2 : Verifier les versions via npm registry** (source canonique)\n\n   Pour **chaque dependance** identifiee :\n   ```bash\n   npm view <package> version\n   # Retourne la derniere version stable (ex: \"19.1.0\")\n   ```\n   Si le nom npm n''est pas evident (ex: Tailwind CSS → `tailwindcss`), utiliser :\n   ```bash\n   npm search <lib> --json | head -5\n   ```\n\n   > **C''est la source la plus fiable** pour les numeros de version.\n   > Ne JAMAIS utiliser une version extraite d''une page web si elle contredit npm registry.\n\n   Compteur : noter le nombre de deps verifiees via npm (`verified_count`).\n\n   **Etape 3 : Rechercher les configs et breaking changes via web** (complementaire)\n\n   Pour **chaque dependance a risque de breaking changes** (identifiee dans le brief/scope) :\n\n   a. **Trouver la doc officielle** :\n      - `WebSearch` : `\"<lib> getting started\"` ou `\"<lib> installation guide\"`\n      - Privilegier les domaines officiels (npmjs.com, github.com/<org>, docs officiels)\n\n   b. **Extraire la configuration** :\n      - `WebFetch` sur la page d''installation officielle\n      - Extraire : packages a installer, fichiers de config requis, snippets de reference\n      - Copier le snippet EXACT depuis la doc (pas de memoire LLM)\n\n   c. **Identifier les breaking changes** :\n      - `WebSearch` : `\"<lib> migration guide\"` ou `\"<lib> upgrade from v<N-1>\"`\n      - Documenter : ancien pattern (a eviter) vs nouveau pattern (a utiliser)\n\n   > **Si WebSearch/WebFetch echoue** (rate limit, erreur reseau) : logger un warning et continuer.\n   > La verification configs/breaking changes est best-effort. Les versions npm sont obligatoires.\n\n   **Etape 4 : Seuil de fiabilite**\n\n   Calculer : `ratio = verified_count / total_deps`.\n   - Si `ratio >= 0.5` (50%+) → continuer normalement.\n   - Si `ratio < 0.5` → logger un warning :\n     ```bash\n     node tools/factory-log.js \"MODEL\" \"stack-warning\" \"Seuil de fiabilite non atteint: X/Y deps verifiees via npm. Risque de versions incorrectes.\"\n     ```\n     Continuer quand meme (ne pas bloquer), mais le warning sera visible dans les logs.\n\n   **Etape 5 : Generer `docs/specs/stack-reference.md`**\n\n   Lire le template `templates/specs/stack-reference.md`.\n   Creer le fichier `docs/specs/stack-reference.md` en remplissant :\n   - **Dependencies runtime** : tableau avec package, version exacte (depuis npm), commande install, URL source\n   - **Dependencies dev** : idem pour les deps de dev\n   - **Configurations de reference** : pour chaque lib necessitant un fichier de config, inclure le snippet EXACT copie depuis la doc officielle (pas de memoire LLM)\n   - **Compatibilite** : notes inter-dependances (ex: \"Tailwind v4 necessite @tailwindcss/vite\")\n   - **Breaking changes connus** : tableau ancien vs nouveau pour chaque lib avec breaking change\n\n   > **Ce fichier est la source de verite** pour toutes les etapes suivantes.\n   > L''architect et le developer doivent s''y referer, pas inventer de versions.\n\n   **Etape 6 : Logger**\n   ```bash\n   node tools/factory-log.js \"MODEL\" \"stack-verified\" \"Verification stack: X/Y deps verifiees via npm, Z configs web → docs/specs/stack-reference.md\"\n   ```\n\n   **3c. Agent Architect** (specs techniques + ADR, avec stack verifiee) :\n   ```bash\n   # Extraire le delta depuis les specs PM (disponibles apres 3a)\n   node tools/extract-version-delta.js -f system -f domain\n\n   # Instrumenter la delegation\n   node tools/instrumentation/collector.js agent ''{\"agent\":\"architect\",\"source\":\"factory-spec\"}''\n   ```\n   ```\n   Task(\n     subagent_type: \"architect\",\n     prompt: \"Genere les specs techniques et ADR.\n     Mode: <evolutionMode>. Version: <evolutionVersion>.\n     Si mode=greenfield: CREATE docs/specs/api.md, ADR-0001-stack.md, project-config.json.\n     Si mode=brownfield: EDIT api.md + CREATE nouveaux ADR + marquer anciens SUPERSEDED.\n     DELTA VERSION COURANTE: <output de extract-version-delta.js>\n     Lis les fichiers BREAK: docs/brief.md, docs/scope.md, docs/acceptance.md.\n     Lis les specs PM: docs/specs/system.md, docs/specs/domain.md.\n     Lis le fichier stack de reference: docs/specs/stack-reference.md.\n     Lis les templates: templates/specs/api.md, templates/adr/ADR-template.md, templates/specs/project-config.json.\n     IMPORTANT: Respecte EXACTEMENT les headings des templates (##).\n\n     STACK REFERENCE (source de verite - UTILISE CES VERSIONS ET CONFIGS, PAS TA MEMOIRE) :\n     Lis docs/specs/stack-reference.md pour toutes les versions, packages et configs.\n\n     Pour chaque dependance dans l''ADR :\n     - Utilise la version exacte et les packages indiques dans stack-reference.md\n     - Inclus les snippets de configuration de reference dans une section ''## Configuration de reference'' de l''ADR\n     - Si une lib a un setup specifique (ex: plugin Vite au lieu de PostCSS), documente-le\n     - NE PAS inventer de config : utilise UNIQUEMENT les infos de stack-reference.md\",\n     description: \"MODEL - Architect specs\"\n   )\n   ```\n\n   **3d. Agent Rules-Memory** (rules Claude Code) :\n   ```bash\n   # Extraire le delta depuis toutes les specs (disponibles apres 3a+3c)\n   node tools/extract-version-delta.js -f system -f domain -f api\n\n   # Instrumenter la delegation\n   node tools/instrumentation/collector.js agent ''{\"agent\":\"rules-memory\",\"source\":\"factory-spec\"}''\n   ```\n   ```\n   Task(\n     subagent_type: \"rules-memory\",\n     prompt: \"Genere les rules Claude Code pour le projet.\n     Mode: <evolutionMode>. Version: <evolutionVersion>.\n     Si mode=greenfield: CREATE les rules dans .claude/rules/.\n     Si mode=brownfield: mettre a jour les rules existantes, supprimer les obsoletes.\n     ADR ACTIFS: <liste des paths retournes par list-active-adrs.js --summary>\n     DELTA VERSION COURANTE: <output de extract-version-delta.js>\n     IMPORTANT: NE PAS charger les ADR au statut SUPERSEDED.\n     Lis les specs: docs/specs/system.md, docs/specs/domain.md, docs/specs/api.md.\n     Lis le template: templates/rule.md.\",\n     description: \"MODEL - Rules generation\"\n   )\n   ```\n\n4. **Executer Gate 2 (sortie avec auto-remediation)** :\n\n   ```bash\n   node tools/gate-check.js 2 --json\n   ```\n\n   Suivre le **protocole standard de gate handling** :\n\n   **Tentative 1** : Analyser le JSON retourne.\n   - Si `status === \"PASS\"` → continuer a l''etape 5.\n   - Si `status === \"FAIL\"` :\n     - Lire `errors[]`. Pour chaque erreur `fixable: true` :\n       - `missing_section` → identifier le fichier et le template de reference dans le message d''erreur (`ref: templates/...`). Relancer l''agent responsable avec prompt : \"Corrige [fichier]. Section manquante : [section]. Lis le template [template] et respecte exactement les headings.\"\n       - `missing_file` → identifier le fichier manquant :\n         - `stack-reference.md` → re-executer l''etape 3b (verification web + generation du fichier). C''est le fork qui le fait, pas un agent.\n         - `system.md` / `domain.md` → relancer l''agent PM (step 3a).\n         - `api.md` → relancer l''agent architect (step 3c).\n         - Autre → relancer l''agent responsable.\n       - `missing_pattern` → identifier le pattern manquant :\n         - `.claude/rules/*.md` → relancer l''agent rules-memory (step 3d).\n         - `docs/adr/ADR-*` → relancer l''agent architect (step 3c).\n       - `config` → relancer l''architect pour corriger project-config.json.\n       - `security` → corriger les secrets/PII directement.\n     - Pour chaque erreur `fixable: false` → STOP, ne pas retenter.\n     - Re-executer : `node tools/gate-check.js 2 --json`\n\n   **Tentative 2** : Relancer les agents fautifs complets (PM, architect ou rules-memory selon les erreurs restantes).\n   - Re-executer : `node tools/gate-check.js 2 --json`\n\n   **Tentative 3** : Si toujours FAIL, retourner le rapport d''echec.\n   - **NE PAS continuer le pipeline.**\n   - Terminer avec : `GATE_FAIL|2|<resume erreurs separees par ;>|3`\n\n5. **Sync ADR** (brownfield) :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/list-active-adrs.js --summary\n   ```\n\n6. **Logger** via :\n   ```bash\n   node tools/factory-log.js \"MODEL\" \"completed\" \"Phase MODEL terminee\"\n   ```\n\n7. **Retourner** un resume avec liste des fichiers generes (chemins complets).\n\n## Protocole d''echec\n\n- **Gate d''entree** (Gate 1) : Si FAIL → STOP immediat + marqueur `GATE_FAIL|1|...|0`.\n- **Gate de sortie** (Gate 2) : Auto-remediation 3x puis marqueur `GATE_FAIL|2|...|3` si echec persistant.\n- **Jamais** de STOP silencieux — toujours retourner un rapport structure.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:35:22.979Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced factory specification capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级工厂规格功能的代码生成代理。","ja":"コード生成エージェントが高度なファクトリースペック機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 공장 사양 기능이 필요한 코드 생성 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Generación de Código que necesitan capacidades de especificación de fábrica avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Génération de Code nécessitant des capacités de spécification de fabrique avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Generierungsagenten, die erweiterte Fabrik-Spezifikationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Geração de Código que precisam de capacidades avançadas de especificação de fábrica.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов генерации кода, которым необходимы расширенные возможности спецификации фабрики.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء توليد الكود الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحديد مواصفات المصنع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate deterministic code structures using a pipeline automatisé Spec-to-Code approach with 4 phases (BREAK →     MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) and 5 gates de validation. It provides agents spécialisés, templates, and outils de qualité.","zh":"使代理能够使用管道自动化的规格至代码方法生成确定性代码结构，包括4个阶段（BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF）和5个验证门。它为代理提供专用模板和质量工具。","ja":"エージェントがパイプライン自動化された仕様からコードアプローチを使用して決定性コード構造を生成できるようにします。4つのフェーズ（BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF）と5つのバリデーションゲートを含みます。エージェントに特化したテンプレートや品質ツールを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 파이프라인 자동화된 사양에서 코드 접근 방식을 사용하여 결정적 코드 구조를 생성할 수 있도록 합니다. 4개의 단계(BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF)와 5개의 검증 게이트를 포함합니다. 에이전트에 특화된 템플릿 및 품질 도구를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar estructuras de código deterministas utilizando un enfoque automatisé Spec-to-Code con 4 fases (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) y 5 gates de validación. Proporciona agentes especializados, plantillas y herramientas de calidad.","fr":"Habilite les agents à générer des structures de code déterministes en utilisant une approche automatisé Spec-to-Code avec 4 phases (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) et 5 gates de validation. Fournit des agents spécialisés, des modèles et des outils de qualité.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, deterministische Code-Strukturen mit einem automatisierten Spec-to-Code-Ansatz mit 4 Phasen (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) und 5 gates de validación zu generieren. Bietet spezialisierte Agenten, Vorlagen und Qualitäts-Tools.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar estruturas de código determinístico usando uma abordagem automática de Spec-to-Code com 4 fases (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) e 5 portas de validação. Ele fornece agentes especializados, templates e ferramentas de qualidade.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать детерминированные кодовые структуры, используя автоматизированный подход Spec-to-Code с 4 фазами (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) и 5 воротами валидации. Он предоставляет специализированных агентов, шаблоны и инструменты качества.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توليد هياكل كود محددة باستخدام نهج أوتوماتيكي من Spec-to-Code مع 4 مراحل (BREAK → MODEL → ACT → DEBRIEF) و 5 بوابات التحقق. يوفر وكلاء متخصصين و قوالب وأدوات جودة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code generation from factory specifications","Generating code templates for different programming languages","Debugging code structures using a phased approach"],"zh":["从工厂规格自动生成代码","为不同编程语言生成代码模板","使用分阶段方法调试代码结构"],"ja":["ファクトリースペックからコードを自動生成する","異なるプログラミング言語のコードテンプレートを生成する","段階的なアプローチを使用してコード構造をデバッグする"],"ko":["공장 사양에서 코드를 자동 생성하는 것","다른 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 코드 템플릿 생성","분阶段 접근 방식을 사용하여 코드 구조 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de código a partir de especificaciones de fábrica","Generación de plantillas de código para diferentes lenguajes de programación","Depuración de estructuras de código utilizando un enfoque por fases"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de code à partir de spécifications de fabrique","Génération de modèles de code pour différents langages de programmation","Débogage de structures de code en utilisant une approche par phases"],"de":["Automatisierung der Code-Generierung aus Fabrik-Spezifikationen","Generierung von Code-Vorlagen für verschiedene Programmiersprachen","Fehlersuche in Code-Strukturen unter Verwendung eines phasenweisen Ansatzes"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de código a partir de especificações de fábrica","Gerar templates de código para diferentes linguagens de programação","Depurar estruturas de código usando uma abordagem por fases"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию кода из спецификаций фабрики","Генерировать шаблоны кода для различных языков программирования","Отладить кодовые структуры, используя фазовый подход"],"ar":["أتمتة توليد الكود من مواصفات المصنع","توليد قوالب من الكود للغات البرمجة المختلفة","تصحيح هياكل الكود باستخدام نهج مرحلي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires a requirements.md file as input","Limited to 5 gates de validation","Python 3.10+ only for node tools execution"],"zh":["需要requirements.md文件作为输入","仅限5个验证门","仅适用于Python 3.10+的节点工具执行"],"ja":["入力としてrequirements.mdファイルを必要とする","バリデーションゲートは5つまで","Python 3.10+のみでノードツールの実行"],"ko":["입력으로 requirements.md 파일이 필요","검증 게이트는 5개까지","Python 3.10+만 노드 도구 실행"],"es":["Requiere un archivo requirements.md como entrada","Limitado a 5 gates de validación","Python 3.10+ solo para la ejecución de herramientas de node"],"fr":["Nécessite un fichier requirements.md comme entrée","Limité à 5 gates de validation","Python 3.10+ uniquement pour l''exécution des outils de node"],"de":["Benötigt eine requirements.md-Datei als Eingabe","Begrenzt auf 5 gates de validación","Python 3.10+ nur für die Ausführung von Node-Tools"],"pt":["Exige um arquivo requirements.md como entrada","Limitado a 5 portas de validação","Python 3.10+ apenas para execução de ferramentas de node"],"ru":["Требует файла requirements.md в качестве входных данных","Ограничен 5 воротами валидации","Python 3.10+ только для выполнения инструментов узла"],"ar":["يتطلب ملف requirements.md كمدخل","محدود بـ 5 بوابات للتحقق","Python 3.10+ فقط لتشغيل أدوات العقدة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"1c71581457409be43a00f324c8704ee235056a1d50a7befc6e7f066904041edd","qualityScore":42}');
