ite + TypeScript + GPT-5.2を使用して開発","スティーブン・キングのThe Long Walkに基づく","サバイバルシミュレーションゲーム","AIエージェントの統合","高性能レンダリング","クロスプラットフォーム対応"],"ko":["Vite + TypeScript + GPT-5.2로 개발","스티븐 킹의 The Long Walk를 기반으로","생存 시뮬레이션 게임","AI 에이전트 통합","고성능 렌더링","크로스 플랫폼 지원"],"es":["Integración con Vite para una experiencia de juego fluida","Utilización de TypeScript para un desarrollo más eficiente","Implementación de GPT-5.2 para una inteligencia artificial avanzada","Diseño de juego de supervivencia inspirado en The Long Walk","Mejora de la experiencia de juego con agentes de IA"],"fr":["Intégration avec Vite pour une expérience de jeu fluide","Utilisation de TypeScript pour un développement plus efficace","Mise en œuvre de GPT-5.2 pour une intelligence artificielle avancée","Conception de jeu de survie inspirée de The Long Walk","Amélioration de l''expérience de jeu avec des agents IA"],"de":["Integration mit Vite für ein flüssiges Spielerlebnis","Verwendung von TypeScript für eine effizientere Entwicklung","Implementierung von GPT-5.2 für eine fortschrittliche künstliche Intelligenz","Spiel-Design inspiriert von The Long Walk","Verbesserung des Spielerlebnisses mit KI-Agenten"],"pt":["Desenvolvido com Vite e TypeScript","Integração com GPT-5.2","Jogo de simulação de sobrevivência baseado em The Long Walk","Experiência única de jogo","Utiliza agente de IA para simulação"],"ru":["Разработан на Vite и TypeScript","Интеграция с GPT-5.2","Симуляционная игра о выживании по мотивам The Long Walk","Уникальный игровой опыт","Использует ИИ агента для симуляции"],"ar":["تم تطويره باستخدام Vite و TypeScript","التكامل مع GPT-5.2","لعبة محاكاة البقاء تعتمد على رواية ستيفن كينج","تجربة فريدة من نوعها","يستخدم وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي للمحاكاة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","生存模拟游戏","The Long Walk","Vite","TypeScript","GPT-5.2","如何使用End-Session","End-Session教程","AI工具集成","跨平台游戏开发"],"ja":["AIエージェント","サバイバルシミュレーションゲーム","The Long Walk","Vite","TypeScript","GPT-5.2","End-Sessionの使い方","End-Sessionチュートリアル","AIエージェントの統合","クロスプラットフォームゲーム開発"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","생存 시뮬레이션 게임","The Long Walk","Vite","TypeScript","GPT-5.2","End-Session 사용법","End-Session 튜토리얼","AI 에이전트 통합","크로스 플랫폼 게임 개발"],"es":["agentes de IA para juegos","cómo utilizar GPT-5.2 en juegos","alternativas a GPT-5.2","Vite vs React","guía de instalación de TypeScript","juegos de supervivencia con IA","desarrollo de juegos con Vite y TypeScript","agentes de IA para juegos de supervivencia"],"fr":["agents IA pour jeux","comment utiliser GPT-5.2 dans les jeux","alternatives à GPT-5.2","Vite vs React","guide d''installation de TypeScript","jeux de survie avec IA","développement de jeux avec Vite et TypeScript","agents IA pour jeux de survie"],"de":["KI-Agenten für Spiele","wie man GPT-5.2 in Spielen verwendet","Alternativen zu GPT-5.2","Vite vs React","Anleitung zur Installation von TypeScript","Überlebensspiele mit KI","Spiele-Entwicklung mit Vite und TypeScript","KI-Agenten für Überlebensspiele"],"pt":["como usar agente End-Session","o que é agente End-Session","alternativa ao agente End-Session","agente End-Session vs outros agentes","instalar agente End-Session","guia de configuração do agente End-Session","jogos de simulação de sobrevivência","desenvolvimento de jogos com Vite e TypeScript"],"ru":["как использовать агент End-Session","что такое агент End-Session","альтернатива агенту End-Session","агент End-Session vs другие агенты","установить агент End-Session","руководство по настройке агента End-Session","симуляционные игры о выживании","разработка игр на Vite и TypeScript"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام وكلاء النهاية الجلسة","ما هو وكلاء النهاية الجلسة","بديل ل وكلاء النهاية الجلسة","وكلاء النهاية الجلسة مقابل وكلاء آخرين","تثبيت وكلاء النهاية الجلسة","دليل إعداد وكلاء النهاية الجلسة","ألعاب محاكاة البقاء","تطوير الألعاب باستخدام Vite و TypeScript"]}},"owner":"bretstarr2024","repo":"The-Long-Walk","repoPath":"bretstarr2024/The-Long-Walk","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T06:13:47Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"end-session","description":"Session closeout — canonicalize, verify, commit, produce handoff artifacts","bodyPreview":"# /end-session\n\nYou are closing a working session on **The Long Walk**. This skill is **write-heavy and procedural**. Execute all steps in order. Do not skip steps. Only ask questions if execution is impossible without clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Canonicalize state\n\nReconcile everything from this session into durable artifacts.\n\n### 1a. Update MEMORY.md\n- Update `~/.claude/projects/-Volumes-Queen-Amara-The-Long-Walk/memory/MEMORY.md`\n- Add any new patterns, lessons learned, or architecture c","body":"# /end-session\n\nYou are closing a working session on **The Long Walk**. This skill is **write-heavy and procedural**. Execute all steps in order. Do not skip steps. Only ask questions if execution is impossible without clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Canonicalize state\n\nReconcile everything from this session into durable artifacts.\n\n### 1a. Update MEMORY.md\n- Update `~/.claude/projects/-Volumes-Queen-Amara-The-Long-Walk/memory/MEMORY.md`\n- Add any new patterns, lessons learned, or architecture changes discovered this session\n- Remove or correct any entries that are now outdated\n- Keep it under 200 lines\n\n### 1b. Update CHANGELOG.md\n- If significant features were added, add a new version entry at the top of `docs/CHANGELOG.md`\n- Follow semver: MAJOR (breaking), MINOR (new feature), PATCH (fix)\n\n### 1c. Mark deferred items explicitly\nIf anything was discussed but intentionally not done, record it. \"We chose not to do X\" is valuable.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Verify builds\n\nBoth stacks must pass before committing.\n\n### Client (Vite + TypeScript)\n```bash\ncd \"/Volumes/Queen Amara/The Long Walk\" && npx tsc --noEmit\n```\n**Gate:** If this fails, fix the type errors before proceeding.\n\n### Server (if server/ exists)\n```bash\ncd \"/Volumes/Queen Amara/The Long Walk\" && npx tsc --noEmit -p server/tsconfig.json\n```\n**Gate:** Fix errors before proceeding.\n\n### Build check\n```bash\ncd \"/Volumes/Queen Amara/The Long Walk\" && npx vite build\n```\n**Gate:** Must succeed.\n\nIf any gate fails and you cannot fix it, **stop and tell the user what''s broken**.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Commit and push\n\n### 3a. Stage changes\nReview all modified files with `git status` and `git diff`. Stage files intentionally.\n\n**Never stage:**\n- `.env`, `.env.local`, credentials files\n- `node_modules/`, `dist/`\n\n### 3b. Commit\nUse atomic commits — one logical change per commit.\n\nCommit message format: `type(scope): description`\n- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `chore`, `test`\n- Scope: `client`, `server`, `viz`, `agents`, `docs`, `skills`\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ntype(scope): description\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n### 3c. Push\n```bash\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n### 3d. Deploy to Railway\nAfter pushing, deploy the latest code to Railway production:\n```\nUse the Railway MCP deploy tool with workspacePath=\"/Volumes/Queen Amara/The Long Walk\"\n```\nWait for deployment to complete. Verify the health endpoint responds:\n```bash\ncurl -s https://the-long-walk-production.up.railway.app/api/health\n```\n**Gate:** Health check must return `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`. If it fails, check Railway logs via the MCP `get-logs` tool.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Generate session ledger (YAML)\n\nSave to `docs/sessions/SESSION_LEDGER_{date}_{slug}.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nsession_id: \"{date}-{slug}\"\ndate: \"{YYYY-MM-DD}\"\nbranch: \"main\"\nversion: \"{from CHANGELOG}\"\nprior_session: \"{session_id from the last ledger}\"\n\nbuild_verification:\n  client_typescript: \"pass | fail\"\n  server_typescript: \"pass | fail | n/a\"\n  vite_build: \"pass | fail\"\n\ncommits:\n  - hash: \"{short hash}\"\n    message: \"{commit message}\"\n\nartifacts_updated:\n  - path: \"{file path}\"\n    change: \"{what changed and why}\"\n\ndecisions_made:\n  - decision: \"{what was decided}\"\n    rationale: \"{why}\"\n\nopen_questions:\n  - \"{question that needs future resolution}\"\n\nknown_risks:\n  - \"{risk that exists}\"\n\nexplicitly_deferred:\n  - \"{thing we chose not to do and why}\"\n\nnext_actions:\n  - \"{ordered, executable step 1}\"\n  - \"{ordered, executable step 2}\"\n  - \"{ordered, executable step 3}\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Write human-readable handoff\n\nSave to `docs/sessions/HANDOFF_{date}_{slug}.md`\n\nThis file must be **self-contained** — sufficient to resume work without prior conversation history.\n\n### Required sections:\n\n```markdown\n# Session Handoff: {Session Title}\n\n**Date:** {YYYY-MM-DD}\n**Session ID:** {from ledger}\n**Version:** {from ledger}\n**Branch:** main\n\n---\n\n## Where We Are\n{2-3 paragraphs: Current state of the project. What works. What the user sees.}\n\n## What Changed This Session\n{Bullet list of every meaningful change, organized by area:}\n### Client\n- {change}\n### Server\n- {change}\n### Infrastructure\n- {change}\n\n## Why These Changes Were Made\n{Brief context — what prompted this work, what problem it solves}\n\n## What Must Happen Next\n{Ordered list of immediate next steps}\n\n## Decisions Made (Do Not Re-Debate)\n{List of decisions with rationale}\n\n## Explicitly Deferred\n{Things we discussed but chose not to do, and why}\n\n## Known Risks\n{Anything that could bite us}\n\n## Key Files Modified\n{Table of files touched and what changed}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Final integrity check\n\nRun through this checklist:\n\n- [ ] All durable knowledge persisted (MEMORY.md, CHANGELOG updated as needed)\n- [ ] Working tree clean (`git status` shows nothing)\n- [ ] Pushed to remote (`git log origin/main..HEAD` shows nothing)\n- [ ] Deployed to Railway (health check passes)\n- [ ] Session ledger saved to `docs/sessions/`\n- [ ] Session handoff saved to `docs/sessions/`\n- [ ] MEMORY.md is under 200 lines\n\nReport the checklist results. If anything is blocked, state what, why, and what input is needed.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\n1. Execute steps in order. Do not skip steps.\n2. Do not ask exploratory or preference questions. Only ask if execution is impossible without clarification.\n3. If a step can''t be completed, explicitly state what''s blocked and why.\n4. Atomic commits — one logical change per commit, clear messages.\n5. Never commit secrets, credentials, or `.env` files.\n6. The handoff must be self-contained — no \"see our conversation\" references.\n7. If nothing meaningful changed this session (just research/conversation), produce a minimal ledger noting \"research-only session, no code changes\" and skip build/commit steps.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T14:58:01.734Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Procedural Agents needing session closure and state reconciliation capabilities, such as those utilizing Vite, TypeScript, and GPT-5.2 agents.","zh":"非常适合需要会话关闭和状态协调功能的程序代理，例如使用 Vite、TypeScript 和 GPT-5.2 代理的代理。","ja":"セッションのクローズと状態の調整機能が必要な手続き型エージェントに最適です。例えば、Vite、TypeScript、GPT-5.2 エージェントなどのエージェントが該当します。","ko":"세션 종료 및 상태 조정 기능이 필요한 절차적 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 Vite, TypeScript 및 GPT-5.2 에이전트와 같은 에이전트가 있습니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes procedimentales que necesitan capacidad de cierre de sesión y reconciliación de estado, como aquellos que utilizan Vite, TypeScript y agentes GPT-5.2.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents procéduraux nécessitant une fermeture de session et des capacités de réconciliation d''état, tels que ceux utilisant Vite, TypeScript et des agents GPT-5.2.","de":"Perfekt für prozedurale Agenten, die Sitzungsschließ- und Statusabgleichfunktionen benötigen, wie z. B. solche, die Vite, TypeScript und GPT-5.2-Agents verwenden.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Procedurais que necessitam de fechamento de sessão e capacidades de reconciliação de estado, como aqueles que utilizam Vite, TypeScript e agentes GPT-5.2.","ru":"Идеально подходит для процедурных агентов, которым необходимы возможности закрытия сессии и согласования состояния, такие как те, которые используют Vite, TypeScript и агенты GPT-5.2.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الإجرائيين الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات إغلاق الجلسة ومراجعة الحالة، مثل أولئك الذين يستخدمون Vite وTypeScript ووكلاء GPT-5.2."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reconcile session data into durable artifacts, utilizing Markdown files like MEMORY.md, ensuring data persistence and facilitating future session continuity through updated records of patterns, lessons learned, and architecture changes.","zh":"赋予代理将会话数据协调为持久性构件的能力，利用 Markdown 文件（如 MEMORY.md），确保数据持久性并通过更新的模式、经验教训和架构变化记录来促进未来的会话连续性。","ja":"エージェントにセッションデータを永続的なアーティファクトに調整する能力を付与します。Markdown ファイル（例：MEMORY.md）を使用して、データの永続性を確保し、更新されたパターン、学び、Architecture 変更のレコードを通じて将来のセッションの連続性を促進します。","ko":"에이전트가 세션 데이터를 지속 가능한 아티팩트로 조정할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. Markdown 파일(MEMORY.md 같은)을 사용하여 데이터의 지속성을 보장하고, 업데이트된 패턴, 교훈 및 아키텍처 변경 기록을 통해 미래의 세션 연속성을 용이하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a reconciliar los datos de sesión en artefactos duraderos, utilizando archivos Markdown como MEMORY.md, garantizando la persistencia de los datos y facilitando la continuidad de la sesión futura a través de registros actualizados de patrones, lecciones aprendidas y cambios en la arquitectura.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réconcilier les données de session en artefacts durables, en utilisant des fichiers Markdown comme MEMORY.md, garantissant la persistance des données et facilitant la continuité de la session future grâce à des enregistrements mis à jour de modèles, de leçons apprises et de changements d''architecture.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Sitzungsdaten in beständige Artefakte zu überführen, indem Markdown-Dateien wie MEMORY.md verwendet werden, wodurch die Datenbeständigkeit gewährleistet und die zukünftige Sitzungsfortsetzung durch aktualisierte Aufzeichnungen von Mustern, Erfahrungen und Architekturänderungen erleichtert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reconciliar os dados da sessão em artefatos duráveis, utilizando arquivos Markdown como MEMORY.md, garantindo a persistência dos dados e facilitando a continuidade das sessões futuras por meio de registros atualizados de padrões, lições aprendidas e alterações na arquitetura.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью согласовать данные сессии в прочные артефакты, используя файлы Markdown, такие как MEMORY.md, обеспечивая сохранность данных и облегчая последующую непрерывность сессий через обновленные записи шаблонов, уроков, извлеченных из опыта, и изменений в архитектуре.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تسويف بيانات الجلسة في هياكل متينة، باستخدام ملفات Markdown مثل MEMORY.md، وضمان استمرار البيانات وتسهيل استمرارية الجلسات المستقبلية من خلال سجلات محدثة للأنمط والدروس المستفادة وتغييرات الهندسة المعمارية."},"useCases":{"en":["Canonicalizing state at the end of a survival simulation game session","Updating project memory with new patterns and lessons learned","Ensuring data durability through reconciliation of session artifacts"],"zh":["在生存模拟游戏会话结束时规范化状态","使用新的模式和经验教训更新项目内存","通过会话构件的协调来确保数据的持久性"],"ja":["サバイバルシミュレーションゲームのセッション終了時に状態を正規化する","新しいパターンと学びを使用してプロジェクトメモリを更新する","セッションアーティファクトの調整を通じてデータの永続性を確保する"],"ko":["생존 시뮬레이션 게임 세션 종료 시 상태를 표준화하는 것","새로운 패턴과 교훈을 사용하여 프로젝트 메모리를 업데이트하는 것","세션 아티팩트의 조정을 통해 데이터의 지속성을 보장하는 것"],"es":["Canonicalizar el estado al final de una sesión de juego de simulación de supervivencia","Actualizar la memoria del proyecto con nuevos patrones y lecciones aprendidas","Garantizar la durabilidad de los datos a través de la reconciliación de artefactos de sesión"],"fr":["Canonicaliser l''état à la fin d''une session de jeu de simulation de survie","Mettre à jour la mémoire du projet avec de nouveaux modèles et leçons apprises","Assurer la durabilité des données grâce à la réconciliation des artefacts de session"],"de":["Den Status am Ende einer Überlebenssimulationspiel-Sitzung kanonisch machen","Das Projektgedächtnis mit neuen Mustern und Erfahrungen aktualisieren","Die Datenbeständigkeit