ong-poll, SSE), producer idempotency, JSON batch mode, TTL "},"features":{"zh":["流读取支持","生产者幂等性","JSON批处理模式","TTL支持","使用axum和tokio的Rust实现"],"ja":["ストリーミング読み取りのサポート","プロデューサーの冪等性","JSONバッチモード","TTLのサポート","axumとtokioを使用したRustの実装"],"ko":["스트리밍 읽기 지원","생산자 동등성","JSON 배치 모드","TTL 지원","axum과 tokio를 사용하여 Rust로 구현"],"es":["Implementación de Durable Streams en Rust","Soporte para lecturas de streaming","Productor idempotente","Modo batch JSON","TTL (Time To Live)"],"fr":["Implémentation de Durable Streams en Rust","Prise en charge des lectures de streaming","Producteur idempotent","Mode batch JSON","TTL (Time To Live)"],"de":["Implementierung von Durable Streams in Rust","Unterstützung für Streaming-Lesevorgänge","Idempotenter Produzent","JSON-Batch-Modus","TTL (Time To Live)"],"pt":["Suporte a leituras de streaming","Produtor idempotente","Modo de lote JSON","TTL (Time To Live)"],"ru":["Поддержка потоковых чтений","Идемпотентный продюсер","Режим пакетной обработки JSON","TTL (Time To Live)"],"ar":["دعم قراءات التدفق","إنتاج المُتكرر","وضع المجموعة JSON","TTL (زمن العيش)"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Durable Streams协议","Rust实现","axum","tokio","流读取","生产者幂等性","JSON批处理","TTL","如何使用m13-domain-error"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Durable Streamsプロトコル","Rustの実装","axum","tokio","ストリーミング読み取り","プロデューサーの冪等性","JSONバッチモード","TTL","m13-domain-errorの使い方"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Durable Streams 프로토콜","Rust로 구현","axum","tokio","스트리밍 읽기","생산자 동등성","JSON 배치 모드","TTL","m13-domain-error 사용 방법"],"es":["herramientas de AI","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","cómo usar m13-domain-error","guía de instalación de m13-domain-error","m13-domain-error vs alternativas"],"fr":["outils d''IA","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","comment utiliser m13-domain-error","guide d''installation de m13-domain-error","m13-domain-error vs alternatives"],"de":["KI-Tools","Durable Streams","Rust","axum","tokio","wie man m13-domain-error verwendet","Installationsanleitung für m13-domain-error","m13-domain-error vs Alternativen"],"pt":["como usar m13-domain-error","o que é Durable Streams","m13-domain-error alternativa","m13-domain-error vs axum","instalar m13-domain-error","guia de configuração m13-domain-error"],"ru":["как использовать m13-domain-error","что такое Durable Streams","альтернатива m13-domain-error","m13-domain-error vs axum","установить m13-domain-error","руководство по настройке m13-domain-error"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام m13-domain-error","ما هو Durable Streams","بديل m13-domain-error","m13-domain-error مقابل axum","تثبيت m13-domain-error","دليل إعداد m13-domain-error"]}},"owner":"thesampaton","repo":"durable-streams-reference","repoPath":"thesampaton/durable-streams-reference","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.930Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m13-domain-error","description":"Use when designing domain error handling. Keywords: domain error, error categorization, recovery strategy, retry, fallback, domain error hierarchy, user-facing vs internal errors, error code design, circuit breaker, graceful degradation, resilience, error context, backoff, retry with backoff, error recovery, transient vs permanent error, 领域错误, 错误分类, 恢复策略, 重试, 熔断器, 优雅降级","bodyPreview":"# Domain Error Strategy\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Who needs to handle this error, and how should they recover?**\n\nBefore designing error types:\n- Is this user-facing or internal?\n- Is recovery possible?\n- What context is needed for debugging?\n\n---\n\n## Error Categorization\n\n| Error Type | Audience | Recovery | Example |\n|------------|----------|----------|---------|\n| User-facing | End users | Guide action | `InvalidEmail`, `NotFound` |\n| Internal | Developers | Debug in","body":"# Domain Error Strategy\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**Who needs to handle this error, and how should they recover?**\n\nBefore designing error types:\n- Is this user-facing or internal?\n- Is recovery possible?\n- What context is needed for debugging?\n\n---\n\n## Error Categorization\n\n| Error Type | Audience | Recovery | Example |\n|------------|----------|----------|---------|\n| User-facing | End users | Guide action | `InvalidEmail`, `NotFound` |\n| Internal | Developers | Debug info | `DatabaseError`, `ParseError` |\n| System | Ops/SRE | Monitor/alert | `ConnectionTimeout`, `RateLimited` |\n| Transient | Automation | Retry | `NetworkError`, `ServiceUnavailable` |\n| Permanent | Human | Investigate | `ConfigInvalid`, `DataCorrupted` |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore designing error types:\n\n1. **Who sees this error?**\n   - End user → friendly message, actionable\n   - Developer → detailed, debuggable\n   - Ops → structured, alertable\n\n2. **Can we recover?**\n   - Transient → retry with backoff\n   - Degradable → fallback value\n   - Permanent → fail fast, alert\n\n3. **What context is needed?**\n   - Call chain → anyhow::Context\n   - Request ID → structured logging\n   - Input data → error payload\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nTo domain constraints (Layer 3):\n\n```\n\"How should I handle payment failures?\"\n    ↑ Ask: What are the business rules for retries?\n    ↑ Check: domain-web or project requirements\n    ↑ Check: SLA (availability requirements)\n```\n\n| Question | Trace To | Ask |\n|----------|----------|-----|\n| Retry policy | domain-web | What''s acceptable latency for retry? |\n| User experience | domain-web | What message should users see? |\n| Compliance | Project requirements | What must be logged for audit? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nTo implementation (Layer 1):\n\n```\n\"Need typed errors\"\n    ↓ m06-error-handling: thiserror for library\n    ↓ m04-zero-cost: Error enum design\n\n\"Need error context\"\n    ↓ m06-error-handling: anyhow::Context\n    ↓ Logging: tracing with fields\n\n\"Need retry logic\"\n    ↓ m07-concurrency: async retry patterns\n    ↓ Crates: tokio-retry, backoff\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Recovery Pattern | When | Implementation |\n|------------------|------|----------------|\n| Retry | Transient failures | exponential backoff |\n| Fallback | Degraded mode | cached/default value |\n| Circuit Breaker | Cascading failures | failsafe-rs |\n| Timeout | Slow operations | `tokio::time::timeout` |\n| Bulkhead | Isolation | separate thread pools |\n\n## Error Hierarchy\n\n```rust\n#[derive(thiserror::Error, Debug)]\npub enum AppError {\n    // User-facing\n    #[error(\"Invalid input: {0}\")]\n    Validation(String),\n\n    // Transient (retryable)\n    #[error(\"Service temporarily unavailable\")]\n    ServiceUnavailable(#[source] reqwest::Error),\n\n    // Internal (log details, show generic)\n    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n    Internal(#[source] anyhow::Error),\n}\n\nimpl AppError {\n    pub fn is_retryable(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::ServiceUnavailable(_))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Retry Pattern\n\n```rust\nuse tokio_retry::{Retry, strategy::ExponentialBackoff};\n\nasync fn with_retry<F, Fut, T, E>(f: F) -> Result<T, E>\nwhere\n    F: Fn() -> Fut,\n    Fut: Future<Output = Result<T, E>>,\n    E: std::fmt::Debug,\n{\n    let strategy = ExponentialBackoff::from_millis(100)\n        .max_delay(Duration::from_secs(10))\n        .take(5);\n\n    Retry::spawn(strategy, || f()).await\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Why Wrong | Better |\n|---------|-----------|--------|\n| Same error for all | No actionability | Categorize by audience |\n| Retry everything | Wasted resources | Only transient errors |\n| Infinite retry | DoS self | Max attempts + backoff |\n| Expose internal errors | Security risk | User-friendly messages |\n| No context | Hard to debug | .context() everywhere |\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Why Bad | Better |\n|--------------|---------|--------|\n| String errors | No structure | thiserror types |\n| panic! for recoverable | Bad UX | Result with context |\n| Ignore errors | Silent failures | Log or propagate |\n| Box<dyn Error> everywhere | Lost type info | thiserror |\n| Error in happy path | Performance | Early validation |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Error handling basics | m06-error-handling |\n| Retry implementation | m07-concurrency |\n| Domain modeling | m09-domain |\n| User-facing APIs | domain-web |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:30:06.237Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Rust-based AI Agents requiring robust error handling and domain-specific error strategies, particularly those leveraging the Durable Streams protocol with axum and tokio.","zh":"适用于需要强大错误处理和特定领域错误策略的基于Rust的AI代理，特别是那些利用Durable Streams协议与axum和tokio的代理。","ja":"RustベースのAIエージェントに適しており、ロバストなエラーハンドリングとドメイン固有のエラーストラテジーを必要とするもの、特にDurable Streamsプロトコルとaxumおよびtokioを利用するもの。","ko":"로스트 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 강력한 오류 처리 및 도메인별 오류 전략이 필요한 경우 특히 Durable Streams 프로토콜과 axum 및 tokio를 사용하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial basados en Rust que requieren un manejo de errores robusto y estrategias de errores específicas del dominio, particularmente aquellos que aprovechan el protocolo Durable Streams con axum y tokio.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle basés sur Rust nécessitant une gestion d''erreurs robuste et des stratégies d''erreurs spécifiques au domaine, en particulier ceux qui utilisent le protocole Durable Streams avec axum et tokio.","de":"Ideal für auf Rust basierende KI-Agents, die eine robuste Fehlerbehandlung und domänenspezifische Fehlerstrategien erfordern, insbesondere solche, die das Durable Streams-Protokoll mit axum und tokio nutzen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA baseados em Rust que exigem tratamento de erros robusto e estratégias de erros específicas do domínio, particularmente aqueles que utilizam o protocolo Durable Streams com axum e tokio.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ на основе Rust, требующих надежной обработки ошибок и доменных стратегий ошибок, особенно тех, которые используют протокол Durable Streams с axum и tokio.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إدارة الوكيل الذكي المبنية على Rust التي تتطلب معالجة الخطأ القوي واستراتيجيات الخطأ الخاصة بالنطاق، ولا سيما تلك التي تستخدم بروتوكول Durable Streams مع axum و tokio."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to categorize and handle domain errors effectively, supporting both user-facing and internal errors with features like streaming reads, producer idempotency, and JSON batch mode, utilizing protocols such as long-poll and SSE.","zh":"赋予代理有效地对域错误进行分类和处理的能力，支持用户面向和内部错误，并具有诸如流读取、生产者等幂性和JSON批处理模式等功能，利用长轮询和SSE等协议。","ja":"エージェントにドメインエラーを効果的に分類および処理する能力を付与し、ユーザー向けおよび内部エラーをサポートし、ストリーミング読み取り、プロデューサー等幂性、JSONバッチモードなどの機能を提供し、ロングポーリングやSSEなどのプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 도메인 오류를 효과적으로 분류하고 처리할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며 사용자 및 내부 오류를 지원하고 스트리밍 읽기, 생산자 등幂성, JSON 배치 모드 등의 기능을 제공하며 롱 폴링 및 SSE 등의 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes categorizar y manejar errores de dominio de manera efectiva, admitiendo errores tanto para usuarios como internos con características como lecturas de transmisión, idempotencia del productor y modo de lote JSON, utilizando protocolos como long-poll y SSE.","fr":"Permet aux agents de catégoriser et de gérer les erreurs de domaine de manière efficace, en prenant en charge à la fois les erreurs orientées utilisateur et internes avec des fonctionnalités telles que les lectures de diffusion, l''idempotence du producteur et le mode de lot JSON, en utilisant des protocoles tels que long-poll et SSE.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Domänenfehler effektiv zu kategorisieren und zu handhaben, indem sowohl benutzerseitige als auch interne Fehler mit Funktionen wie Streaming-Lesevorgängen, Hersteller-Idempotenz und JSON-Batch-Modus unterstützt werden, unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie long-poll und SSE.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a categorizar e lidar com erros de domínio de forma eficaz, suportando erros tanto para o usuário quanto internos com recursos como leituras de streaming, idempotência do produtor e modo de lote JSON, utilizando protocolos como long-poll e SSE.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью классифицировать и обрабатывать доменные ошибки эффективно, поддерживая как пользовательские, так и внутренние ошибки с функциями, такими как потоковые чтения, идемпотентность производителя и режим пакетной обработки JSON, используя протоколы, такие как long-poll и SSE.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تصنيف ومعالجة أخطاء النطاق بفعالية، مع دعم أخطاء مواجهة المستخدم وأخطاء داخلية باستخدام ميزات مثل قراءات التدفق، ومثابرة المنتج، ووضع المجموعة JSON، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل long-poll و SSE."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing error types for Rust applications with axum and tokio","Implementing domain error strategies for user-facing and internal errors","Debugging errors with context needed for effective recovery and troubleshooting"],"zh":["为使用axum和tokio的Rust应用程序设计错误类型","为用户面向和内部错误实现域错误策略","需要上下文以进行有效恢复和故障排除的错误调试"],"ja":["axumとtokioを使用するRustアプリケーション用のエラータイプを設計する","ユーザー向けおよび内部エラー用のドメインエラーストラテジーを実装する","有効な復旧とトラブルシューティングに必要なコンテキストを持つエラーデバッグ"],"ko":["axum과 tokio를 사용하는 로스트 애플리케이션에 대한 오류 유형 설계","사용자 및 내부 오류에 대한 도메인 오류 전략 구현","유효한 복구 및 문제 해결을 위한 오류 디버깅과 필요한 컨텍스트"],"es":["Diseñar tipos de errores para aplicaciones Rust con axum y tokio","Implementar estrategias de errores de dominio para errores orientados al usuario y errores internos","Depurar errores con contexto necesario para una recuperación y depuración efectivas"],"fr":["Concevoir des types d''erreurs pour les applications Rust avec axum et tokio","Mettre en œuvre des stratégies d''erreurs de domaine pour les erreurs orientées utilisateur et les erreurs internes","Déboguer les erreurs avec un contexte nécessaire pour une récupération et une débogage efficaces"],"de":["Entwerfen von Fehlertypen für Rust-Anwendungen mit axum und tokio","Implementierung von Domänenfehlerstrategien für benutzerseitige und interne Fehler","Fehlerbehebung mit notwendigem Kontext für eine effektive Wiederherstellung und Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Projetar tipos de erros para aplicações Rust com axum e tokio","Implementar estratégias de erros de domínio para erros de usuário e internos","Depurar erros com contexto necessário para recuperação e depuração eficazes"],"ru":["Проектировать типы ошибок для приложений Rust с axum и tokio","Реализовывать доменные стратегии ошибок для пользовательских и внутренних ошибок","Отлаживать ошибки с контекстом, необходимым для эффективного восстановления и устранения неполадок"],"ar":["تصميم أنواع أخطاء للتطبيقات المبنية على Rust مع axum و tokio","تنفيذ استراتيجيات أخطاء النطاق لأخطاء مواجهة المستخدم وأخطاء داخلية","تصحيح أخطاء بالسياق الضروري لاستعادة فعالة ومعالجة الأخطاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Rust programming language","Specific to applications using the Durable Streams protocol","Error handling strategy may need adaptation for non-Rust environments"],"zh":["需要了解Rust编程语言","特定于使用Durable Streams协议的应用程序","错误处理策略可能需要适应非Rust环境"],"ja":["Rustプログラミング言語の理解が必要","Durable Streamsプロトコルを使用するアプリケーションに特有","エラーハンドリングストラテジーは非Rust環境に対して適応する必要があるかもしれない"],"ko":["로스트 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 이해가 필요","Durable Streams 프로토콜을 사용하는 애플리케이션에 특정","오류 처리 전략은 비로스트 환경에 맞게 적응할 필요가 있을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del lenguaje de programación Rust","Específico para aplicaciones que utilizan el protocolo Durable Streams","La estrategia de manejo de errores puede necesitar adaptación para entornos no Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du langage de programmation Rust","Spécifique aux applications utilisant le protocole Durable Streams","La stratégie de gestion des erreurs peut nécessiter une adaptation pour les environnements non Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis der Rust-Programmiersprache","Spezifisch für Anwendungen, die das Durable Streams-Protokoll verwenden","Die Fehlerbehandlungsstrategie kann eine Anpassung für nicht-Rust-Umgebungen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento da linguagem de programação Rust","Específico para aplicações que utilizam o protocolo Durable Streams","A estratégia de tratamento de erros pode precisar de adaptação para ambientes não-Rust"],"ru":["Требует понимания языка программирования Rust","Конкретно для приложений, использующих протокол Durable Streams","Стратегия обработки ошибок может потребовать адаптации для сред, не основанных на Rust"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بلغة برمجة Rust","محدد للتطبيقات التي تستخدم بروتوكول Durable Streams","يمكن أن تتطلب استراتيجية معالجة الأخطاء للتكيف مع البيئات غير مبنية على Rust"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"5e87ba8162af9e34e6a6afe6f50e7e708bc5363216f7d691870d25965cafa1d3","qualityScore":42}');
