d с помощью Go Tapd SDK","Реализация API для ИИ Агентов","Разработка приложений на Go","Интеграция с другими инструментами разработки","Повышение производительности за счет автоматизации задач"],"ar":["وصول إلى واجهة برمجة التطبيقات Tapd باستخدام SDK Go Tapd","تنفيذ واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لأدوات ذكاء اصطناعي","تطوير التطبيقات بلغة Go","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير أخرى","تحسين الإنتاجية من خلال تلقيم المهام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Go Tapd SDK","Tapd API","Go开发语言","API访问","开发效率","如何使用Go Tapd SDK","Go Tapd SDK安装","Go Tapd SDK设置指南"],"ja":["Go Tapd SDK","Tapd API","Go開発言語","APIアクセス","開発効率","Go Tapd SDKの使い方","Go Tapd SDKのインストール","Go Tapd SDKの設定ガイド"],"ko":["Go Tapd SDK","Tapd API","Go 개발 언어","API 접근","개발 효율성","Go Tapd SDK 사용법","Go Tapd SDK 설치","Go Tapd SDK 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo implementar api","herramientas de ai para desarrolladores","go tapd sdk","tapd api","integración de api con go","alternativas a go tapd sdk","guía de instalación de go tapd sdk"],"fr":["comment mettre en œuvre l''api","outils d''ia pour les développeurs","go tapd sdk","tapd api","intégration de l''api avec go","alternatives à go tapd sdk","guide d''installation de go tapd sdk"],"de":["wie implementiere ich api","ki-tools für entwickler","go tapd sdk","tapd api","integration von api mit go","alternativen zu go tapd sdk","anleitung zur installation von go tapd sdk"],"pt":["como implementar api","o que é api","ferramentas de ia agente","go tapd sdk","desenvolvimento de aplicações com go","integração com outras ferramentas de desenvolvimento","melhoria da produtividade com automação de tarefas","guias de instalação do go tapd sdk"],"ru":["как реализовать api","что такое api","ии агенты","go tapd sdk","разработка приложений на go","интеграция с другими инструментами разработки","повышение производительности за счет автоматизации задач","руководства по установке go tapd sdk"],"ar":["كيفية تنفيذ واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","ما هي واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي","sdk go tapd","تطوير التطبيقات بلغة go","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير أخرى","تحسين الإنتاجية من خلال تلقيم المهام","دليل تثبيت sdk go tapd"]}},"owner":"go-tapd","repo":"tapd","repoPath":"go-tapd/tapd","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.953Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"implement-api","description":"Implement a new TAPD API endpoint in the go-tapd SDK when a user provides an API documentation URL or asks to add/implement an endpoint (Story/Bug/Task/Iteration/etc.), including request/response structs, service methods, tests, test data, and features.md updates.","bodyPreview":"# Implement API\n\n## Overview\nImplement a TAPD API endpoint in this repo using the standard workflow and conventions.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Collect inputs: API doc URL, service type, brief description.\n2. Read project guidance: `guide.md`; use `references/implement-api.md` as a checklist.\n3. Fetch the API doc content when a URL is provided; extract required params/response fields.\n4. Locate a similar implementation in `api_*.go` and `api_*_test.go`; mirror patterns and naming.\n5. Implement code:\n   - R","body":"# Implement API\n\n## Overview\nImplement a TAPD API endpoint in this repo using the standard workflow and conventions.\n\n## Workflow\n1. Collect inputs: API doc URL, service type, brief description.\n2. Read project guidance: `guide.md`; use `references/implement-api.md` as a checklist.\n3. Fetch the API doc content when a URL is provided; extract required params/response fields.\n4. Locate a similar implementation in `api_*.go` and `api_*_test.go`; mirror patterns and naming.\n5. Implement code:\n   - Request struct: pointer fields, `url` tags, Chinese comments.\n   - Response struct: value fields with nullable pointers, `json` tags, Chinese comments.\n   - Service interface method and implementation with API doc link in the comment.\n6. Add tests:\n   - Test data in `internal/testdata/api/{resource}/{endpoint}.json`.\n   - Unit test in `api_*_test.go` validating method/path/params and key fields.\n   - Integration test in `tests/api_*_prod_test.go` (single-test run only).\n7. Update docs: mark the endpoint in `features.md`.\n8. Run tests and report results.\n\n## Conventions and checks\n- Follow `guide.md` exactly for naming, request/response types, and patterns.\n- Preserve existing response wrappers and helpers; do not invent new ones.\n- Always include the API documentation link in the method comment.\n- Keep comments in Chinese for exported fields.\n- Do not run integration tests in batch.\n\n## Output expectations\n- Provide a short summary of the API implemented.\n- List modified files with line numbers.\n- Provide test commands executed and their results.\n- Provide a usage snippet for the new method.\n- Call out any assumptions or missing API details.\n\n## Resources\n- `references/implement-api.md`: Checklist and repo entry points.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:44:38.767Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for API-focused Agents needing streamlined TAPD API endpoint implementation using the Go Tapd SDK","zh":"适用于需要简化 TAPD API 端点实现的 API-focused Agents，使用 Go Tapd SDK","ja":"API-focused Agents に向けて、TAPD API 端点の実装を簡化するために、Go Tapd SDK を使用する","ko":"API-focused Agents 에서 TAPD API 端점을 구현할 때 Go Tapd SDK 를 사용하여 TAPD API 端점을 구현하는 것을 간소화하는 데 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes centrados en API que necesitan una implementación de puntos de conexión de API de TAPD optimizada usando el SDK de Go Tapd","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents axés sur l''API nécessitant une mise en œuvre de points de terminaison d''API TAPD rationalisée à l''aide du SDK Go Tapd","de":"Perfekt für API-fokussierte Agenten, die eine optimierte Implementierung von TAPD-API-Endpunkten unter Verwendung des Go-Tapd-SDK benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em API que necessitam de implementação de endpoint de API TAPD simplificada usando o SDK Go Tapd","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на API, которым требуется упрощенная реализация конечных точек API TAPD с использованием SDK Go Tapd","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يركزون على واجهة برمجة التطبيقات (API) والذين يحتاجون إلى تنفيذ نقطة نهاية واجهة برمجة التطبيقات TAPD المُبسّطة باستخدام SDK Go Tapd"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement TAPD API endpoints using standard workflow and conventions, leveraging the Go client library for accessing the Tapd API, and utilizing API documentation to extract required parameters and response fields","zh":"通过标准工作流和惯例、利用 Go 客户端库来访问 Tapd API、并且通过 API 文档来提取所需参数和响应字段来实现 TAPD API 端点","ja":"標準的なワークフローと規約を通じて、Go クライントライブラリを利用して Tapd API にアクセスし、API 文書を通じて必要なパラメータとレスポンスフィールドを抽出し、TAPD API 端点を実現する","ko":"표준적인 워크플로우와 규약을 통해 Go 클라이언트 라이ブラ리를 사용하여 Tapd API 에 접근하고, API 문서를 통해 필요한 파라미터와 응답 필드를 추출하여 TAPD API 端점을 구현할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar puntos de conexión de API de TAPD utilizando un flujo de trabajo estándar y convenciones, aprovechando la biblioteca de cliente de Go para acceder a la API de Tapd y utilizando la documentación de la API para extraer parámetros y campos de respuesta requeridos","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des points de terminaison d''API TAPD en utilisant un workflow standard et des conventions, en exploitant la bibliothèque cliente Go pour accéder à l''API Tapd et en utilisant la documentation de l''API pour extraire les paramètres et les champs de réponse requis","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, TAPD-API-Endpunkte unter Verwendung eines Standard-Workflows und -Konventionen zu implementieren, indem sie die Go-Client-Bibliothek zur Zugriff auf die Tapd-API nutzen und die API-Dokumentation verwenden, um erforderliche Parameter und Antwortfelder zu extrahieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar endpoints de API TAPD usando fluxo de trabalho padrão e convenções, aproveitando a biblioteca de cliente Go para acessar a API Tapd e utilizando a documentação da API para extrair parâmetros e campos de resposta necessários","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать конечные точки API TAPD, используя стандартный рабочий процесс и соглашения, а также использует клиентскую библиотеку Go для доступа к API Tapd и использует документацию API для извлечения необходимых параметров и полей ответа","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ نقاط النهاية لواجهة برمجة التطبيقات TAPD باستخدام تدفق عمل قياسي والاتفاقيات، مستفيدة من مكتبة العميل Go للوصول إلى واجهة برمجة التطبيقات Tapd واستخدام توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لاستخراج المعلمات وحقول الاستجابة المطلوبة"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing new TAPD API endpoints","Mirroring existing API patterns for consistency","Automating API documentation fetching and parameter extraction"],"zh":["实现新的 TAPD API 端点","镜像现有的 API 模式以保持一致性","自动化 API 文档获取和参数提取"],"ja":["新しい TAPD API 端点を実現する","既存の API パターンを鏡像して一貫性を維持する","API 文書の取得とパラメータの抽出を自動化する"],"ko":["새로운 TAPD API 端점을 구현하는 것","既存의 API 패턴을鏡像하여 일관성을 유지하는 것","API 문서의 가져오기와 파라미터의 추출을 자동화하는 것"],"es":["Implementación de nuevos puntos de conexión de API de TAPD","Reflejo de patrones de API existentes para la coherencia","Automatización de la recuperación y extracción de parámetros de la documentación de la API"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de nouveaux points de terminaison d''API TAPD","Miroir de modèles d''API existants pour la cohérence","Automatisation de la récupération et de l''extraction de paramètres de la documentation de l''API"],"de":["Implementierung neuer TAPD-API-Endpunkte","Spiegelung bestehender API-Muster für Konsistenz","Automatisierung des Abrufs und der Extraktion von API-Dokumentationsparametern"],"pt":["Implementar novos endpoints de API TAPD","Espelhar padrões de API existentes para consistência","Automatizar a obtenção da documentação da API e extração de parâmetros"],"ru":["Реализация новых конечных точек API TAPD","Отражение существующих шаблонов API для согласованности","Автоматизация извлечения документации API и извлечения параметров"],"ar":["تنفيذ نقاط نهاية جديدة لواجهة برمجة التطبيقات TAPD","تعزيز أنماط واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الحالية لتحقيق الاتساق","توفير آلي لاستخراج توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات واستخراج المعلمات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Go Tapd SDK installation","Needs API documentation URL for implementation","Limited to TAPD API endpoints"],"zh":["需要 Go Tapd SDK 安装","需要 API 文档 URL 才能实现","仅限于 TAPD API 端点"],"ja":["Go Tapd SDK のインストールが必要","実現するには API 文書 URL が必要","TAPD API 端点のみに限られている"],"ko":["Go Tapd SDK 의 설치가 필요합니다.","구현하기 위해 API 문서 URL 이 필요합니다.","TAPD API 端점만으로 제한됩니다."],"es":["Requiere la instalación del SDK de Go Tapd","Necesita la URL de la documentación de la API para la implementación","Limitado a los puntos de conexión de la API de TAPD"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation du SDK Go Tapd","A besoin de l''URL de la documentation de l''API pour la mise en œuvre","Limité aux points de terminaison de l''API TAPD"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation des Go-Tapd-SDK","Benötigt die API-Dokumentations-URL für die Implementierung","Begrenzt auf TAPD-API-Endpunkte"],"pt":["Requer instalação do SDK Go Tapd","Necessita de URL de documentação da API para implementação","Limitado a endpoints de API TAPD"],"ru":["Требует установки SDK Go Tapd","Требует URL-адреса документации API для реализации","Ограничен конечными точками API TAPD"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت SDK Go Tapd","يحتاج إلى عنوان URL لتوثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات لتنفيذها","محدود بنقاط النهاية لواجهة برمجة التطبيقات TAPD"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"71a5e7d1a102dfb88666e27799f5651152665714c2224e5e61c529d992b55a76","qualityScore":42}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jaxxstorm/sentinel/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'jaxxstorm', 'sentinel', 'jaxxstorm/sentinel', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 42, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.967Z', '2026-03-02T02:52:55.587Z', 'f764e94014ec70ccd261ab580debbaa6ce74eff2877bffc80734e64fb70bb397', '{"id":"jaxxstorm/sentinel/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"openspec-onboard AI智能代理监控您的Tailnet，实时通知网络变化","ja":"openspec-onboard AIエージェントはTailnetを監視し、変更を通知","ko":"openspec-onboard AI 에이전트는 Tailnet을 모니터링하고 변경 사항을 알림","es":"openspec-onboard es una herramienta de AI que monitorea tu tailnet y te notifica de cambios. Ideal para desarrolladores que buscan una solución para vigilar su red","fr":"openspec-onboard est un outil d''IA qui surveille votre tailnet et vous notify de modifications. Idéal pour les développeurs qui recherchent une solution pour surveiller leur réseau","de":"openspec-onboard ist ein KI-Tool, das Ihr Tailnet überwacht und Sie über Änderungen benachrichtigt. Ideal für Entwickler, die nach einer Lösung suchen, um ihr Netzwerk zu überwachen","pt":"O openspec-onboard é uma ferramenta de IA que monitora e notifica alterações no seu tailnet, garantindo a segurança e integridade da sua rede.","ru":"ИИ Агент openspec-onboard наблюдает и уведомляет о изменениях в вашем tailnet, обеспечивая безопасность и целостность вашей сети.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي openspec-onboard تراقب وتحديث التغييرات في شبكتك، مما يضمن أمانها وسلامة البيانات","en":"Watch over your tailnet and notify of changes"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理openspec-onboard：Tailnet监控","ja":"AIエージェントopenspec-onboard：Tailnetの監視","ko":"AI 에이전트 openspec-onboard: Tailnet 모니터링","es":"Herramientas de AI: openspec-onboard para monitorear tailnet","fr":"Outils d''IA : openspec-onboard pour surveiller tailnet","de":"KI-Tools: openspec-onboard für Tailnet-Überwachung","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: openspec-onboard para Monitoramento de...","ru":"ИИ Агенты: openspec-onboard для наблюдения за Tailnet","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: openspec-onboard لمراقبة Tailnet","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-onboard AI智能代理监控您的Tailnet，实时通知网络变化","ja":"openspec-onboard AIエージェントはTailnetを監視し、変更を通知","ko":"openspec-onboard AI 에이전트는 Tailnet을 모니터링하고 변경 사항을 알림","es":"openspec-onboard es una herramienta de AI que monitorea tu tailnet y te notifica de cambios. Ideal para desarrolladores que buscan una solución para vigilar ...","fr":"openspec-onboard est un outil d''IA qui surveille votre tailnet et vous notify de modifications. Idéal pour les développeurs qui recherchent une solution pour...","de":"openspec-onboard ist ein KI-Tool, das Ihr Tailnet überwacht und Sie über Änderungen benachrichtigt. Ideal für Entwickler, die nach einer Lösung suchen, um ih...","pt":"O openspec-onboard é uma ferramenta de IA que monitora e notifica alterações no seu tailnet, garantindo a segurança e integridade da sua rede.","ru":"ИИ Агент openspec-onboard наблюдает и уведомляет о изменениях в вашем tailnet, обеспечивая безопасность и целостность вашей сети.","ar":"أداة الذكاء الاصطناعي openspec-onboard تراقب وتحديث التغييرات في شبكتك، مما يضمن أمانها وسلامة البيانات","en":"Watch over your tailnet and notify of changes"},"definition":{"en":"Watch over your tailnet and notify of changes"},"features":{"zh":["Tailnet监控","实时通知","网络变化检测","AI智能代理技术","简单易用"],"ja":["Tailnetの監視","リアルタイム通知","ネットワーク変更の検出","AIエージェント技術","シンプルで使いやすい"],"ko":["Tailnet 모니터링","실시간 알림","네트워크 변경 감지","AI 에이전트 기술","간단하고 사용하기 쉬운"],"es":["Monitoreo de tailnet en tiempo real","Notificaciones de cambios y actualizaciones","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo","Seguridad y privacidad garantizadas","Fácil instalación y configuración"],"fr":["Surveillance du tailnet en temps réel","Notifications de modifications et de mises à jour","Intégration avec des outils de développement","Sécurité et confidentialité garanties","Installation et configuration faciles"],"de":["Echtzeit-Überwachung von Tailnet","Benachrichtigungen über Änderungen und Updates","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Sicherheit und Datenschutz garantiert","Einfache Installation und Konfiguration"],"pt":["Monitoramento de tailnet em tempo real","Notificação de alterações e atualizações","Integração com ferramentas de segurança","Análise de dados e relatórios","Suporte a múltiplas plataformas"],"ru":["Мониторинг tailnet в режиме реального времени","Уведомление об изменениях и обновлениях","Интеграция с инструментами безопасности","Анализ данных и отчеты","Поддержка нескольких платформ"],"ar":["مراقبة شبكة التAILNET في الوقت الفعلي","إخطار بالتغيرات والتحديثات","التكامل مع أدوات الأمان","تحليل البيانات والتقرير","دعم منصات متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Tailnet监控","openspec-onboard教程","AI工具","网络安全","实时通知","openspec-onboard安装","AI智能代理比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Tailnetの監視","openspec-onboardの使い方","AIツール","ネットワークセキュリティ","リアルタイム通知","openspec-onboardの設定","AIエージェントの比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Tailnet 모니터링","openspec-onboard 사용법","AI 도구","네트워크 보안","실시간 알림","openspec-onboard 설치","AI 에이전트 비교"],"es":["herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","monitoreo de tailnet","notificaciones de cambios","integración con herramientas de desarrollo","seguridad y privacidad en la nube","cómo utilizar openspec-onboard","alternativas a openspec-onboard","openspec-onboard vs competidores"],"fr":["outils d''IA pour développeurs","surveillance du tailnet","notifications de modifications","intégration avec des outils de développement","sécurité et confidentialité dans le cloud","comment utiliser openspec-onboard","alternatives à openspec-onboard","openspec-onboard vs concurrents"],"de":["KI-Tools für Entwickler","Überwachung von Tailnet","Benachrichtigungen über Änderungen","Integration mit Entwicklungstools","Sicherheit und Datenschutz in der Cloud","wie man openspec-onboard verwendet","Alternativen zu openspec-onboard","openspec-onboard vs Wettbewerber"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","monitoramento de tailnet","segurança de rede","integração com ferramentas de segurança","como usar openspec-onboard","alternativas para openspec-onboard","instalação do openspec-onboard","guia de configuração do openspec-onboard"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","наблюдение за tailnet","безопасность сети","интеграция с инструментами безопасности","как использовать openspec-onboard","альтернативы для openspec-onboard","установка openspec-onboard","руководство по настройке openspec-onboard"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","مراقبة شبكة التAILNET","أمان الشبكة","التكامل مع أدوات الأمان","كيفية استخدام openspec-onboard","بديل لopenspec-onboard","تثبيت openspec-onboard","دليل إعداد openspec-onboard"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"sentinel","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/sentinel","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.967Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:52:55.587Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration and codebase analysis.","zh":"适合需要指导的OpenSpec工作流集成和代码库分析的开发代理。","ja":"OpenSpecワークフローの統合とコードベースの分析を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"OpenSpec 워크플로 통합 및 코드베이스 분석이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una integración de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec guiada y análisis de código base.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de workflow OpenSpec guidée et d''analyse de base de code.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine guidierte OpenSpec-Workflow-Integration und Codebase-Analyse benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada e análise de código","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима интеграция рабочего процесса OpenSpec с руководством и анализ кодовой базы","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الناشئين الذين يحتاجون إلى إرشادات لتكامل تدفق العمل المفتوح والتحليل القاعدي للкод"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate and teach users through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle, utilizing JSON output and bash commands like `openspec status` and `openspec init`, while explaining each step in real-time within the user''s codebase.","zh":"赋予代理导航并教导用户完成第一个完整的OpenSpec工作流周期的能力，利用JSON输出和bash命令，如`openspec status`和`openspec init`，同时在用户的代码库中实时解释每一步。","ja":"OpenSpecワークフローのサイクルを完了するための最初のステップからユーザーをナビゲートし、教えることが代理人に可能になります。JSON出力と、`openspec status`および`openspec init`などのbashコマンドを使用して、ユーザーのコードベース内でリアルタイムに各ステップを説明します。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자를 첫 번째 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 탐색하고 가르칠 수 있도록 합니다. JSON 출력과 bash 명령어를 사용하여, 예를 들어 `openspec status`와 `openspec init`를 사용하고, 사용자의 코드베이스 내에서 실시간으로 각 단계를 설명합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar y enseñar a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec completo, utilizando la salida JSON y comandos bash como `openspec status` y `openspec init`, mientras explica cada paso en tiempo real dentro de la base de código del usuario.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer et d''enseigner aux utilisateurs à travers leur premier cycle de workflow OpenSpec complet, en utilisant la sortie JSON et les commandes bash comme `openspec status` et `openspec init`, tout en expliquant chaque étape en temps réel à l''intérieur de la base de code de l''utilisateur.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Mitteln, die Benutzer durch ihren ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus zu navigieren und zu unterrichten, indem JSON-Ausgabe und Bash-Befehle wie `openspec status` und `openspec init` verwendet werden, während jede Schritt in Echtzeit innerhalb der Codebase des Benutzers erklärt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar e ensinar os usuários ao longo de seu primeiro ciclo de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec completo, utilizando saída JSON e comandos bash como `openspec status` e `openspec init`, ao mesmo tempo explicando cada etapa em tempo real dentro da base de código do usuário","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью ориентироваться и обучать пользователей на протяжении их первого полного цикла рабочего процесса OpenSpec, используя выходные данные JSON и команды bash, такие как `openspec status` и `openspec init`, а также объясняя каждую ступень в режиме реального времени внутри кодовой базы пользователя","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من الملاحة وتعليم المستخدمين خلال دورة کاملة من تدفق العمل المفتوح، باستخدام الإخراج JSON وأوامر bash مثل `openspec status` و `openspec init`، في نفس الوقت يقومون بتوضيح كل خطوة في الوقت الفعلي داخل قاعدة الشفرة للمستخدم"},"useCases":{"en":["Guiding users through OpenSpec initialization","Analyzing and notifying of changes in the tailnet","Walking users through a complete OpenSpec workflow cycle"],"zh":["引导用户完成OpenSpec初始化","分析并通知tailnet中的更改","引导用户完成完整的OpenSpec工作流周期"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化をユーザーに導く","tailnet内の変更を分析して通知する","OpenSpecワークフローのサイクルを完了するためのユーザーを導く"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화를 사용자에게 안내하기","tailnet의 변경 사항을 분석하고 알리기","사용자를 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클로 안내하기"],"es":["Guiar a los usuarios a través de la inicialización de OpenSpec","Analizar y notificar los cambios en la tailnet","Llevar a los usuarios a través de un ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec completo"],"fr":["Guider les utilisateurs à travers l''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Analyser et notifier les changements dans la tailnet","Conduire les utilisateurs à travers un cycle de workflow OpenSpec complet"],"de":["Benutzer durch die Initialisierung von OpenSpec führen","Änderungen in der Tailnet analysieren und benachrichtigen","Benutzer durch einen vollständigen OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus führen"],"pt":["Orientar os usuários pela inicialização do OpenSpec","Analisar e notificar sobre alterações na tailnet","Levar os usuários por um ciclo completo de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec"],"ru":["Руководство пользователями при инициализации OpenSpec","Анализ и уведомление об изменениях в tailnet","Проведение пользователей через полный цикл рабочего процесса OpenSpec"],"ar":["إرشاد المستخدمين خلال عملية إعداد المفتوح","تحليل والإشعار عن التغييرات في الشبكة الخلفية","مرافقة المستخدمين خلال دورة کاملة من تدفق العمل المفتوح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec to be initialized in the project","Must have bash access for command execution"],"zh":["需要在项目中初始化OpenSpec","必须具有bash访问权限以执行命令"],"ja":["プロジェクト内でOpenSpecを初期化する必要がある","コマンドの実行にはbashへのアクセスが必要"],"ko":["프로젝트에서 OpenSpec를 초기화해야 함","명령어를 실행하기 위해서는 bash 접근 권한이 필요함"],"es":["Requiere que OpenSpec esté inicializado en el proyecto","Debe tener acceso bash para la ejecución de comandos"],"fr":["Nécessite que OpenSpec soit initialisé dans le projet","Doit avoir un accès bash pour l''exécution de commandes"],"de":["Benötigt, dass OpenSpec im Projekt initialisiert ist","Muss Bash-Zugriff für Befehlsausführung haben"],"pt":["Exige que o OpenSpec seja inicializado no projeto","Deve ter acesso bash para execução de comandos"],"ru":["Требует инициализации OpenSpec в проекте","Должно иметь доступ к bash для выполнения команд"],"ar":["يتطلب تشغيل المفتوح في المشروع","يجب أن يكون لديه حق الوصول إلى bash لتنفيذ الأوامر"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"f764e94014ec70ccd261ab580debbaa6ce74eff2877bffc80734e64fb70bb397","qualityScore":42}');
