s webpack","commit-workのインストール","commit-workの設定ガイド","シングルページアプリケーション開発ツール","AIエージェント","commit-workのチュートリアル"],"ko":["commit-work 사용법","싱글페이지 애플리케이션 개발이란","commit-work 대안","commit-work vs webpack","commit-work 설치","commit-work 설정 가이드","싱글페이지 애플리케이션 개발 도구","AI 에이전트","commit-work 튜토리얼"],"es":["cómo usar commit-work","qué es commit-work","commit-work alternativa","commit-work vs create-react-app","instalación de commit-work","guía de configuración de commit-work","desarrollo de SPA con commit-work","herramientas de desarrollo para SPA"],"fr":["comment utiliser commit-work","qu''est-ce que commit-work","alternative à commit-work","commit-work vs create-react-app","installation de commit-work","guide de configuration de commit-work","développement de SPA avec commit-work","outils de développement pour les SPA"],"de":["wie man commit-work verwendet","was ist commit-work","alternative zu commit-work","commit-work vs create-react-app","installation von commit-work","anleitung zur konfiguration von commit-work","entwicklung von single-page-anwendungen mit commit-work","entwicklungstools für single-page-anwendungen"],"pt":["como usar Commit Work","o que é Commit Work","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","Commit Work vs outras ferramentas","instalar Commit Work","guia de configuração do Commit Work","desenvolvimento de SPA","ferramentas de desenvolvimento para React","Node.js para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать Commit Work","что такое Commit Work","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","Commit Work vs другие инструменты","установить Commit Work","руководство по настройке Commit Work","разработка одностраничных приложений","инструменты разработки для React","Node.js для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Commit Work","ما هو Commit Work","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمطوري","Commit Work مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت Commit Work","دليل إعداد Commit Work","تطوير تطبيقات صفحة واحدة","أدوات تطوير ل React","Node.js لمطوري"]}},"owner":"bartstc","repo":"vite-ts-react-template","repoPath":"bartstc/vite-ts-react-template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-28T12:47:07.712Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit-work","description":"Create high-quality git commits: review/stage intended changes, split into logical commits, and write clear commit messages (including Conventional Commits). Use when the user asks to commit, craft a commit message, stage changes, or split work into multiple commits.","bodyPreview":"# Commit work\n\n## Goal\n\nMake commits that are easy to review and safe to ship:\n\n- only intended changes are included\n- commits are logically scoped (split when needed)\n- commit messages describe what changed and why\n\n## Inputs to ask for (if missing)\n\n- Single commit or multiple commits? (If unsure: default to multiple small commits when there are unrelated changes.)\n- Commit style: Conventional Commits are required.\n- Any rules: max subject length, required scopes.\n\n## Workflow (checklist)\n\n1.","body":"# Commit work\n\n## Goal\n\nMake commits that are easy to review and safe to ship:\n\n- only intended changes are included\n- commits are logically scoped (split when needed)\n- commit messages describe what changed and why\n\n## Inputs to ask for (if missing)\n\n- Single commit or multiple commits? (If unsure: default to multiple small commits when there are unrelated changes.)\n- Commit style: Conventional Commits are required.\n- Any rules: max subject length, required scopes.\n\n## Workflow (checklist)\n\n1. Inspect the working tree before staging\n   - `git status`\n   - `git diff` (unstaged)\n   - If many changes: `git diff --stat`\n2. Decide commit boundaries (split if needed)\n   - Split by: feature vs refactor, backend vs frontend, formatting vs logic, tests vs prod code, dependency bumps vs behavior changes.\n   - If changes are mixed in one file, plan to use patch staging.\n3. Stage only what belongs in the next commit\n   - Prefer patch staging for mixed changes: `git add -p`\n   - To unstage a hunk/file: `git restore --staged -p` or `git restore --staged <path>`\n4. Review what will actually be committed\n   - `git diff --cached`\n   - Sanity checks:\n     - no secrets or tokens\n     - no accidental debug logging\n     - no unrelated formatting churn\n5. Describe the staged change in 1-2 sentences (before writing the message)\n   - \"What changed?\" + \"Why?\"\n   - If you cannot describe it cleanly, the commit is probably too big or mixed; go back to step 2.\n6. Write the commit message\n   - Use Conventional Commits (required):\n     - `type(scope): short summary`\n     - blank line\n     - body (what/why, not implementation diary)\n     - footer (BREAKING CHANGE) if needed\n   - Prefer an editor for multi-line messages: `git commit -v`\n   - Use `references/commit-message-template.md` if helpful.\n7. Run the smallest relevant verification\n   - Run the repo''s fastest meaningful check (unit tests, lint, or build) before moving on.\n8. Repeat for the next commit until the working tree is clean\n\n## Deliverable\n\nProvide:\n\n- the final commit message(s)\n- a short summary per commit (what/why)\n- the commands used to stage/review (at minimum: `git diff --cached`, plus any tests run)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T13:12:29.478Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Version Control Agents needing standardized commit message formatting and change management.","zh":"适合需要标准化提交消息格式和变更管理的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが標準化されたコミットメッセージ形式と変更管理を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"표준화된 커밋 메시지 형식 및 변경 관리가 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Control de Versiones que necesitan un formato de mensaje de confirmación estandarizado y administración de cambios.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Contrôle de Version nécessitant un formatage standardisé des messages de validation et une gestion des changements.","de":"Perfekt für Version Control Agents, die ein standardisiertes Commit-Nachrichten-Format und Änderungsmanagement benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Controle de Versão que necessitam de formatação de mensagens de commit padronizadas e gerenciamento de alterações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контроля версий, требующих стандартизированного форматирования сообщений о коммитах и управления изменениями.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى تنسيق رسائل الالتزام ومدير التغييرات الموحد"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create logically scoped commits with descriptive messages using Conventional Commits, ensuring easy review and safe deployment of changes, while following specific rules such as max subject length and required scopes.","zh":"赋予代理创建逻辑作用域的提交，并使用Conventional Commits生成描述性消息，确保更改的易审查和安全部署，同时遵循诸如最大主题长度和所需作用域等特定规则。","ja":"エージェントがConventional Commitsを使用して論理的にスコープされたコミットを作成し、記述的なメッセージを生成することを可能にし、変更の簡単なレビューと安全なデプロイを確実に行い、最大サブジェクト長や必要なスコープなどの特定のルールに従う。","ko":"에이전트가 Conventional Commits를 사용하여 논리적으로 범위가 지정된 커밋을 생성하고 설명 메시지를 생성할 수 있도록 하여 변경 사항의 쉽게 검토하고 안전한 배포를 보장하면서 최대 제목 길이 및 필요한 범위와 같은 특정 규칙을 따릅니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear confirmaciones lógicamente delimitadas con mensajes descriptivos utilizando Conventional Commits, asegurando una revisión fácil y una implementación segura de los cambios, siguiendo reglas específicas como la longitud máxima del asunto y los alcances requeridos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des validations logiquement délimitées avec des messages descriptifs en utilisant Conventional Commits, assurant ainsi une révision facile et un déploiement sécurisé des modifications, tout en suivant des règles spécifiques telles que la longueur maximale du sujet et les portées requises.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, logisch umschriebene Commits mit beschreibenden Nachrichten unter Verwendung von Conventional Commits zu erstellen, um eine einfache Überprüfung und eine sichere Bereitstellung von Änderungen zu gewährleisten, während spezifische Regeln wie die maximale Betrefflänge und erforderliche Bereiche eingehalten werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar commits com escopo lógico e mensagens descritivas usando Conventional Commits, garantindo uma revisão fácil e implantação segura de alterações, seguindo regras específicas, como comprimento máximo do assunto e escopos necessários.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать логически определенные коммиты с описательными сообщениями, используя Conventional Commits, обеспечивая легкий обзор и безопасную установку изменений, при этом следуя определенным правилам, таким как максимальная длина темы и обязательные области.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء التزامات مدروسة منطقياً مع رسائل وصفية باستخدام Conventional Commits، مما يضمن مراجعة سهلة وتنفيذ آمن للتغييرات، مع اتباع قواعد محددة مثل أقصى طول للموضوع والنطاقات المطلوبة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit message generation","Validating commit history for consistency","Splitting large changes into smaller, reviewable commits"],"zh":["自动化提交消息生成","验证提交历史的一致性","将大型更改拆分为较小、可审查的提交"],"ja":["コミットメッセージの自動生成","コミット履歴の整合性の検証","大きな変更を小さくレビュー可能なコミットに分割"],"ko":["커밋 메시지 자동 생성","커밋 기록 일관성 검증","큰 변경 사항을 작은 검토 가능한 커밋으로 분할"],"es":["Automatizar la generación de mensajes de confirmación","Validar la historia de confirmaciones para la coherencia","Dividir grandes cambios en confirmaciones más pequeñas y revisables"],"fr":["Automatiser la génération de messages de validation","Valider l''historique des validations pour la cohérence","Diviser les grands changements en validations plus petites et révisables"],"de":["Automatisieren der Erstellung von Commit-Nachrichten","Validieren der Commit-Historie für Konsistenz","Aufteilen großer Änderungen in kleinere, überprüfbare Commits"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de mensagens de commit","Validar o histórico de commit para consistência","Dividir alterações grandes em commits menores e revisáveis"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию сообщений о коммитах","Проверять историю коммитов на последовательность","Разделять большие изменения на меньшие, проверяемые коммиты"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في إنشاء رسائل الالتزام","التحقق من تاريخ الالتزام للتسلسل","تقسيم التغييرات الكبيرة إلى التزامات صغيرة قابلة لمراجعة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to Conventional Commits style","May require manual configuration for max subject length and scopes"],"zh":["需要遵循Conventional Commits样式","可能需要手动配置最大主题长度和作用域"],"ja":["Conventional Commitsスタイルに従う必要がある","最大サブジェクト長やスコープの手動設定が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["Conventional Commits 스타일을 따라야 함","최대 제목 길이 및 범위에 대한 수동 구성이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al estilo Conventional Commits","Puede requerir configuración manual para la longitud máxima del asunto y los alcances"],"fr":["Nécessite une adhésion au style Conventional Commits","Peut nécessiter une configuration manuelle pour la longueur maximale du sujet et les portées"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Conventional Commits-Stils","Kann manuelle Konfiguration für die maximale Betrefflänge und Bereiche erfordern"],"pt":["Exige aderência ao estilo Conventional Commits","Pode exigir configuração manual para comprimento máximo do assunto e escopos"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения стиля Conventional Commits","Может потребовать ручную настройку для максимальной длины темы и областей"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع نمط Conventional Commits","قد يتطلب تنظیم يدوي ل أقصى طول للموضوع والنطاقات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"369786c13587086f6d052256a9fd4a1cdcb4173952b5bc9ce15afce9f0aeb00a","qualityScore":41}');
