ti-stream para várias fontes de dados"],"ru":["Событийный источник для отслеживания изменений","Бесконечная агрегация для данных","Интеграция с Rust для разработчиков","Возможности код-ревью для обеспечения качества","Поддержка.multi-stream для нескольких источников данных"],"ar":["مصدر الحدث لتتبع التغييرات","دمج غير محدود للبيانات","تكامل مع Rust لمطوري البرمجيات","ميزات مراجعة الكود لضمان الجودة","دعم متعدد الحالات لمصادر البيانات المتعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","代码审查工具","Rust Aggregateless","Multi-Stream Event-Sourcing","代码审查AI智能代理","如何使用代码审查AI智能代理","代码审查AI智能代理安装","代码审查AI智能代理设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","コードレビューツール","Rust Aggregateless","Multi-Stream Event-Sourcing","コードレビューアイエージェント","コードレビューアイエージェントの使用方法","コードレビューアイエージェントのインストール","コードレビューアイエージェントの設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","코드 리뷰 도구","Rust Aggregateless","Multi-Stream Event-Sourcing","코드 리뷰 AI 에이전트","코드 리뷰 AI 에이전트 사용 방법","코드 리뷰 AI 에이전트 설치","코드 리뷰 AI 에이전트 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de revisión de código de IA","cómo usar Aggregateless","qué es Event-Sourcing","alternativas a Rust","Rust vs Go","instalación de herramientas de revisión de código de IA","guía de configuración de Event-Sourcing"],"fr":["outils d''examen de code IA","comment utiliser Aggregateless","qu''est-ce que Event-Sourcing","alternatives à Rust","Rust vs Go","installation d''outils d''examen de code IA","guide de configuration de Event-Sourcing"],"de":["KI-Code-Überprüfungstools","wie man Aggregateless verwendet","was ist Event-Sourcing","Alternativen zu Rust","Rust vs Go","Installation von KI-Code-Überprüfungstools","Konfigurationsanleitung für Event-Sourcing"],"pt":["como usar code review","o que é event sourcing","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","code review em rust","alternativas para code review","guias de instalação de code review","configuração de code review"],"ru":["как использовать код-ревью","что такое событийный источник","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","код-ревью для rust","альтернативы код-ревью","руководства по установке код-ревью","настройка код-ревью"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام مراجعة الكود","ما هو مصدر الحدث","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمطوري البرمجيات","مراجعة الكود في Rust","بديلات مراجعة الكود","دليل تثبيت مراجعة الكود","إعدادات مراجعة الكود"]}},"owner":"jwilger","repo":"eventcore","repoPath":"jwilger/eventcore","stars":11,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T06:17:26Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":">-","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Code Review\n\n**Value:** Feedback and communication -- structured review catches defects that\nthe author cannot see, and separating review into stages prevents thoroughness\nin one area from crowding out another.\n\n## Purpose\n\nTeaches a systematic three-stage code review that evaluates spec compliance,\ncode quality, and domain integrity as separate passes. Prevents combined\nreviews from letting issues slip through by ensuring each dimension gets\nfocused attention.\n\n## Practices\n\n### Three Stages,","body":"# Code Review\n\n**Value:** Feedback and communication -- structured review catches defects that\nthe author cannot see, and separating review into stages prevents thoroughness\nin one area from crowding out another.\n\n## Purpose\n\nTeaches a systematic three-stage code review that evaluates spec compliance,\ncode quality, and domain integrity as separate passes. Prevents combined\nreviews from letting issues slip through by ensuring each dimension gets\nfocused attention.\n\n## Practices\n\n### Three Stages, In Order\n\nReview code in three sequential stages. Do not combine them. Each stage has a\nsingle focus. A failure in an earlier stage blocks later stages -- there is no\npoint reviewing code quality on code that does not meet the spec.\n\n**Stage 1: Spec Compliance.** Does the code do what was asked? Not more, not\nless.\n\nFor each acceptance criterion or requirement:\n\n1. Find the code that implements it\n2. Find the test that verifies it\n3. Confirm the implementation matches the spec exactly\n\nMark each criterion: PASS, FAIL (missing/incomplete/divergent), or CONCERN\n(implemented but potentially incorrect). Flag anything built beyond\nrequirements as OVER-BUILT.\n\nIf any criterion is FAIL, stop. Return to implementation before continuing.\n\n### Vertical Slice Layer Coverage\n\nFor tasks that implement a vertical slice (adding user-observable behavior), perform the following checks in order:\n\n1. **Entry-point wiring check (diff-based):** Examine whether the changeset includes modifications to the application''s entry point or its wiring/routing layer. If the slice claims to add new user-observable behavior but the diff does not touch any wiring or entry-point code, the review **fails** unless the author explicitly documents why existing wiring already routes to the new behavior.\n\n2. **End-to-end traceability:** Verify that a path can be traced from the application''s external entry point, through any infrastructure or integration layer, to the new domain logic, and back to observable output. If any segment of this path is missing from the changeset and not already present in the codebase, flag the gap.\n\n3. **Boundary-level test coverage:** Confirm that at least one test exercises the new behavior through the application''s external boundary (e.g., an HTTP request, a CLI invocation, a message on a queue) rather than calling internal functions directly. Where the application architecture makes automated boundary tests feasible, their absence is a review concern.\n\n4. **Test-level smell check:** If every test in the changeset is a unit test of isolated internal functions with no integration or acceptance-level test, flag this as a concern. The slice may be implementing domain logic without proving it is reachable through the running application.\n\n**Stage 2: Code Quality.** Is the code clear, maintainable, and well-tested?\n\nReview each changed file for:\n\n- **Clarity:** Can you understand what the code does without extra context?\n  Are names descriptive? Is the structure obvious?\n- **Domain types:** Are semantic types used where primitives appear? You MUST follow\n  the `domain-modeling` skill for primitive obsession detection.\n- **Error handling:** Are errors handled with typed errors? Are all paths\n  covered?\n- **Test quality:** Do tests verify behavior, not implementation? Is coverage\n  adequate for the changed code?\n- **YAGNI:** Is there unused code, speculative features, or premature\n  abstraction?\n\nCategorize findings by severity:\n\n- CRITICAL: Bug risk, likely to cause defects\n- IMPORTANT: Maintainability concern, should fix before merge\n- SUGGESTION: Style or minor improvement, optional\n\nIf any CRITICAL issue exists, stop. Return to implementation.\n\n**Stage 3: Domain Integrity.** Final gate -- does the code respect domain\nboundaries?\n\nCheck for:\n\n1. **Compile-time enforcement opportunities:** Are tests checking things the\n   type system could enforce instead?\n2. **Domain type consistency:** Are semantic types used at all boundaries, or\n   do primitives leak through?\n3. **Validation placement:** Is validation at construction (parse-don''t-validate),\n   not scattered through business logic?\n4. **State representation:** Can the types represent invalid states?\n\nFlag issues but do not block on suggestions. Domain integrity flags are\nstrongly recommended but not required for merge.\n\n### Review Output\n\nProduce a structured summary after all three stages:\n\n```\nREVIEW SUMMARY\nStage 1 (Spec Compliance): PASS/FAIL\nStage 2 (Code Quality): PASS/FAIL/PASS with suggestions\nStage 3 (Domain Integrity): PASS/FAIL/PASS with flags\n\nOverall: APPROVED / CHANGES REQUIRED\n\nIf CHANGES REQUIRED:\n  1. [specific required change]\n  2. [specific required change]\n```\n\n### Handling Disagreements\n\nWhen your review finding conflicts with the implementation approach:\n\n1. State the concern with specific code references\n2. Explain the risk -- what could go wrong\n3. Propose an alternative\n4. If no agreement after one round, escalate to the user\n\nYou exist to catch what the author missed, not to block progress.\n\n### Business Value and UX Awareness\n\nDuring Stage 1, also consider:\n\n- Does this slice deliver visible user value?\n- Are acceptance criteria specific and testable (not vague)?\n- Does the user journey remain coherent after this change?\n- Are edge cases and error states handled from the user''s perspective?\n\nThese are not blocking concerns but should be noted when relevant.\n\n## Enforcement Note\n\nThis skill provides advisory guidance. It instructs the agent on correct\nreview procedure but cannot mechanically prevent skipping stages or merging\nwithout review. When used with the `tdd` skill in automated mode, the\norchestrator can gate PR creation on review completion. In guided mode or\nstandalone, the agent follows these practices by convention. If you observe\nstages being skipped, point it out.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter completing a review guided by this skill, verify:\n\n- [ ] All three stages were performed separately, in order\n- [ ] Every acceptance criterion was mapped to code and tests in Stage 1\n- [ ] Each changed file was assessed for clarity and domain type usage in Stage 2\n- [ ] Domain integrity was checked for compile-time enforcement opportunities in Stage 3\n- [ ] A structured summary was produced with clear PASS/FAIL per stage\n- [ ] Any CHANGES REQUIRED items list specific, actionable fixes\n\nIf any criterion is not met, revisit the relevant stage before finalizing.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThis skill works standalone. For enhanced workflows, it integrates with:\n\n- **domain-modeling:** Provides the primitive obsession and parse-don''t-validate\n  principles referenced in Stage 2 and Stage 3\n- **tdd:** Reviews often follow a TDD cycle; this skill validates the\n  output of that cycle\n- **mutation-testing:** Can follow code review as an additional quality gate\n\nMissing a dependency? Install with:\n\n```\nnpx skills add jwilger/agent-skills --skill domain-modeling\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T13:21:29.275Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring structured feedback and multi-stage review processes for spec compliance, code quality, and domain integrity","zh":"适用于需要结构化反馈和多阶段审查流程以满足规范、代码质量和领域完整性的代码分析代理的理想选择","ja":"規範、コード品質、ドメイン完全性に対する構造化フィードバックと多段階のレビュー プロセスを必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適","ko":"규격, 코드 품질, 도메인 무결성을 위한 구조화된 피드백 및 多단계 리뷰 프로세스가 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren retroalimentación estructurada y procesos de revisión de múltiples etapas para el cumplimiento de especificaciones, la calidad del código y la integridad del dominio.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une rétroaction structurée et des processus de révision multi-étapes pour la conformité aux spécifications, la qualité du code et l''intégrité du domaine.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die strukturiertes Feedback und mehrstufige Überprüfungsprozesse für Spezifikationskonformität, Codequalität und Domänenintegrität benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem feedback estruturado e processos de revisão em múltiplas etapas para conformidade de especificação, qualidade de código e integridade de domínio","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих структурированной обратной связи и многоэтапных процессов рассмотрения для соблюдения спецификаций, качества кода и целостности домена","ar":"مثالية لعمليات تحليل الشفرة التي تتطلب تعليقات منسقة وعمليات استعراض متعددة المراحل لامتثال المواصفات و质量 الشفرة وصحة النطاق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically evaluate code through separate review stages, ensuring thoroughness and preventing issues from slipping through by utilizing three-stage code review that assesses spec compliance, code quality, and domain integrity, leveraging event-sourcing principles for Rust","zh":"赋予代理系统地评估代码的能力，通过独立的审查阶段，确保彻底性，并通过利用针对Rust的事件源原则的三阶段代码审查来防止问题的发生，评估规范、代码质量和领域完整性","ja":"エージェントにコードを体系的に評価する能力を与え、独立したレビュー段階を経て、徹底性を確保し、問題が見落とされるのを防ぐために、Rust向けのイベントソーシング原則を利用した3段階のコードレビューで規範、コード品質、ドメイン完全性を評価","ko":"에이전트에 코드를 체계적으로 평가할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 독립적인 리뷰 단계를 통해 철저성을 보장하고, 문제가 놓치지 않도록 Rust를 위한 이벤트 소싱 원리를 활용한 3단계 코드 리뷰를 통해 규격, 코드 품질, 도메인 무결성을 평가","es":"Permite a los agentes evaluar código sistemáticamente a través de etapas de revisión separadas, garantizando exhaustividad y evitando que los problemas pasen desapercibidos mediante la utilización de una revisión de código de tres etapas que evalúa el cumplimiento de especificaciones, la calidad del código y la integridad del dominio, aprovechando los principios de event-sourcing para Rust.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''évaluer systématiquement le code grâce à des étapes de révision distinctes, garantissant l''exhaustivité et empêchant les problèmes de passer inaperçus en utilisant une revue de code en trois étapes qui évalue la conformité aux spécifications, la qualité du code et l''intégrité du domaine, en tirant parti des principes d''event-sourcing pour Rust.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Code systematisch durch separate Überprüfungsstufen zu bewerten, sorgt für Gründlichkeit und verhindert, dass Probleme übersehen werden, indem ein dreistufiger Code-Review verwendet wird, der die Spezifikationskonformität, die Codequalität und die Domänenintegrität bewertet, unter Nutzung der Event-Sourcing-Prinzipien für Rust.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a avaliar sistematicamente o código por meio de etapas de revisão separadas, garantindo a completude e prevenindo problemas de passar despercebidos ao utilizar uma revisão de código de três etapas que avalia a conformidade de especificação, qualidade de código e integridade de domínio, aproveitando princípios de event-sourcing para Rust","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически оценивать код посредством отдельных стадий рассмотрения, гарантируя тщательность и предотвращая проблемы, которые могут остаться незамеченными, используя трехэтапный процесс рассмотрения кода, который оценивает соблюдение спецификаций, качество кода и целостность домена, используя принципы event-sourcing для Rust","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تقييم الشفرة بشكل منهجي من خلال مراحل استعراض منفصلة، مما يضمن الشمولية ويلغي прохожд المشكلات بدون ملاحظة، من خلال استخدام استعراض الشفرة ثلاثي المراحل الذي يقيم امتثال المواصفات و qualité الشفرة وصحة النطاق، مستفيدا من مبدأ event-sourcing لصالح Rust"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for Rust projects","Evaluating spec compliance in multi-stream event-sourcing architectures","Debugging domain integrity issues through focused review stages"],"zh":["自动化Rust项目的代码审查","评估多流事件源架构中的规格合规性","通过专注的审查阶段调试领域完整性问题"],"ja":["Rustプロジェクトのコードレビューの自動化","マルチストリームイベントソーシングアーキテクチャでの規範コンプライアンスの評価","ドメイン完全性の問題を絞り込んだレビュー段階でデバッグ"],"ko":["Rust 프로젝트의 코드 리뷰 자동화","다중 스트림 이벤트 소싱 아키텍처에서의 규격 준수 평가","도메인 무결성 문제를 집중적인 리뷰 단계를 통해 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para proyectos Rust","Evaluación del cumplimiento de especificaciones en arquitecturas de event-sourcing de múltiples streams","Depuración de problemas de integridad del dominio a través de etapas de revisión focalizadas"],"fr":["Automatisation des revues de code pour les projets Rust","Évaluation de la conformité aux spécifications dans les architectures event-sourcing multi-flux","Débogage des problèmes d''intégrité du domaine grâce à des étapes de révision ciblées"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für Rust-Projekte","Bewertung der Spezifikationskonformität in Multi-Stream-Event-Sourcing-Architekturen","Debugging von Domänenintegritätsproblemen durch fokussierte Überprüfungsstufen"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para projetos Rust","Avaliar conformidade de especificação em arquiteturas de event-sourcing multi-stream","Depurar problemas de integridade de domínio por meio de etapas de revisão focadas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода для проектов Rust","Оценивать соблюдение спецификаций в архитектурах event-sourcing с несколькими потоками","Исправлять проблемы целостности домена посредством сосредоточенных стадий рассмотрения"],"ar":["تutomatizar استعراض الشفرة لمشاريع Rust","تقييم امتثال المواصفات في هندسة event-sourcing متعددة المسارات","تصحيح مشاكل صحة النطاق من خلال مراحل استعراض محددة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Currently in early development/experimental phase","Specifically designed for Rust and aggregateless, multi-stream event-sourcing"],"zh":["目前处于早期开发/实验阶段","专门为Rust和聚合无、多流事件源设计"],"ja":["現在、早期開発/実験段階にあり","Rustとアグリゲートレス、 マルチストリームイベントソーシング専用に設計"],"ko":["현재 초기 개발/실험 단계에 있음","Rust 및 집계 없는 다중 스트림 이벤트 소싱을 위한 专用 설계"],"es":["Actualmente en fase experimental/desarrollo inicial","Específicamente diseñado para Rust y event-sourcing sin agregados y de múltiples streams"],"fr":["Actuellement en phase de développement précoce/expérimentale","Spécialement conçu pour Rust et l''event-sourcing sans agrégats et multi-flux"],"de":["Aktuell in früher Entwicklungs-/Experimentierphase","Speziell für Rust und aggregateless, Multi-Stream-Event-Sourcing entwickelt"],"pt":["Atualmente em fase de desenvolvimento experimental inicial","Especificamente projetado para Rust e aggregateless, event-sourcing multi-stream"],"ru":["В настоящее время находится на ранней стадии разработки/экспериментальной фазе","Специально разработан для Rust и aggregateless, event-sourcing с несколькими потоками"],"ar":["حاليًا في مرحلة التطوير التجريبي المبكر","مصمم خصيصًا لصالح Rust و aggregateless، event-sourcing متعددة المسارات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8241c29e1331983558c9273ecade261523f17cbc62a1c01d2fa3356d442abaa9","qualityScore":41}');
