ローカルのGitHubナレッジベースを管理し、GitHub検索機能を提供するために使用されます。環境変数を設定することで、プライベートリポジトリへのアクセスが可能","ko":"GitHub-KB 스킬은 로컬 GitHub 지식庫를 관리하고 GitHub 검색 기능을 제공하기 위해 사용됩니다. 환경 변수를 설정하면 프라이ベ이트 저장소에 접근할 수 있습니다","es":"La base de conocimiento de GitHub es una herramienta para gestionar y buscar proyectos de GitHub de forma local","fr":"La base de connaissances GitHub est un outil pour gérer et rechercher des projets GitHub de manière locale","de":"Die GitHub-Wissensbasis ist ein Tool zum Verwalten und Suchen von GitHub-Projekten auf lokaler Ebene","pt":"O skill github-kb permite gerenciar uma base de conhecimento local do GitHub e fornecer funcionalidades de busca via gh CLI","ru":"Навык github-kb позволяет управлять локальной базой знаний GitHub и предоставлять возможности поиска через gh CLI","ar":"تمكن مهارة github-kb من إدارة قاعدة معرفة جيثب محلية وتوفير إمكانيات البحث عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر gh","en":"All versions of all skills that are on clawdhub.com archived"},"definition":{"en":"All versions of all skills that are on clawdhub.com archived"},"features":{"zh":["管理本地GitHub知识库","通过gh CLI提供GitHub搜索功能","支持私有仓库访问","设置环境变量","支持GITHUB_TOKEN和GITHUB_KB_PATH变量"],"ja":["ローカルのGitHubナレッジベースを管理","gh CLI経由でGitHub検索機能を提供","プライベートリポジトリへのアクセスをサポート","環境変数を設定","GITHUB_TOKENとGITHUB_KB_PATH変数をサポート"],"ko":["로컬 GitHub 지식庫를 관리","gh CLI를 통해 GitHub 검색 기능을 제공","프라이베이트 저장소에 접근","환경 변수를 설정","GITHUB_TOKEN과 GITHUB_KB_PATH 변수를 지원"],"es":["Administración de base de conocimiento local de GitHub","Búsqueda en GitHub mediante gh CLI","Configuración de variables de entorno para acceso a repositorios privados","Soporte para tokens de acceso personales de GitHub","Catálogo de proyectos con descripciones breves en GITHUB_KB.md"],"fr":["Gestion d''une base de connaissances locale GitHub","Recherche sur GitHub via gh CLI","Configuration des variables d''environnement pour l''accès aux dépôts privés","Prise en charge des jetons d''accès personnels GitHub","Catalogue de projets avec des descriptions brèves dans GITHUB_KB.md"],"de":["Verwaltung einer lokalen GitHub-Wissensbasis","Suche in GitHub über gh CLI","Konfiguration von Umgebungsvariablen für den Zugriff auf private Repositorys","Unterstützung für persönliche GitHub-Zugriffstoken","Katalog von Projekten mit kurzen Beschreibungen in GITHUB_KB.md"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de base de conhecimento local do GitHub","Busca via gh CLI","Configuração de variáveis de ambiente","Suporte a repositórios privados com token de acesso pessoal","Catalogação de projetos com descrições breves"],"ru":["Управление локальной базой знаний GitHub","Поиск через gh CLI","Настройка переменных окружения","Поддержка приватных репозиториев с личным токеном доступа","Каталогизация проектов с краткими описаниями"],"ar":["إدارة قاعدة معرفة جيثب محلية","البحث عبر واجهة سطر الأوامر gh","تكوين متغيرات البيئة","دعم المستودعات الخاصة بالرمز الشخصي","فهرسة المشاريع مع_descriptions قصيرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitHub知识库","GitHub-KB","gh CLI","私有仓库","环境变量","GITHUB_TOKEN","GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"ja":["GitHubナレッジベース","GitHub-KB","gh CLI","プライベートリポジトリ","環境変数","GITHUB_TOKEN","GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"ko":["GitHub 지식庫","GitHub-KB","gh CLI","프라이베이트 저장소","환경 변수","GITHUB_TOKEN","GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"es":["GitHub","base de conocimiento","gh CLI","repositorios privados","tokens de acceso","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["GitHub","base de connaissances","gh CLI","dépôts privés","jetons d''accès","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["GitHub","Wissensbasis","gh CLI","private Repositorys","Zugriffstoken","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["github kb","base de conhecimento local","gerenciamento de conhecimento","busca github","gh cli","token de acesso pessoal","repositórios privados"],"ru":["github kb","локальная база знаний","управление знаниями","поиск github","gh cli","личный токен доступа","приватные репозитории"],"ar":["قاعدة معرفة جيثب","المعرفة المحلية","إدارة المعرفة","البحث جيثب","واجهة سطر الأوامر gh","الرمز الشخصي","المستودعات الخاصة"]}},"owner":"openclaw","repo":"skills","repoPath":"openclaw/skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.872Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"github-kb","description":"Manage a local GitHub knowledge base and provide GitHub search capabilities via gh CLI. Use when users ask about repos, PRs, issues, request to clone GitHub repositories, explore codebases, or need information about GitHub projects. Supports searching GitHub via gh CLI and managing local KB with GITHUB_KB.md catalog. Configure via GITHUB_TOKEN and GITHUB_KB_PATH environment variables.","bodyPreview":"# GitHub Knowledge Base\n\nManage a local GitHub knowledge base and provide GitHub search capabilities via gh CLI. Key file: GITHUB_KB.md at the root of the KB directory catalogs all projects with brief descriptions.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet environment variables before use:\n- `GITHUB_TOKEN` - GitHub Personal Access Token (optional, for private repos)\n- `GITHUB_KB_PATH` - Path to local KB directory (default: `/home/node/clawd/github-kb`)\n\nExample:\n```bash\nexport GITHUB_TOKEN=\"ghp_xxxx...\"\nexport GIT","body":"# GitHub Knowledge Base\n\nManage a local GitHub knowledge base and provide GitHub search capabilities via gh CLI. Key file: GITHUB_KB.md at the root of the KB directory catalogs all projects with brief descriptions.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet environment variables before use:\n- `GITHUB_TOKEN` - GitHub Personal Access Token (optional, for private repos)\n- `GITHUB_KB_PATH` - Path to local KB directory (default: `/home/node/clawd/github-kb`)\n\nExample:\n```bash\nexport GITHUB_TOKEN=\"ghp_xxxx...\"\nexport GITHUB_KB_PATH=\"/your/path/github-kb\"\n```\n\n**Token Privacy:** Never hardcode tokens. Inject via environment variables or container secrets.\n\n## GitHub CLI (gh)\n\n**Requirement:** GitHub CLI must be installed and authenticated.\n\n**Installation:**\n- **macOS:** `brew install gh`\n- **Linux:** `apt install gh` or see [official install guide](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/trunk/docs/install_linux.md)\n- **Windows:** `winget install GitHub.cli`\n\n**Authentication:**\n```bash\n# Interactive login\ngh auth login\n\n# Or use token from GITHUB_TOKEN env var\ngh auth login --with-token <(echo \"$GITHUB_TOKEN\")\n```\n\n**Verify:** `gh auth status`\n\nIf `gh` is not installed or not authenticated, skip search operations and use only local KB features.\n\n### Searching Repos\n\n```bash\n# Search repos by keyword\ngh search repos <query> [--limit <n>]\n\n# Examples:\ngh search repos \"typescript cli\" --limit 10\ngh search repos \"language:python stars:>1000\" --limit 20\ngh search repos \"topic:mcp\" --limit 15\n```\n\n**Search qualifiers:**\n- `language:<lang>` - Filter by programming language\n- `stars:<n>` or `stars:><n>` - Filter by star count\n- `topic:<name>` - Filter by topic\n- `user:<owner>` - Search within a user''s repos\n- `org:<org>` - Search within an organization\n\n### Searching Issues\n\n```bash\ngh search issues \"react hooks bug\" --limit 20\ngh search issues \"repo:facebook/react state:open\" --limit 30\ngh search issues \"language:typescript label:bug\" --limit 15\n```\n\n**Search qualifiers:**\n- `repo:<owner/repo>` - Search in specific repository\n- `state:open|closed` - Filter by issue state\n- `author:<username>` - Filter by author\n- `label:<name>` - Filter by label\n- `language:<lang>` - Filter by repo language\n- `comments:<n>` or `comments:><n>` - Filter by comment count\n\n### Searching Pull Requests\n\n```bash\n# Search PRs\ngh search prs <query> [--limit <n>]\n\n# Examples:\ngh search prs \"repo:vercel/next.js state:open\" --limit 30\ngh search prs \"language:go is:merged\" --limit 15\n```\n\n**Search qualifiers:**\n- `repo:<owner/repo>` - Search in specific repository\n- `state:open|closed|merged` - Filter by PR state\n- `author:<username>` - Filter by author\n- `label:<name>` - Filter by label\n- `language:<lang>` - Filter by repo language\n- `is:merged|unmerged` - Filter by merge status\n\n### Viewing PR/Issue Details\n\n```bash\n# View issue/PR details\ngh issue view <number> --repo <owner/repo>\ngh pr view <number> --repo <owner/repo>\n\n# View with comments\ngh issue view <number> --repo <owner/repo> --comments\ngh pr view <number> --repo <owner/repo> --comments\n```\n\n## Local Knowledge Base Workflow\n\n### Querying About a Repo in KB\n\n1. Read GITHUB_KB.md to understand what projects exist\n2. Locate the project directory under ${GITHUB_KB_PATH:-/home/node/clawd/github-kb}/\n\n### Cloning a New Repo to KB\n\n1. Search GitHub if the full repo name is not known\n2. Clone to KB directory:\n   ```bash\n   git clone https://github.com/<owner>/<name>.git ${GITHUB_KB_PATH:-/home/node/clawd/github-kb}/<name>\n   ```\n3. Generate project description: Read README or key files to understand the project\n4. Update GITHUB_KB.md: Add entry for the new repo following the existing format:\n   ```markdown\n   ### [<name>](/<name>)\n   Brief one-line description of what the project does. Additional context if useful (key features, tech stack, etc.).\n   ```\n5. Confirm completion: Tell user the repo was cloned and where to find it\n\n### Default Clone Location\n\nIf user says \"clone X\" without specifying a directory, default to ${GITHUB_KB_PATH:-/home/node/clawd/github-kb}/.\n\n## GITHUB_KB.md Format\n\nThe catalog file follows this structure:\n\n```markdown\n# GitHub Knowledge Base\n\nThis directory contains X GitHub projects covering various domains.\n\n---\n\n## Category Name\n\n### [project-name](/project-name)\nBrief description of the project.\n```\n\nMaintain categorization and consistent formatting when updating.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:06:01.785Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring streamlined GitHub repository management and search functionality via gh CLI.","zh":"适合需要简化 GitHub 仓库管理和搜索功能的开发代理，通过 gh CLI 实现。","ja":"GitHub リポジトリの管理と検索機能をストリームライン化する必要がある開発エージェントに適しています。gh CLI を使用します。","ko":"GitHub 리포지토리 관리 및 검색 기능을 스트림라인화해야 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다. gh CLI를 통해 제공됩니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una gestión de repositorios de GitHub simplificada y funcionalidad de búsqueda a través de la CLI de gh.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une gestion de référentiels GitHub simplifiée et une fonctionnalité de recherche via la CLI gh.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine strukturierte GitHub-Repository-Verwaltung und Suchfunktion über die gh-CLI erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de desenvolvimento que exigem gestão de repositório do GitHub simplificada e funcionalidade de pesquisa via CLI do gh.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих упрощенного управления репозиториями GitHub и функциональности поиска через CLI gh.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يتطلب إدارة مخزن GitHub مبسطًا وتوفر وظائف البحث من خلال واجهة سطر الأوامر gh."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage a local GitHub knowledge base, providing advanced search capabilities and cataloging projects with brief descriptions using the GITHUB_KB.md file, all while leveraging environment variables like GITHUB_TOKEN for private repository access.","zh":"赋予代理管理本地 GitHub 知识库的能力，提供高级搜索功能，并使用 GITHUB_KB.md 文件对项目进行目录编制，所有这些都利用环境变量，如 GITHUB_TOKEN 进行私有仓库访问。","ja":"エージェントがローカルの GitHub ナレッジベースを管理できるようにし、高度な検索機能を提供し、GITHUB_KB.md ファイルを使用してプロジェクトを簡単な説明とともにカタログ化します。環境変数の GITHUB_TOKEN を使用してプライベート リポジトリにアクセスします。","ko":"에이전트가 로컬 GitHub 지식 베이스를 관리할 수 있도록 해주며, 고급 검색 기능을 제공하고 GITHUB_KB.md 파일을 사용하여 프로젝트를 간단한 설명과 함께 카탈로그화합니다. 환경 변수인 GITHUB_TOKEN을 사용하여 비공개 리포지토리에 접근합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes gestionar una base de conocimientos local de GitHub, proporcionando capacidades de búsqueda avanzadas y catalogando proyectos con descripciones breves utilizando el archivo GITHUB_KB.md, todo mientras aprovecha variables de entorno como GITHUB_TOKEN para acceder a repositorios privados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer une base de connaissances GitHub locale, offrant des capacités de recherche avancées et cataloguant des projets avec des descriptions brèves en utilisant le fichier GITHUB_KB.md, le tout en exploitant des variables d''environnement comme GITHUB_TOKEN pour accéder aux référentiels privés.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, eine lokale GitHub-Wissensbasis zu verwalten, indem sie erweiterte Suchfunktionen bereitstellen und Projekte mit kurzen Beschreibungen über die Datei GITHUB_KB.md katalogisieren, während sie gleichzeitig Umgebungsvariablen wie GITHUB_TOKEN für den Zugriff auf private Repositorys nutzen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes gerenciem uma base de conhecimento local do GitHub, fornecendo capacidades de pesquisa avançadas e catalogação de projetos com descrições breves usando o arquivo GITHUB_KB.md, aproveitando variáveis de ambiente como GITHUB_TOKEN para acesso a repositórios privados.","ru":"Позволяет агентам управлять локальной базой знаний GitHub, обеспечивая расширенные возможности поиска и каталогизацию проектов с краткими описаниями с помощью файла GITHUB_KB.md, используя переменные среды, такие как GITHUB_TOKEN, для доступа к приватным репозиториям.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من إدارة قاعدة معرفة محلية لجيت هاب، وتوفير إمكانيات بحث متقدمة وفسرد مشاريع مع وصف موجز باستخدام ملف GITHUB_KB.md، مع الاستفادة من متغيّرات البيئة مثل GITHUB_TOKEN للوصول إلى مستودعات خاصة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating GitHub repository searches","Cataloging projects with brief descriptions in GITHUB_KB.md","Managing local knowledge base directories via GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"zh":["自动化 GitHub 仓库搜索","使用 GITHUB_KB.md 文件对项目进行目录编制","通过 GITHUB_KB_PATH 管理本地知识库目录"],"ja":["GitHub リポジトリの検索を自動化する","GITHUB_KB.md ファイルを使用してプロジェクトをカタログ化する","GITHUB_KB_PATH を使用してローカルのナレッジベース ディレクトリを管理する"],"ko":["GitHub 리포지토리 검색 자동화","GITHUB_KB.md 파일을 사용하여 프로젝트를 카탈로그화","GITHUB_KB_PATH를 사용하여 로컬 지식 베이스 디렉토리를 관리"],"es":["Automatizar las búsquedas de repositorios de GitHub","Catalogar proyectos con descripciones breves en GITHUB_KB.md","Gestionar directorios de la base de conocimientos local a través de GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"fr":["Automatiser les recherches de référentiels GitHub","Cataloguer des projets avec des descriptions brèves dans GITHUB_KB.md","Gérer les répertoires de la base de connaissances locale via GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"de":["Automatisierung der GitHub-Repository-Suchen","Katalogisierung von Projekten mit kurzen Beschreibungen in GITHUB_KB.md","Verwaltung von lokalen Wissensbasis-Verzeichnissen über GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"pt":["Automatizar pesquisas de repositório do GitHub","Catalogar projetos com descrições breves no arquivo GITHUB_KB.md","Gerenciar diretórios de base de conhecimento local via GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"ru":["Автоматизировать поиск репозиториев GitHub","Каталогизировать проекты с краткими описаниями в файле GITHUB_KB.md","Управлять локальными директориями базы знаний через GITHUB_KB_PATH"],"ar":["تحقيق آلي للبحث في مستودعات جيت هاب","تسجيل مشاريع مع وصف موجز في ملف GITHUB_KB.md","إدارة دليل قاعدة المعرفة المحلي عبر GITHUB_KB_PATH"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires GitHub Personal Access Token for private repos","Dependent on gh CLI for GitHub interactions","Needs environment variables set (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"zh":["需要 GitHub 个人访问令牌来访问私有仓库","依赖于 gh CLI 进行 GitHub 交互","需要设置环境变量（GITHUB_TOKEN、GITHUB_KB_PATH）"],"ja":["プライベート リポジトリにアクセスするには GitHub のパーソナル アクセス トークンが必要","GitHub の操作には gh CLI に依存","環境変数（GITHUB_TOKEN、GITHUB_KB_PATH）を設定する必要がある"],"ko":["비공개 리포지토리에 접근하기 위해 GitHub 개인 접근 토큰이 필요","GitHub 상호 작용을 위해 gh CLI에 의존","환경 변수(GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)를 설정해야 함"],"es":["Requiere un token de acceso personal de GitHub para repositorios privados","Dependiente de la CLI de gh para interacciones con GitHub","Necesita variables de entorno configuradas (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"fr":["Nécessite un jeton d''accès personnel GitHub pour les référentiels privés","Dépendant de la CLI gh pour les interactions avec GitHub","Nécessite des variables d''environnement configurées (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"de":["Benötigt ein GitHub-Personal-Zugriffstoken für private Repositorys","Abhängig von der gh-CLI für GitHub-Interaktionen","Benötigt konfigurierte Umgebungsvariablen (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"pt":["Exige Token de Acesso Pessoal do GitHub para repositórios privados","Depende da CLI do gh para interações com o GitHub","Necessita de variáveis de ambiente definidas (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"ru":["Требует личного токена доступа к GitHub для приватных репозиториев","Зависит от CLI gh для взаимодействия с GitHub","Требует настроенных переменных среды (GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_KB_PATH)"],"ar":["يتطلب رمز وصول شخصي لمستودعات جيت هاب الخاصة","يعتمد على واجهة سطر الأوامر gh للتفاعل مع جيت هاب","يحتاج إلى تعريف متغيرات بيئية (GITHUB_TOKEN، GITHUB_KB_PATH)"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"8d62830e2d00b0b63fe36620febd451b583dbcfad38acf354a1d77942401e303","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('rawwerks/rlm-cli/rlm', 'community', 'rawwerks', 'rlm-cli', 'rawwerks/rlm-cli', 'rlm', 0, 0, 40, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.877Z', '2026-03-02T02:07:16.418Z', 'd69e096ed158d6ff4516238286c74ac9412111b5463dc032292e91aaf179cb9e', '{"id":"rawwerks/rlm-cli/rlm","name":"rlm","description":{"zh":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","ja":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","ko":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","es":"RLM CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos para modelos de lenguaje recursivos que permite a los desarrolladores manejar contextos casi infinitos.","fr":"RLM CLI est un outil en ligne de commande pour les modèles de langage récursifs qui permet aux développeurs de gérer des contextes quasi-infinis.","de":"RLM CLI ist ein Command-Line-Tool für rekursive Sprachmodelle, das es Entwicklern ermöglicht, fast unendliche Kontexte zu verarbeiten.","pt":"O RLM CLI é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para modelos de linguagem recursiva, permitindo o processamento de contexto quase infinito.","ru":"RLM CLI - это инструмент командной строки для рекурсивных языковых моделей, позволяющий обрабатывать контекст почти бесконечной длины.","ar":"أداة RLM CLI هي أداة سطر أوامر لنمذجة اللغة التكرارية، وتتيح معالجة السياق شبه لا نهائي.","en":"CLI for Recursive Language Models"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"RLM CLI","ja":"RLM ","ko":"RLM CLI","es":"RLM CLI: Modelo de Lenguaje Recursivo para Desarrolladores","fr":"RLM CLI : Modèle de Langage Récurcif pour Développeurs","de":"RLM CLI: Rekursives Sprachmodell für Entwickler","pt":"RLM CLI: Ferramenta de Modelo de Linguagem Recursiva","ru":"RLM CLI: Инструмент для рекурсивных языковых моделей","ar":"RLM CLI: أداة النموذج اللغوي التكراري","en":"rlm"},"description":{"zh":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","ja":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","ko":"RLM CLIRecursive Language Models","es":"RLM CLI es una herramienta de línea de comandos para modelos de lenguaje recursivos que permite a los desarrolladores manejar contextos casi infinitos.","fr":"RLM CLI est un outil en ligne de commande pour les modèles de langage récursifs qui permet aux développeurs de gérer des contextes quasi-infinis.","de":"RLM CLI ist ein Command-Line-Tool für rekursive Sprachmodelle, das es Entwicklern ermöglicht, fast unendliche Kontexte zu verarbeiten.","pt":"O RLM CLI é uma ferramenta de linha de comando para modelos de linguagem recursiva, permitindo o processamento de contexto quase infinito.","ru":"RLM CLI - это инструмент командной строки для рекурсивных языковых моделей, позволяющий обрабатывать контекст почти бесконечной длины.","ar":"أداة RLM CLI هي أداة سطر أوامر لنمذجة اللغة التكرارية، وتتيح معالجة السياق شبه لا نهائي.","en":"CLI for Recursive Language Models"},"definition":{"en":"CLI for Recursive Language Models"},"features":{"zh":["Recursive Language Models","CLI","","URLS","stdin"],"ja":["Recursive Language Models","CLI","","URLS","stdin"],"ko":["Recursive Language Models","CLI","","URLS","stdin"],"es":["Soporte para archivos, directorios, URLs y stdin","Instalación sencilla con pip o pipx","Compatibilidad con diferentes backends","Uso de claves de API para autenticación","Flexibilidad para manejar contextos complejos"],"fr":["Prise en charge de fichiers, de répertoires, d''URL et de stdin","Installation simple avec pip ou pipx","Compatibilité avec différents backends","Utilisation de clés d''API pour l''authentification","Flexibilité pour gérer des contextes complexes"],"de":["Unterstützung für Dateien, Verzeichnisse, URLs und stdin","Einfache Installation mit pip oder pipx","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Backends","Verwendung von API-Schlüsseln für die Authentifizierung","Flexibilität für die Verarbeitung komplexer Kontexte"],"pt":["Processamento de contexto quase infinito","Suporte a arquivos, diretórios, URLs e stdin","Instalação fácil via pip ou pipx","Compatibilidade com diferentes backends","Interface de linha de comando intuitiva"],"ru":["Обработка контекста почти бесконечной длины","Поддержка файлов, директорий, URL и stdin","Легкая установка через pip или pipx","Совместимость с разными бэкендами","Интуитивный интерфейс командной строки"],"ar":["معالجة السياق شبه لا نهائي","دعم الملفات والمجلدات والرابط والstdin","تثبيت سهل عبر pip أو pipx","التوافق مع الخوادم الخلفية المختلفة","واجهة سطر أوامر直افة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["RLM CLI","Recursive Language Models","CLI","LLM","API","OpenRouter","OpenAI"],"ja":["RLM CLI","Recursive Language Models","CLI","LLM","API","OpenRouter","OpenAI"],"ko":["RLM CLI","Recursive Language Models","CLI","LLM","API","OpenRouter","OpenAI"],"es":["RLM CLI","Modelo de lenguaje recursivo","Desarrollo de software","Herramientas de línea de comandos","Procesamiento de lenguaje natural","Inteligencia artificial","Desarrolladores de software"],"fr":["RLM CLI","Modèle de langage récursif","Développement de logiciels","Outils en ligne de commande","Traitement du langage naturel","Intelligence artificielle","Développeurs de logiciels"],"de":["RLM CLI","Rekursives Sprachmodell","Software-Entwicklung","Command-Line-Tools","Verarbeitung von natürlicher Sprache","Künstliche Intelligenz","Software-Entwickler"],"pt":["modelo de linguagem recursiva","RLM CLI","processamento de contexto","ferramenta de linha de comando","desenvolvimento de software","inteligência artificial","processamento de linguagem natural"],"ru":["рекурсивная языковая модель","RLM CLI","обработка контекста","инструмент командной строки","разработка программного обеспечения","искусственный интеллект","обработка естественного языка"],"ar":["نمذجة اللغة التكرارية","RLM CLI","معالجة السياق","أداة سطر أوامر","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي","معالجة اللغة الطبيعية"]}},"owner":"rawwerks","repo":"rlm-cli","repoPath":"rawwerks/rlm-cli","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.877Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rlm","description":"Recursive Language Models (RLM) CLI - enables LLMs to recursively process large contexts by decomposing inputs and calling themselves over parts. Use for code analysis, diff reviews, codebase exploration. Triggers on rlm ask, rlm complete, rlm search, rlm index.","bodyPreview":"# RLM CLI\n\nRecursive Language Models (RLM) CLI - enables LLMs to handle near-infinite context by recursively decomposing inputs and calling themselves over parts. Supports files, directories, URLs, and stdin.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install rlm-cli    # or: pipx install rlm-cli\nuvx rlm-cli ask ...    # run without installing\n```\n\nSet an API key for your backend (openrouter is default):\n```bash\nexport OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...  # default backend\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY=...      # for --backend o","body":"# RLM CLI\n\nRecursive Language Models (RLM) CLI - enables LLMs to handle near-infinite context by recursively decomposing inputs and calling themselves over parts. Supports files, directories, URLs, and stdin.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install rlm-cli    # or: pipx install rlm-cli\nuvx rlm-cli ask ...    # run without installing\n```\n\nSet an API key for your backend (openrouter is default):\n```bash\nexport OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...  # default backend\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY=...      # for --backend openai\nexport ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...   # for --backend anthropic\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### ask - Query with context\n\n```bash\nrlm ask <inputs> -q \"question\"\n```\n\n**Inputs** (combinable):\n| Type | Example | Notes |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| Directory | `rlm ask . -q \"...\"` | Recursive, respects .gitignore |\n| File | `rlm ask main.py -q \"...\"` | Single file |\n| URL | `rlm ask https://x.com -q \"...\"` | Auto-converts to markdown |\n| stdin | `git diff \\| rlm ask - -q \"...\"` | `-` reads from pipe |\n| Literal | `rlm ask \"text\" -q \"...\" --literal` | Treat as raw text |\n| Multiple | `rlm ask a.py b.py -q \"...\"` | Combine any types |\n\n**Options:**\n| Flag | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `-q \"...\"` | Question/prompt (required) |\n| `--backend` | Provider: `openrouter` (default), `openai`, `anthropic` |\n| `--model NAME` | Model override (format: `provider/model` or just `model`) |\n| `--json` | Machine-readable output |\n| `--output-format` | Output format: `text`, `json`, or `json-tree` |\n| `--summary` | Show execution summary with depth statistics |\n| `--extensions .py .ts` | Filter by extension |\n| `--include/--exclude` | Glob patterns |\n| `--max-iterations N` | Limit REPL iterations (default: 30) |\n| `--max-depth N` | Recursive RLM depth (default: 1 = no recursion) |\n| `--max-budget N.NN` | Spending limit in USD (requires OpenRouter) |\n| `--max-timeout N` | Time limit in seconds |\n| `--max-tokens N` | Total token limit (input + output) |\n| `--max-errors N` | Consecutive error limit before stopping |\n| `--no-index` | Skip auto-indexing |\n| `--exa` | Enable Exa web search (requires `EXA_API_KEY`) |\n| `--inject-file FILE` | Execute Python code between iterations |\n\n**JSON output structure:**\n```json\n{\"ok\": true, \"exit_code\": 0, \"result\": {\"response\": \"...\"}, \"stats\": {...}}\n```\n\n**JSON-tree output (`--output-format=json-tree`):**\nAdds execution tree showing nested RLM calls:\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"response\": \"...\",\n    \"tree\": {\n      \"depth\": 0,\n      \"model\": \"openai/gpt-4\",\n      \"duration\": 2.3,\n      \"cost\": 0.05,\n      \"iterations\": [...],\n      \"children\": [...]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Summary output (`--summary`):**\nShows depth-wise statistics after completion:\n- JSON mode: adds `summary` field to `stats`\n- Text mode: prints summary to stderr\n\n```\n=== RLM Execution Summary ===\nTotal depth: 2 | Nodes: 3 | Cost: $0.0054 | Duration: 17.38s\nDepth 0: 1 call(s) ($0.0047, 13.94s)\nDepth 1: 2 call(s) ($0.0007, 3.44s)\n```\n\n### complete - Query without context\n\n```bash\nrlm complete \"prompt text\"\nrlm complete \"Generate SQL\" --json --backend openai\n```\n\n### search - Search indexed files\n\n```bash\nrlm search \"query\" [options]\n```\n\n| Flag | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `--limit N` | Max results (default: 20) |\n| `--language python` | Filter by language |\n| `--paths-only` | Output file paths only |\n| `--json` | JSON output |\n\nAuto-indexes on first use. Manual index: `rlm index .`\n\n### index - Build search index\n\n```bash\nrlm index .              # Index current dir\nrlm index ./src --force  # Force full reindex\n```\n\n### doctor - Check setup\n\n```bash\nrlm doctor       # Check config, API keys, deps\nrlm doctor --json\n```\n\n## Workflows\n\n**Git diff review:**\n```bash\ngit diff | rlm ask - -q \"Review for bugs\"\ngit diff --cached | rlm ask - -q \"Ready to commit?\"\ngit diff HEAD~3 | rlm ask - -q \"Summarize changes\"\n```\n\n**Codebase analysis:**\n```bash\nrlm ask . -q \"Explain architecture\"\nrlm ask src/ -q \"How does auth work?\" --extensions .py\n```\n\n**Search + analyze:**\n```bash\nrlm search \"database\" --paths-only\nrlm ask src/db.py -q \"How is connection pooling done?\"\n```\n\n**Compare files:**\n```bash\nrlm ask old.py new.py -q \"What changed?\"\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n**Precedence:** CLI flags > env vars > config file > defaults\n\n**Config locations:** `./rlm.yaml`, `./.rlm.yaml`, `~/.config/rlm/config.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nbackend: openrouter\nmodel: google/gemini-3-flash-preview\nmax_iterations: 30\n```\n\n**Environment variables:**\n- `RLM_BACKEND` - Default backend\n- `RLM_MODEL` - Default model\n- `RLM_CONFIG` - Config file path\n- `RLM_JSON=1` - Always output JSON\n\n## Recursion and Budget Limits\n\n### Recursive RLM (`--max-depth`)\n\nEnable recursive `llm_query()` calls where child RLMs process sub-tasks:\n\n```bash\n# 2 levels of recursion\nrlm ask . -q \"Research thoroughly\" --max-depth 2\n\n# With budget cap\nrlm ask . -q \"Analyze codebase\" --max-depth 3 --max-budget 0.50\n```\n\n### Budget Control (`--max-budget`)\n\nLimit spending per completion. Raises `BudgetExceededError` when exceeded:\n\n```bash\n# Cap at $1.00\nrlm complete \"Complex task\" --max-budget 1.00\n\n# Very low budget (will likely exceed)\nrlm ask . -q \"Analyze everything\" --max-budget 0.001\n```\n\n**Requirements:** OpenRouter backend (returns cost data in responses).\n\n### Other Limits\n\n**Timeout (`--max-timeout`)** - Stop after N seconds:\n```bash\nrlm complete \"Complex task\" --max-timeout 30\n```\n\n**Token limit (`--max-tokens`)** - Stop after N total tokens:\n```bash\nrlm ask . -q \"Analyze\" --max-tokens 10000\n```\n\n**Error threshold (`--max-errors`)** - Stop after N consecutive code errors:\n```bash\nrlm complete \"Write code\" --max-errors 3\n```\n\n### Stop Conditions\n\nRLM execution stops when any of these occur:\n1. **Final answer** - LLM calls `FINAL_VAR(\"variable_name\")` with the NAME of a variable (as a string)\n2. **Max iterations** - Exceeds `--max-iterations` (exit code 0, graceful - forces final answer)\n\n**FINAL_VAR usage** (common mistake - pass variable NAME, not value):\n```python\n# CORRECT:\nresult = {\"answer\": \"hello\", \"score\": 42}\nFINAL_VAR(\"result\")  # pass the variable NAME as a string\n\n# WRONG:\nFINAL_VAR(result)  # passing the dict directly causes AttributeError\n```\n3. **Max budget exceeded** - Spending > `--max-budget` (exit code 20, error)\n4. **Max timeout exceeded** - Time > `--max-timeout` (exit code 20, error with partial answer)\n5. **Max tokens exceeded** - Tokens > `--max-tokens` (exit code 20, error with partial answer)\n6. **Max errors exceeded** - Consecutive errors > `--max-errors` (exit code 20, error with partial answer)\n7. **User cancellation** - Ctrl+C or SIGUSR1 (exit code 0, returns partial answer as success)\n8. **Max depth reached** - Child RLM at depth 0 cannot recurse further\n\n**Note on max iterations:** This is a soft limit. When exceeded, RLM prompts the LLM one more time to provide a final answer. Modern LLMs typically complete in 1-2 iterations.\n\n**Partial answers:** When timeout, tokens, or errors stop execution, the error includes `partial_answer` if any response was generated before stopping.\n\n**Early exit (Ctrl+C):** Pressing Ctrl+C (or sending SIGUSR1) returns the partial answer as success (exit code 0) with `early_exit: true` in the result.\n\n### Inject File (--inject-file)\n\nUpdate REPL variables mid-run by modifying an inject file:\n\n```bash\n# Create inject file\necho ''focus = \"authentication\"'' > inject.py\n\n# Run with inject file\nrlm ask . -q \"Analyze based on ''focus''\" --inject-file inject.py\n\n# In another terminal, update mid-run\necho ''focus = \"authorization\"'' > inject.py\n```\n\nThe file is checked before each iteration and executed if modified.\n\n## Exit Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| 0 | Success |\n| 2 | CLI usage error |\n| 10 | Input error (file not found) |\n| 11 | Config error (missing API key) |\n| 20 | Backend/API error (includes budget exceeded) |\n| 30 | Runtime error |\n| 40 | Index/search error |\n\n## LLM Search Tools\n\nWhen `rlm ask` runs on a directory, the LLM gets search tools:\n\n| Tool | Cost | Privacy | Use For |\n|------|------|---------|---------|\n| `rg.search()` | Free | Local | Exact patterns, function names, imports |\n| `tv.search()` | Free | Local | Topics, concepts, related files |\n| `exa.search()` | **$** | **API** | Web search (requires `--exa` flag) |\n| `pi.*` | **$$$** | **API** | Hierarchical PDF/document navigation |\n\n### Free Local Tools (auto-loaded)\n\n- **rg.search(pattern, paths, globs)** - ripgrep for exact patterns\n- **tv.search(query, limit)** - Tantivy BM25 for concepts\n\n### Exa Web Search (--exa flag, Costs Money)\n\n⚠️ **Opt-in**: Requires `--exa` flag and `EXA_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n**Setup:**\n```bash\nexport EXA_API_KEY=...  # Get from https://exa.ai\n```\n\n**Usage in REPL:**\n```python\nfrom rlm_cli.tools_search import exa, web\n\n# Basic search\nresults = exa.search(query=\"Python async patterns\", limit=5)\nfor r in results:\n    print(f\"{r[''title'']}: {r[''url'']}\")\n\n# With highlights (relevant excerpts)\nresults = exa.search(\n    query=\"error handling best practices\",\n    limit=3,\n    include_highlights=True\n)\n\n# Semantic alias\nresults = web(query=\"machine learning tutorial\", limit=5)\n\n# Find similar pages\nresults = exa.find_similar(url=\"https://example.com/article\", limit=5)\n```\n\n**exa.search() parameters:**\n| Param | Default | Description |\n|-------|---------|-------------|\n| `query` | required | Search query |\n| `limit` | 10 | Max results |\n| `search_type` | \"auto\" | \"auto\", \"neural\", or \"keyword\" |\n| `include_domains` | None | Only these domains |\n| `exclude_domains` | None | Exclude these domains |\n| `include_text` | False | Include full page text |\n| `include_highlights` | True | Include relevant excerpts |\n| `category` | None | \"company\", \"research paper\", \"news\", etc. |\n\n**When to use exa.search() / web():**\n- Finding external documentation, tutorials, articles\n- Researching topics beyond the local codebase\n- Finding similar pages to a reference URL\n\n### PageIndex (pi.* - Opt-in, Costs Money)\n\n⚠️ **WARNING**: PageIndex sends document content to LLM APIs and costs money.\n\n**Only use when:**\n1. User explicitly requests document/PDF analysis\n2. Document has hierarchical structure (reports, manuals)\n3. User accepts cost/privacy tradeoffs\n\n**Prerequisites:**\n- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` (or other backend key) must be set in environment\n- PageIndex submodule must be initialized\n- Run within rlm-cli''s virtual environment (has required dependencies)\n\n**Setup (REQUIRED before any pi.* operation):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/path/to/rlm-cli/rlm\")        # rlm submodule\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/path/to/rlm-cli/pageindex\")  # pageindex submodule\n\nfrom rlm.clients import get_client\nfrom rlm_cli.tools_pageindex import pi\n\n# Configure with existing rlm backend\nclient = get_client(backend=\"openrouter\", backend_kwargs={\"model_name\": \"google/gemini-2.0-flash-001\"})\npi.configure(client)\n```\n\n**Indexing (costs $$$):**\n```python\n# Build tree index - THIS COSTS MONEY (no caching, re-indexes each call)\ntree = pi.index(path=\"report.pdf\")\n# Returns: PITree object with doc_name, nodes, doc_description, raw\n```\n\n**Viewing structure (free after indexing):**\n```python\n# Display table of contents\nprint(pi.toc(tree))\n\n# Get section by node_id (IDs are \"0000\", \"0001\", \"0002\", etc.)\nsection = pi.get_section(tree, \"0003\")\n# Returns: PINode with title, node_id, start_index, end_index, summary, children\n# Returns: None if not found\n\nif section:\n    print(f\"{section.title}: pages {section.start_index}-{section.end_index}\")\n```\n\n**Finding node IDs:**\nNode IDs are assigned sequentially (\"0000\", \"0001\", ...) in tree traversal order.\nTo see all node IDs, access the raw tree structure:\n```python\nimport json\nprint(json.dumps(tree.raw[\"structure\"], indent=2))\n# Each node has: title, node_id, start_index, end_index\n```\n\n**pi.* API Reference:**\n| Method | Cost | Returns | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `pi.configure(client)` | Free | None | Set rlm backend (REQUIRED first) |\n| `pi.status()` | Free | dict | Check availability, config, warning |\n| `pi.index(path=str)` | $$$ | PITree | Build tree from PDF |\n| `pi.toc(tree, max_depth=3)` | Free | str | Formatted table of contents |\n| `pi.get_section(tree, node_id)` | Free | PINode or None | Get section by ID |\n| `pi.available()` | Free | bool | Check if PageIndex installed |\n| `pi.configured()` | Free | bool | Check if client configured |\n\n**PITree attributes:** `doc_name`, `nodes` (list of PINode), `doc_description`, `raw` (dict)\n**PINode attributes:** `title`, `node_id`, `start_index`, `end_index`, `summary` (may be None), `children` (may be None)\n\n**Notes:**\n- `summary` is only populated if `add_summaries=True` in `pi.index()`\n- `children` is None for leaf nodes (sections with no subsections)\n- `tree.raw[\"structure\"]` is a flat list; hierarchy is in PINode.children\n- PageIndex extracts document structure (TOC), not content. Use page numbers to locate sections in the original PDF.\n\n**Example output from pi.toc():**\n```\n📄 annual_report.pdf\n\n• Executive Summary (p.1-5)\n• Financial Overview (p.6-20)\n  • Revenue (p.6-10)\n  • Expenses (p.11-15)\n  • Projections (p.16-20)\n• Risk Factors (p.21-35)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:07:16.418Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced Language Agents needing recursive language model capabilities for handling vast context","zh":"非常适合需要递归语言模型能力来处理大量上下文的高级语言代理","ja":"高度な言語エージェントが大量のコンテキストを処理するために必要な再帰言語モデル能力に最適","ko":"방대한 양의 contexto를 처리하기 위해 재귀 언어 모델 기능이 필요한 고급 언어 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje Avanzados que necesitan capacidades de modelo de lenguaje recursivo para manejar un contexto vasto","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage Avancés ayant besoin de capacités de modèle de langage récursif pour gérer un contexte vaste","de":"Perfekt für fortschrittliche Sprachagenten, die rekursive Sprachmodellfunktionen für die Verarbeitung eines umfangreichen Kontexts benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem Avançados que precisam de capacidades de modelo de linguagem recursivo para lidar com vasto contexto","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых языковых агентов, требующих рекурсивных возможностей языковой модели для обработки огромного контекста","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء اللغويين المتقدمين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات نموذج لغة متكرر لتعامل مع سياق واسع"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle near-infinite context by recursively decomposing inputs and calling themselves over parts using CLI, supporting files, directories, URLs, and stdin through libraries like rlm-cli, and integrating with backends via OpenRouter API Key or OpenAI API Key","zh":"通过递归分解输入并使用CLI、支持文件、目录、URL和stdin来调用自身的部分，并通过OpenRouter API密钥或OpenAI API密钥与后端集成，赋予代理处理近无限上下文的能力","ja":"CLI、ファイル、ディレクトリ、URL、stdinを介して部分を呼び出し、OpenRouter APIキーまたはOpenAI APIキーを使用してバックエンドと統合することで、エージェントに近無限のコンテキストを処理する能力を提供する","ko":"CLI, 파일, 디렉토리, URL 및 stdin을 통해 부분을 호출하고 OpenRouter API 키 또는 OpenAI API 키를 사용하여 백엔드와 통합하여 에이전트가 거의 무한한 contexto를 처리할 수 있도록 하는 것","es":"Habilita a los agentes a manejar un contexto casi infinito mediante la descomposición recursiva de las entradas y llamadas a sí mismos sobre partes utilizando CLI, archivos, directorios, URLs y stdin a través de bibliotecas como rlm-cli, e integrándose con backends a través de OpenRouter API Key o OpenAI API Key","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer un contexte presque infini en décomposant de manière récursive les entrées et en s''appelant eux-mêmes sur des parties en utilisant CLI, des fichiers, des répertoires, des URL et stdin via des bibliothèques comme rlm-cli, et en s''intégrant avec des backends via OpenRouter API Key ou OpenAI API Key","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, einen fast unendlichen Kontext zu verarbeiten, indem sie Eingaben rekursiv in Teile zerlegen und sich selbst über CLI, Dateien, Verzeichnisse, URLs und stdin aufrufen, unterstützt durch Bibliotheken wie rlm-cli, und sich in Backends über OpenRouter-API-Schlüssel oder OpenAI-API-Schlüssel integrieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lidarem com contexto quase infinito decompondo recursivamente as entradas e chamando a si mesmos sobre partes usando CLI, suportando arquivos, diretórios, URLs e stdin por meio de bibliotecas como rlm-cli, e integrando com backends via Chave de API OpenRouter ou Chave de API OpenAI","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обрабатывать几乎 бесконечный контекст, рекурсивно разбивая входные данные и вызывая самих себя по частям, используя CLI, поддерживая файлы, каталоги, URL и stdin через библиотеки, такие как rlm-cli, и интегрируясь с бэкендами через ключ API OpenRouter или ключ API OpenAI","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التعامل مع السياق الذي لا نهاية له تقريبًا من خلال تحليل المدخلات بشكل متكرر وتحويلها إلى أنفسهم أكثر من مرة باستخدام CLI، ودعم الملفات والمجلدات والروابط والمدخلات المعيارية من خلال مكتبات مثل rlm-cli، والدمج مع الخوادم الخلفية عبر مفتاح واجهة برمجة التطبيقات OpenRouter أو مفتاح واجهة برمجة التطبيقات OpenAI"},"useCases":{"en":["Decomposing large inputs for efficient processing","Recursively calling language models for enhanced context understanding","Integrating with OpenRouter or OpenAI for advanced backend capabilities"],"zh":["分解大型输入以进行高效处理","递归调用语言模型以增强上下文理解","与OpenRouter或OpenAI集成以实现高级后端功能"],"ja":["大きな入力を効率的に処理するために分解する","コンテキスト理解を強化するために言語モデルを再帰的に呼び出す","OpenRouterまたはOpenAIと統合して高度なバックエンド機能を実現する"],"ko":["효율적인 처리를 위해 대형 입력을 분해하는 것","context 이해를 강화하기 위해 언어 모델을 재귀적으로 호출하는 것","고급 백엔드 기능을 구현하기 위해 OpenRouter 또는 OpenAI와 통합하는 것"],"es":["Descomponer grandes entradas para un procesamiento eficiente","Llamar recursivamente a modelos de lenguaje para una mejor comprensión del contexto","Integrarse con OpenRouter o OpenAI para funcionalidades de backend avanzadas"],"fr":["Décomposer de grandes entrées pour un traitement efficace","Appeler de manière récursive des modèles de langage pour une meilleure compréhension du contexte","S''intégrer avec OpenRouter ou OpenAI pour des fonctionnalités de backend avancées"],"de":["Große Eingaben in Teile zerlegen, um eine effiziente Verarbeitung zu ermöglichen","Rekursiv Sprachmodelle aufrufen, um das Kontextverständnis zu verbessern","Sich in OpenRouter oder OpenAI integrieren, um erweiterte Backend-Funktionen zu nutzen"],"pt":["Decompor entradas grandes para processamento eficiente","Chamar modelos de linguagem recursivamente para compreensão aprimorada do contexto","Integrar com OpenRouter ou OpenAI para capacidades avançadas de backend"],"ru":["Разбить большие входные данные для эффективной обработки","Рекурсивно вызывать языковые модели для улучшенного понимания контекста","Интегрироваться с OpenRouter или OpenAI для продвинутых возможностей бэкенда"],"ar":["تجزئة المدخلات الكبيرة للمعالجة الفعالة","استدعاء نماذج اللغة بشكل متكرر لتحسين فهم السياق","التكامل مع OpenRouter أو OpenAI لتحقيق إمكانيات متقدمة للخادم الخلفي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires API key for backend integration","Dependent on rlm-cli installation or uvx for execution"],"zh":["需要API密钥进行后端集成","依赖于rlm-cli安装或uvx进行执行"],"ja":["バックエンド統合にはAPIキーが必要","実行にはrlm-cliのインストールまたはuvxに依存する"],"ko":["백엔드 통합을 위해 API 키가 필요","실행을 위해 rlm-cli 설치 또는 uvx에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una clave de API para la integración con el backend","Depende de la instalación de rlm-cli o uvx para la ejecución"],"fr":["Nécessite une clé d''API pour l''intégration avec le backend","Dépend de l''installation de rlm-cli ou uvx pour l''exécution"],"de":["Benötigt einen API-Schlüssel für die Integration mit dem Backend","Hängt von der Installation von rlm-cli oder uvx für die Ausführung ab"],"pt":["Requer chave de API para integração com backend","Depende da instalação do rlm-cli ou uvx para execução"],"ru":["Требует ключа API для интеграции с бэкендом","Зависит от установки rlm-cli или uvx для выполнения"],"ar":["يتطلب مفتاح واجهة برمجة التطبيقات للتحقق من الخادم الخلفي","يعتمد على تثبيت rlm-cli أو uvx للتشغيل"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d69e096ed158d6ff4516238286c74ac9412111b5463dc032292e91aaf179cb9e","qualityScore":40}');
