站对AI代理可访问，实现在线任务的自动化","ja":"リモートブラウザースキルは、WebサイトをAIエージェントにアクセス可能にし、オンラインタスクの自動化を実現します","ko":"원격 브라우저 스킬은 웹사이트를 AI 에이전트에 접근 가능하게 하고 온라인 작업의 자동화를 실현합니다","es":"El remote-browser permite a los desarrolladores acceder a sitios web de forma remota y automatizar tareas en línea con herramientas de agente de IA","fr":"Le remote-browser permet aux développeurs d''accéder à des sites web de manière distante et d''automatiser des tâches en ligne avec des outils d''agents IA","de":"Der remote-browser ermöglicht es Entwicklern, auf Webseiten zuzugreifen und Online-Aufgaben mit AI-Agent-Tools zu automatisieren","pt":"O Remote-Browser permite que websites sejam acessíveis para agentes de IA, facilitando a automação de tarefas online.","ru":"Remote-Browser делает сайты доступными для ИИ Агентов, упрощая автоматизацию задач онлайн.","ar":"يسمح Remote-Browser للعملاء الذكاء الاصطناعي بالوصول إلى المواقع الإلكترونية، مما يسهل автоматизация المهام عبر الإنترنت.","en":"🌐 Make websites accessible for AI agents. Automate tasks online with ease."},"definition":{"en":"🌐 Make websites accessible for AI agents. Automate tasks online with ease."},"features":{"zh":["支持AI代理访问网站","自动化在线任务","提高开发效率","支持多种编程语言","提供CLI工具","支持Node.js和Python集成"],"ja":["AIエージェントによるWebサイトアクセスをサポート","オンラインタスクの自動化","開発効率の向上","多くのプログラミング言語をサポート","CLIツールを提供","Node.jsとPythonとの統合をサポート"],"ko":["AI 에이전트가 웹사이트에 접근할 수 있도록 지원","온라인 작업의 자동화","개발 효율의 향상","다수의 프로그래밍 언어를 지원","CLI 툴을 제공","Node.js와 Python과의 통합을 지원"],"es":["Acceso remoto a sitios web","Automatización de tareas en línea","Integración con herramientas de agente de IA","Compatibilidad con múltiples plataformas","Seguridad y autenticación avanzadas"],"fr":["Accès distant à des sites web","Automatisation de tâches en ligne","Intégration avec des outils d''agents IA","Compatibilité avec plusieurs plateformes","Sécurité et authentification avancées"],"de":["Remote-Zugriff auf Webseiten","Automatisierung von Online-Aufgaben","Integration mit AI-Agent-Tools","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Plattformen","Erweiterte Sicherheit und Authentifizierung"],"pt":["Acesso a websites para agentes de IA","Automação de tarefas online","Integração com CLI","Suporte a React e Node.js","Facilidade de uso","Documentação completa"],"ru":["Доступ к сайтам для ИИ Агентов","Автоматизация задач онлайн","Интеграция с CLI","Поддержка React и Node.js","Легкость использования","Полная документация"],"ar":["الوصول إلى المواقع الإلكترونية للعملاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","أتمتة المهام عبر الإنترنت","التكامل مع CLI","دعم React و Node.js","سهولة الاستخدام","وثائق شاملة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用远程浏览器技能","什么是AI代理","远程浏览器技能替代品","远程浏览器技能与Selenium比较","远程浏览器技能安装","远程浏览器技能设置指南","AI代理工具","自动化在线任务"],"ja":["リモートブラウザースキルの使用方法","AIエージェントとは","リモートブラウザースキルの代替品","リモートブラウザースキルとSeleniumの比較","リモートブラウザースキルのインストール","リモートブラウザースキルの設定ガイド","AIエージェントツール","オンラインタスクの自動化"],"ko":["원격 브라우저 스킬 사용법","AI 에이전트란","원격 브라우저 스킬 대체품","원격 브라우저 스킬과 Selenium 비교","원격 브라우저 스킬 설치","원격 브라우저 스킬 설정 가이드","AI 에이전트 툴","온라인 작업 자동화"],"es":["herramientas de agente de IA","automatización de tareas en línea","acceso remoto a sitios web","remote-browser alternativa","cómo usar remote-browser","instalación de remote-browser","guía de configuración de remote-browser"],"fr":["outils d''agents IA","automatisation de tâches en ligne","accès distant à des sites web","remote-browser alternative","comment utiliser remote-browser","installation de remote-browser","guide de configuration de remote-browser"],"de":["AI-Agent-Tools","Automatisierung von Online-Aufgaben","Remote-Zugriff auf Webseiten","remote-browser Alternative","wie man remote-browser verwendet","Installation von remote-browser","Konfigurationsanleitung für remote-browser"],"pt":["como usar Remote-Browser","o que é agente de IA","Remote-Browser alternativa","Remote-Browser vs Selenium","instalar Remote-Browser","guia de configuração do Remote-Browser","desenvolvimento de software com Remote-Browser","automação de tarefas com Remote-Browser"],"ru":["как использовать Remote-Browser","что такое ИИ Агент","альтернатива Remote-Browser","Remote-Browser vs Selenium","установка Remote-Browser","руководство по настройке Remote-Browser","разработка программного обеспечения с Remote-Browser","автоматизация задач с Remote-Browser"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Remote-Browser","ما هو العميل الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل Remote-Browser","Remote-Browser مقابل Selenium","تثبيت Remote-Browser","دليل إعداد Remote-Browser","تطوير البرمجيات مع Remote-Browser","أتمتة المهام مع Remote-Browser"]}},"owner":"browser-use","repo":"browser-use","repoPath":"browser-use/browser-use","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.885Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"remote-browser","description":"Controls a cloud browser from a sandboxed remote machine. Use when the agent is running in a sandbox (no GUI) and needs to navigate websites, interact with web pages, fill forms, take screenshots, or expose local dev servers via tunnels.","bodyPreview":"# Remote Browser Automation for Sandboxed Agents\n\nThis skill is for agents running on **sandboxed remote machines** (cloud VMs, CI, coding agents) that need to control a browser. Install `browser-use` and drive a cloud browser — no local Chrome needed.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore using this skill, `browser-use` must be installed and configured. Run diagnostics to verify:\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use doctor\n```\n\nFor more information, see https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/blob/main/browser_use/skil","body":"# Remote Browser Automation for Sandboxed Agents\n\nThis skill is for agents running on **sandboxed remote machines** (cloud VMs, CI, coding agents) that need to control a browser. Install `browser-use` and drive a cloud browser — no local Chrome needed.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore using this skill, `browser-use` must be installed and configured. Run diagnostics to verify:\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use doctor\n```\n\nFor more information, see https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/blob/main/browser_use/skill_cli/README.md\n\n## Core Workflow\n\nCommands use the cloud browser:\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Start session (automatically uses remote mode)\nbrowser-use open https://example.com\n# Returns: url, live_url (view the browser in real-time)\n\n# Step 2+: All subsequent commands use the existing session\nbrowser-use state                   # Get page elements with indices\nbrowser-use click 5                 # Click element by index\nbrowser-use type \"Hello World\"      # Type into focused element\nbrowser-use input 3 \"text\"          # Click element, then type\nbrowser-use screenshot              # Take screenshot (base64)\nbrowser-use screenshot page.png     # Save screenshot to file\n\n# Done: Close the session\nbrowser-use close                   # Close browser and release resources\n```\n\n## Essential Commands\n\n```bash\n# Navigation\nbrowser-use open <url>                    # Navigate to URL\nbrowser-use back                          # Go back\nbrowser-use scroll down                   # Scroll down (--amount N for pixels)\n\n# Page State (always run state first to get element indices)\nbrowser-use state                         # Get URL, title, clickable elements\nbrowser-use screenshot                    # Take screenshot (base64)\nbrowser-use screenshot path.png           # Save screenshot to file\n\n# Interactions (use indices from state)\nbrowser-use click <index>                 # Click element\nbrowser-use type \"text\"                   # Type into focused element\nbrowser-use input <index> \"text\"          # Click element, then type\nbrowser-use keys \"Enter\"                  # Send keyboard keys\nbrowser-use select <index> \"option\"       # Select dropdown option\n\n# Data Extraction\nbrowser-use eval \"document.title\"         # Execute JavaScript\nbrowser-use get text <index>              # Get element text\nbrowser-use get html --selector \"h1\"      # Get scoped HTML\n\n# Wait\nbrowser-use wait selector \"h1\"            # Wait for element\nbrowser-use wait text \"Success\"           # Wait for text\n\n# Session\nbrowser-use close                         # Close browser session\n\n# AI Agent\nbrowser-use run \"task\"                    # Run agent (async by default)\nbrowser-use task status <id>              # Check task progress\n```\n\n## Commands\n\n### Navigation & Tabs\n```bash\nbrowser-use open <url>              # Navigate to URL\nbrowser-use back                    # Go back in history\nbrowser-use scroll down             # Scroll down\nbrowser-use scroll up               # Scroll up\nbrowser-use scroll down --amount 1000  # Scroll by specific pixels (default: 500)\nbrowser-use switch <tab>            # Switch tab by index\nbrowser-use close-tab               # Close current tab\nbrowser-use close-tab <tab>         # Close specific tab\n```\n\n### Page State\n```bash\nbrowser-use state                   # Get URL, title, and clickable elements\nbrowser-use screenshot              # Take screenshot (base64)\nbrowser-use screenshot path.png     # Save screenshot to file\nbrowser-use screenshot --full p.png # Full page screenshot\n```\n\n### Interactions\n```bash\nbrowser-use click <index>           # Click element\nbrowser-use type \"text\"             # Type into focused element\nbrowser-use input <index> \"text\"    # Click element, then type\nbrowser-use keys \"Enter\"            # Send keyboard keys\nbrowser-use keys \"Control+a\"        # Key combination\nbrowser-use select <index> \"option\" # Select dropdown option\nbrowser-use hover <index>           # Hover over element\nbrowser-use dblclick <index>        # Double-click\nbrowser-use rightclick <index>      # Right-click\n```\n\nUse indices from `browser-use state`.\n\n### JavaScript & Data\n```bash\nbrowser-use eval \"document.title\"   # Execute JavaScript\nbrowser-use get title               # Get page title\nbrowser-use get html                # Get page HTML\nbrowser-use get html --selector \"h1\"  # Scoped HTML\nbrowser-use get text <index>        # Get element text\nbrowser-use get value <index>       # Get input value\nbrowser-use get attributes <index>  # Get element attributes\nbrowser-use get bbox <index>        # Get bounding box (x, y, width, height)\n```\n\n### Cookies\n```bash\nbrowser-use cookies get             # Get all cookies\nbrowser-use cookies get --url <url> # Get cookies for specific URL\nbrowser-use cookies set <name> <val>  # Set a cookie\nbrowser-use cookies set name val --domain .example.com --secure\nbrowser-use cookies set name val --same-site Strict  # SameSite: Strict, Lax, None\nbrowser-use cookies set name val --expires 1735689600  # Expiration timestamp\nbrowser-use cookies clear           # Clear all cookies\nbrowser-use cookies clear --url <url>  # Clear cookies for specific URL\nbrowser-use cookies export <file>   # Export to JSON\nbrowser-use cookies import <file>   # Import from JSON\n```\n\n### Wait Conditions\n```bash\nbrowser-use wait selector \"h1\"                         # Wait for element\nbrowser-use wait selector \".loading\" --state hidden    # Wait for element to disappear\nbrowser-use wait text \"Success\"                        # Wait for text\nbrowser-use wait selector \"#btn\" --timeout 5000        # Custom timeout (ms)\n```\n\n### Python Execution\n```bash\nbrowser-use python \"x = 42\"           # Set variable\nbrowser-use python \"print(x)\"         # Access variable (prints: 42)\nbrowser-use python \"print(browser.url)\"  # Access browser object\nbrowser-use python --vars             # Show defined variables\nbrowser-use python --reset            # Clear namespace\nbrowser-use python --file script.py   # Run Python file\n```\n\nThe Python session maintains state across commands. The `browser` object provides:\n- `browser.url`, `browser.title`, `browser.html` — page info\n- `browser.goto(url)`, `browser.back()` — navigation\n- `browser.click(index)`, `browser.type(text)`, `browser.input(index, text)`, `browser.keys(keys)` — interactions\n- `browser.screenshot(path)`, `browser.scroll(direction, amount)` — visual\n- `browser.wait(seconds)`, `browser.extract(query)` — utilities\n\n### Agent Tasks\n```bash\nbrowser-use run \"Fill the contact form with test data\"   # AI agent\nbrowser-use run \"Extract all product prices\" --max-steps 50\n\n# Specify LLM model\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --llm gpt-4o\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --llm claude-sonnet-4-20250514\n\n# Proxy configuration (default: us)\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --proxy-country uk\n\n# Session reuse\nbrowser-use run \"task 1\" --keep-alive        # Keep session alive after task\nbrowser-use run \"task 2\" --session-id abc-123 # Reuse existing session\n\n# Execution modes\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --flash       # Fast execution mode\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --wait        # Wait for completion (default: async)\n\n# Advanced options\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --thinking    # Extended reasoning mode\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --no-vision   # Disable vision (enabled by default)\n\n# Using a cloud profile (create session first, then run with --session-id)\nbrowser-use session create --profile <cloud-profile-id> --keep-alive\n# → returns session_id\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --session-id <session-id>\n\n# Task configuration\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --start-url https://example.com  # Start from specific URL\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --allowed-domain example.com     # Restrict navigation (repeatable)\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --metadata key=value             # Task metadata (repeatable)\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --skill-id skill-123             # Enable skills (repeatable)\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --secret key=value               # Secret metadata (repeatable)\n\n# Structured output and evaluation\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --structured-output ''{\"type\":\"object\"}''  # JSON schema for output\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --judge                          # Enable judge mode\nbrowser-use run \"task\" --judge-ground-truth \"answer\"\n```\n\n### Task Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use task list                     # List recent tasks\nbrowser-use task list --limit 20          # Show more tasks\nbrowser-use task list --status finished   # Filter by status (finished, stopped)\nbrowser-use task list --session <id>      # Filter by session ID\nbrowser-use task list --json              # JSON output\n\nbrowser-use task status <task-id>         # Get task status (latest step only)\nbrowser-use task status <task-id> -c      # All steps with reasoning\nbrowser-use task status <task-id> -v      # All steps with URLs + actions\nbrowser-use task status <task-id> --last 5  # Last N steps only\nbrowser-use task status <task-id> --step 3  # Specific step number\nbrowser-use task status <task-id> --reverse # Newest first\n\nbrowser-use task stop <task-id>           # Stop a running task\nbrowser-use task logs <task-id>           # Get task execution logs\n```\n\n### Cloud Session Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use session list                  # List cloud sessions\nbrowser-use session list --limit 20       # Show more sessions\nbrowser-use session list --status active  # Filter by status\nbrowser-use session list --json           # JSON output\n\nbrowser-use session get <session-id>      # Get session details + live URL\nbrowser-use session get <session-id> --json\n\nbrowser-use session stop <session-id>     # Stop a session\nbrowser-use session stop --all            # Stop all active sessions\n\nbrowser-use session create                          # Create with defaults\nbrowser-use session create --profile <id>           # With cloud profile\nbrowser-use session create --proxy-country uk       # With geographic proxy\nbrowser-use session create --start-url https://example.com\nbrowser-use session create --screen-size 1920x1080\nbrowser-use session create --keep-alive\nbrowser-use session create --persist-memory\n\nbrowser-use session share <session-id>              # Create public share URL\nbrowser-use session share <session-id> --delete     # Delete public share\n```\n\n### Cloud Profile Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use profile list                  # List cloud profiles\nbrowser-use profile list --page 2 --page-size 50\nbrowser-use profile get <id>              # Get profile details\nbrowser-use profile create                # Create new profile\nbrowser-use profile create --name \"My Profile\"\nbrowser-use profile update <id> --name \"New Name\"\nbrowser-use profile delete <id>\n```\n\n### Tunnels\n```bash\nbrowser-use tunnel <port>           # Start tunnel (returns URL)\nbrowser-use tunnel <port>           # Idempotent - returns existing URL\nbrowser-use tunnel list             # Show active tunnels\nbrowser-use tunnel stop <port>      # Stop tunnel\nbrowser-use tunnel stop --all       # Stop all tunnels\n```\n\n### Session Management\n```bash\nbrowser-use sessions                # List active sessions\nbrowser-use close                   # Close current session\nbrowser-use close --all             # Close all sessions\n```\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Exposing Local Dev Servers\n\nUse when you have a dev server on the remote machine and need the cloud browser to reach it.\n\n**Core workflow:** Start dev server → create tunnel → browse the tunnel URL.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Start your dev server\npython -m http.server 3000 &\n\n# 2. Expose it via Cloudflare tunnel\nbrowser-use tunnel 3000\n# → url: https://abc.trycloudflare.com\n\n# 3. Now the cloud browser can reach your local server\nbrowser-use open https://abc.trycloudflare.com\nbrowser-use state\nbrowser-use screenshot\n```\n\n**Note:** Tunnels are independent of browser sessions. They persist across `browser-use close` and can be managed separately. Cloudflared must be installed — run `browser-use doctor` to check.\n\n### Running Subagents\n\nUse cloud sessions to run autonomous browser agents in parallel.\n\n**Core workflow:** Launch task(s) with `run` → poll with `task status` → collect results → clean up sessions.\n\n- **Session = Agent**: Each cloud session is a browser agent with its own state\n- **Task = Work**: Jobs given to an agent; an agent can run multiple tasks sequentially\n- **Session lifecycle**: Once stopped, a session cannot be revived — start a new one\n\n#### Launching Tasks\n\n```bash\n# Single task (async by default — returns immediately)\nbrowser-use run \"Search for AI news and summarize top 3 articles\"\n# → task_id: task-abc, session_id: sess-123\n\n# Parallel tasks — each gets its own session\nbrowser-use run \"Research competitor A pricing\"\n# → task_id: task-1, session_id: sess-a\nbrowser-use run \"Research competitor B pricing\"\n# → task_id: task-2, session_id: sess-b\nbrowser-use run \"Research competitor C pricing\"\n# → task_id: task-3, session_id: sess-c\n\n# Sequential tasks in same session (reuses cookies, login state, etc.)\nbrowser-use run \"Log into example.com\" --keep-alive\n# → task_id: task-1, session_id: sess-123\nbrowser-use task status task-1  # Wait for completion\nbrowser-use run \"Export settings\" --session-id sess-123\n# → task_id: task-2, session_id: sess-123 (same session)\n```\n\n#### Managing & Stopping\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use task list --status finished      # See completed tasks\nbrowser-use task stop task-abc               # Stop a task (session may continue if --keep-alive)\nbrowser-use session stop sess-123            # Stop an entire session (terminates its tasks)\nbrowser-use session stop --all               # Stop all sessions\n```\n\n#### Monitoring\n\n**Task status is designed for token efficiency.** Default output is minimal — only expand when needed:\n\n| Mode | Flag | Tokens | Use When |\n|------|------|--------|----------|\n| Default | (none) | Low | Polling progress |\n| Compact | `-c` | Medium | Need full reasoning |\n| Verbose | `-v` | High | Debugging actions |\n\n```bash\n# For long tasks (50+ steps)\nbrowser-use task status <id> -c --last 5   # Last 5 steps only\nbrowser-use task status <id> -v --step 10  # Inspect specific step\n```\n\n**Live view**: `browser-use session get <session-id>` returns a live URL to watch the agent.\n\n**Detect stuck tasks**: If cost/duration in `task status` stops increasing, the task is stuck — stop it and start a new agent.\n\n**Logs**: `browser-use task logs <task-id>` — only available after task completes.\n\n## Global Options\n\n| Option | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `--session NAME` | Named session (default: \"default\") |\n| `--browser MODE` | Browser mode (only if multiple modes installed) |\n| `--profile ID` | Cloud profile ID for persistent cookies. Works with `open`, `session create`, etc. — does NOT work with `run` (use `--session-id` instead) |\n| `--json` | Output as JSON |\n\n## Tips\n\n1. **Run `browser-use doctor`** to verify installation before starting\n2. **Always run `state` first** to see available elements and their indices\n3. **Sessions persist** across commands — the browser stays open until you close it\n4. **Tunnels are independent** — they persist across `browser-use close`\n5. **Use `--json`** for programmatic parsing\n6. **`tunnel` is idempotent** — calling it again for the same port returns the existing URL\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**\"Browser mode ''chromium'' not installed\"?**\n- Expected for sandboxed agents — remote mode only supports cloud browsers\n- Run `browser-use doctor` to verify configuration\n\n**Cloud browser won''t start?**\n- Run `browser-use doctor` to check configuration\n\n**Tunnel not working?**\n- Verify cloudflared is installed: `which cloudflared`\n- `browser-use tunnel list` to check active tunnels\n- `browser-use tunnel stop <port>` and retry\n\n**Element not found?**\n- Run `browser-use state` to see current elements\n- `browser-use scroll down` then `browser-use state` — element might be below fold\n\n**Session reuse fails after `task stop`**:\nCreate a new session instead:\n```bash\nbrowser-use session create --profile <profile-id> --keep-alive\nbrowser-use run \"new task\" --session-id <new-session-id>\n```\n\n**Task stuck at \"started\"**: Check cost with `task status` — if not increasing, the task is stuck. View live URL with `session get`, then stop and start a new agent.\n\n**Sessions persist after tasks complete**: Run `browser-use session stop --all` to clean up.\n\n## Cleanup\n\n**Always close resources when done:**\n\n```bash\nbrowser-use close                     # Close browser session\nbrowser-use session stop --all        # Stop cloud sessions (if any)\nbrowser-use tunnel stop --all         # Stop tunnels (if any)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:09:02.778Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud-based Agents requiring automated browser interactions for web scraping, testing, or automation tasks","zh":"适合于需要自动浏览器交互的基于云的代理，用于网页抓取、测试或自动化任务","ja":"クラウドベースのエージェントが自動ブラウザ操作を必要とするウェブスクレイピング、テスト、または自動化タスクに最適","ko":"자동 브라우저 상호 작용이 필요한 클라우드 기반 에이전트에 적합하여 웹 스크레이핑, 테스트 또는 자동화 작업을 수행할 수 있습니다","es":"Ideal para agentes basados en la nube que requieren interacciones de navegador automatizadas para tareas de scraping web, pruebas o automatización","fr":"Idéal pour les agents basés sur le cloud nécessitant des interactions de navigateur automatisées pour le scraping web, les tests ou les tâches d''automatisation","de":"Ideal für cloudbasierte Agenten, die automatisierte Browser-Interaktionen für Web-Scraping-, Test- oder Automatisierungsaufgaben benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes baseados em Nuvem que exigem interações de navegador automatizadas para extração de dados da web, testes ou tarefas de automação","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, требующих автоматизированных взаимодействий браузера для веб-скрейпинга, тестирования или задач автоматизации","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء القائمين على السحابة الذين يتطلبون تفاعلات متصفح آلية لاستخراج بيانات الويب أو الاختبار أو مهام التutomatisation"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to control a cloud browser, automating tasks online with ease, using the `browser-use` library, and driving a cloud browser without needing local Chrome installation, supporting protocols like HTTP and HTTPS","zh":"赋予代理控制云浏览器的能力，使用 `browser-use` 库自动执行在线任务，无需本地 Chrome 安装，支持 HTTP 和 HTTPS 等协议","ja":"`browser-use` ライブラリを使用して、エージェントがクラウドブラウザを制御し、ローカル Chrome のインストール不要で、HTTP および HTTPS などのプロトコルをサポートして、オンラインでのタスクを自動化する","ko":"에이전트가 클라우드 브라우저를 제어할 수 있도록 하여 `browser-use` 라이브러리를 사용하고 로컬 Chrome 설치가 필요하지 않으며 HTTP 및 HTTPS와 같은 프로토콜을 지원하여 온라인 작업을 자동화합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a controlar un navegador en la nube, automatizando tareas en línea con facilidad, utilizando la biblioteca `browser-use` y conduciendo un navegador en la nube sin necesidad de instalación local de Chrome, soportando protocolos como HTTP y HTTPS","fr":"Permet aux agents de contrôler un navigateur cloud, automatisant les tâches en ligne avec facilité, en utilisant la bibliothèque `browser-use` et en conduisant un navigateur cloud sans nécessiter d''installation locale de Chrome, en prenant en charge des protocoles comme HTTP et HTTPS","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, einen Cloud-Browser zu steuern, Aufgaben online mit Leichtigkeit zu automatisieren, indem sie die `browser-use`-Bibliothek verwenden und einen Cloud-Browser ohne lokale Chrome-Installation steuern, wobei Protokolle wie HTTP und HTTPS unterstützt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a controlar um navegador de nuvem, automatizando tarefas online com facilidade, usando a biblioteca `browser-use` e dirigindo um navegador de nuvem sem precisar da instalação local do Chrome, suportando protocolos como HTTP e HTTPS","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью контролировать облачный браузер, автоматизируя задачи в Интернете с легкостью, используя библиотеку `browser-use` и управляя облачным браузером без необходимости локальной установки Chrome, поддерживая протоколы như HTTP и HTTPS","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحكم في متصفح سحابي، وتأتمة المهام عبر الإنترنت بسهولة، باستخدام مكتبة `browser-use` وتوجيه متصفح سحابي دون الحاجة إلى تثبيت كروم المحلي، ودعم بروتوكولات مثل HTTP وHTTPS"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating web scraping tasks","Debugging web applications","Generating reports from web data"],"zh":["自动执行网页抓取任务","调试网页应用程序","从网页数据生成报告"],"ja":["ウェブスクレイピングタスクの自動化","ウェブアプリケーションのデバッグ","ウェブデータからのレポート生成"],"ko":["웹 스크레이핑 작업 자동화","웹 애플리케이션 디버깅","웹 데이터에서 보고서 생성"],"es":["Automatizar tareas de scraping web","Depurar aplicaciones web","Generar informes a partir de datos web"],"fr":["Automatiser les tâches de scraping web","Déboguer les applications web","Générer des rapports à partir de données web"],"de":["Automatisieren von Web-Scraping-Aufgaben","Debuggen von Web-Anwendungen","Erstellen von Berichten aus Web-Daten"],"pt":["Automatizar tarefas de extração de dados da web","Depurar aplicações web","Gerar relatórios a partir de dados da web"],"ru":["Автоматизировать задачи веб-скрейпинга","Отлаживать веб-приложения","Генерировать отчеты из веб-данных"],"ar":["تأتمة مهام استخراج بيانات الويب","تصحيح أخطاء تطبيقات الويب","генерировать تقارير من بيانات الويب"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires `browser-use` installation and configuration","Needs sandboxed remote machine environment","Must run diagnostics with `browser-use doctor`"],"zh":["需要 `browser-use` 安装和配置","需要沙盒化的远程机器环境","必须使用 `browser-use doctor` 运行诊断"],"ja":["`browser-use` のインストールと設定が必要","サンドボックス化されたリモートマシン環境が必要","`browser-use doctor` で診断を実行する必要がある"],"ko":["`browser-use` 설치 및 구성이 필요합니다","샌드박스화된 원격 머신 환경이 필요합니다","`browser-use doctor`로 진단을 실행해야 합니다"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de `browser-use`","Necesita un entorno de máquina remota aislado","Deben ejecutarse diagnósticos con `browser-use doctor`"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de `browser-use`","A besoin d''un environnement de machine distante sandboxé","Doit exécuter des diagnostics avec `browser-use doctor`"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation und Konfiguration von `browser-use`","Benötigt eine isolierte Remote-Maschine-Umgebung","Müssen Diagnosen mit `browser-use doctor` durchgeführt werden"],"pt":["Exige instalação e configuração do `browser-use`","Necessita de ambiente de máquina remota sandboxed","Deve executar diagnósticos com `browser-use doctor`"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации `browser-use`","Требует sandbox-окружения удаленной машины","Должен запускать диагностику с `browser-use doctor`"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين `browser-use`","يحتاج إلى بيئة جهاز بعيد محمية","يجب تشغيل التشخيص مع `browser-use doctor`"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"fc60ca63b33235fd077b7713d63d17b70a52ec4e00189d3c0bf64976907933eb","qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('aircrushin/promptMinder/agent-sdk', 'community', 'aircrushin', 'promptMinder', 'aircrushin/promptMinder', 'agent-sdk', 0, 0, 40, '2026-03-02T01:56:10.895Z', '2026-03-02T02:10:40.924Z', '02bf3f4d2c889d304dd24cad107842f193ac6d6c4656bbba29db1857ec5930c4', '{"id":"aircrushin/promptMinder/agent-sdk","name":"agent-sdk","description":{"zh":"Agent SDK是一个开源的AI智能代理平台，专注于提示词管理，提供高效的开发解决方案","ja":"Agent SDKはオープンソースのAIエージェントプラットフォームで、プロンプト管理に特化しています","ko":"Agent SDK는 오픈소스의 AI 에이전트 플랫폼으로 프롬프트 관리에 중점을 두어 개발자의 효율성을 높입니다","es":"agent-sdk es una plataforma de código abierto que se centra en la gestión de prompts para desarrolladores de IA","fr":"agent-sdk est une plateforme open source qui se concentre sur la gestion de prompts pour les développeurs d''IA","de":"agent-sdk ist eine Open-Source-Plattform, die sich auf das Prompt-Management für KI-Entwickler konzentriert","pt":"O Agent-SDK é uma plataforma de código aberto que se concentra na gestão de prompt para desenvolvedores de AI, permitindo a criação de soluções personalizadas","ru":"Agent-SDK - это открытая платформа, ориентированная на управление промптами для разработчиков ИИ, позволяющая создавать индивидуальные решения","ar":"Agent-SDK هي منصة مفتوحة المصدر تركز على إدارة التوجيهات لمطوري الذكاء الاصطناعي، مما يسمح بإنشاء حلول مخصصة","en":"一个开源的，专注于提示词管理的平台 / An open-source platform focused on prompt management"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 - Agent SDK提示词管理平台","ja":"AIエージェント - Agent SDKプロンプト管理プラットフォーム","ko":"AI 에이전트 - Agent SDK 프롬프트 관리 플랫폼","es":"Herramientas de AI: agent-sdk para gestión de prompts","fr":"Outils d''IA: agent-sdk pour la gestion de prompts","de":"KI-Tools: agent-sdk für Prompt-Management","pt":"Ferramentas de AI: Agent-SDK para Gestão de Prompt","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Agent-SDK для управления промптами","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: Agent-SDK لإدارة التو